1
00:00:52,229 --> 00:00:53,229
I don't know...

2
00:00:53,687 --> 00:00:55,187
what you are about to do

3
00:00:55,937 --> 00:00:56,937
right now.

4
00:00:57,521 --> 00:00:58,521
But I feel

5
00:00:58,896 --> 00:01:00,187
it's going to be...

6
00:01:00,437 --> 00:01:03,812
a major turning point
in your life.

7
00:01:05,146 --> 00:01:06,187
Similarly,

8
00:01:06,521 --> 00:01:09,771
before making every such
important decision in life,

9
00:01:10,729 --> 00:01:12,062
do you ever take five minutes

10
00:01:12,521 --> 00:01:15,562
just to be relaxed?

11
00:01:16,187 --> 00:01:17,646
To do that,
first you have to...

12
00:01:18,062 --> 00:01:20,771
relax your body,

13
00:01:21,479 --> 00:01:24,979
and keep your mind calm.

14
00:01:25,479 --> 00:01:27,896
To relax your body,

15
00:01:28,687 --> 00:01:32,812
a highly effective practice...

16
00:01:33,396 --> 00:01:34,771
is the countdown technique.

17
00:01:35,396 --> 00:01:36,396
First,

18
00:01:36,896 --> 00:01:38,896
take a deep breath

19
00:01:39,437 --> 00:01:40,854
through your nose.

20
00:01:41,312 --> 00:01:42,479
Inhale.

21
00:01:43,729 --> 00:01:49,146
Hold it right there
for two seconds.

22
00:01:50,146 --> 00:01:51,729
And then, slowly,

23
00:01:53,062 --> 00:01:54,228
[dashboard clicks open]

24
00:01:54,229 --> 00:01:55,811
through your lips

25
00:01:55,812 --> 00:01:56,853
[car horn blares]

26
00:01:56,854 --> 00:01:58,020
gently release that breath

27
00:01:58,021 --> 00:01:59,728
[distant city traffic]

28
00:01:59,729 --> 00:02:00,978
Slowly

29
00:02:00,979 --> 00:02:02,479
just like this

30
00:02:02,937 --> 00:02:04,562
start counting down

31
00:02:05,812 --> 00:02:06,812
99...

32
00:02:07,854 --> 00:02:09,061
98...

33
00:02:09,062 --> 00:02:10,145
[car door closes]

34
00:02:10,146 --> 00:02:11,604
97...

35
00:02:12,771 --> 00:02:14,187
96...

36
00:02:14,937 --> 00:02:16,228
95...

37
00:02:16,229 --> 00:02:17,395
[muffled traffic sounds]

38
00:02:17,396 --> 00:02:19,229
Each time you count down...

39
00:02:30,437 --> 00:02:32,437
[muffled traffic sounds]

40
00:02:43,646 --> 00:02:45,396
[brakes squeal softly
as van approaches]

41
00:02:45,896 --> 00:02:47,187
[van door opens]

42
00:03:01,979 --> 00:03:03,979
[intriguing music]

43
00:03:13,979 --> 00:03:15,646
[music builds]

44
00:03:40,729 --> 00:03:42,104
[pulsating music]

45
00:03:43,562 --> 00:03:45,937
[engines roaring,
tires screeching]

46
00:03:55,437 --> 00:03:57,104
[chaotic street noise]

47
00:03:57,937 --> 00:03:59,729
[engine whining in pursuit]

48
00:04:02,562 --> 00:04:04,270
[score rising dramatically]

49
00:04:04,271 --> 00:04:05,437
[rapid gear shifts]

50
00:04:06,521 --> 00:04:08,021
[loud crash]

51
00:04:15,646 --> 00:04:17,396
[English song plays]

52
00:04:24,979 --> 00:04:26,687
[tires grind to a halt]

53
00:04:46,396 --> 00:04:48,146
[score rises dramatically]

54
00:05:18,979 --> 00:05:20,020
[music fades]

55
00:05:20,021 --> 00:05:21,104
[gunshot blasts, tire pops]

56
00:05:23,271 --> 00:05:26,646
[traffic humming]

57
00:05:29,354 --> 00:05:30,729
Taluk Hospital, right?

58
00:05:30,854 --> 00:05:32,104
Yeah, got it.

59
00:05:32,437 --> 00:05:33,979
No trouble being
caused there, right?

60
00:05:34,687 --> 00:05:36,521
Okay, I'll send someone over.

61
00:05:39,271 --> 00:05:41,728
Why did you guys take on
a job you can't handle?

62
00:05:41,729 --> 00:05:43,396
Just to embarrass me too?!

63
00:05:43,562 --> 00:05:45,187
Didn't I assign you
a task this morning?

64
00:05:45,479 --> 00:05:47,479
Then why did you drag
yourselves over here?

65
00:05:47,771 --> 00:05:49,396
That's exactly what
brought us here, sir.

66
00:05:49,646 --> 00:05:51,187
Oh? Was it here?

67
00:05:51,312 --> 00:05:52,811
No, sir. Down at that corner.

68
00:05:52,812 --> 00:05:55,729
Sir, while checking the C... CCTV
over there, we heard a noise.

69
00:05:57,479 --> 00:05:58,603
When we got here,

70
00:05:58,604 --> 00:06:01,686
we saw three masked guys with guns
making a run for it.

71
00:06:01,687 --> 00:06:04,811
We chased them down and were
just about to catch them...

72
00:06:04,812 --> 00:06:07,145
when they shot
and blew out our jeep's tire!

73
00:06:07,146 --> 00:06:09,354
Don't bother saying the rest.
The whole town saw it!

74
00:06:11,229 --> 00:06:12,896
[music building slowly]

75
00:06:15,396 --> 00:06:17,104
The chief is looking for you both.

76
00:06:17,312 --> 00:06:19,979
Go wait over there,
face the music, and clear out.

77
00:06:22,146 --> 00:06:23,271
Actually...

78
00:06:23,479 --> 00:06:24,603
don't just waste your time here.

79
00:06:24,604 --> 00:06:26,811
Someone's been admitted
to the Taluk hospital.

80
00:06:26,812 --> 00:06:28,436
Seems like some local brawl.

81
00:06:28,437 --> 00:06:30,104
Find out what happened
and call me.

82
00:06:30,854 --> 00:06:31,895
Sir!

83
00:06:31,896 --> 00:06:33,104
Who did those guys take, sir?

84
00:06:33,812 --> 00:06:34,812
Was it some V.I.P.?

85
00:06:38,479 --> 00:06:39,896
Nope. Just a regular Joe.

86
00:06:40,271 --> 00:06:41,312
A nobody!

87
00:06:41,604 --> 00:06:43,521
[music rising]

88
00:06:47,646 --> 00:06:49,229
[van engine rumbles]

89
00:07:04,896 --> 00:07:06,146
[loud explosion]

90
00:07:13,479 --> 00:07:15,146
[tires screech]

91
00:07:16,812 --> 00:07:18,562
Bro! Just drive faster.

92
00:07:18,729 --> 00:07:20,229
It's time for me to
get back to work.

93
00:07:20,771 --> 00:07:22,687
Don't we have to dump
this guy somewhere?

94
00:07:23,271 --> 00:07:25,061
Hey, hey, stop there!

95
00:07:25,062 --> 00:07:26,312
Pull over at that spot.

96
00:07:27,229 --> 00:07:29,561
Hey... there are people and cars
around. Don't cause a scene!

97
00:07:29,562 --> 00:07:31,312
It won't be a scene, man.
Just stop the car!

98
00:07:32,729 --> 00:07:33,937
[car screeches to a halt]

99
00:07:35,437 --> 00:07:37,978
Tell that loser partner of yours
that we're coming to see him soon.

100
00:07:37,979 --> 00:07:39,562
- Get out, you piece of trash!
- Get down!

101
00:07:42,354 --> 00:07:43,479
Just leave him there!

102
00:07:43,812 --> 00:07:45,186
Hey, that's far enough!
Come back!

103
00:07:45,187 --> 00:07:46,187
Come on!

104
00:07:47,854 --> 00:07:49,854
Go get yourself
run over and die!

105
00:07:50,229 --> 00:07:51,521
[groans in pain]

106
00:07:56,854 --> 00:07:58,396
[screams in agony]

107
00:07:59,354 --> 00:08:00,521
Come back!

108
00:08:02,646 --> 00:08:03,646
Hey!

109
00:08:04,021 --> 00:08:05,062
Dude, that's enough!
Get over here!

110
00:08:05,187 --> 00:08:07,021
People are going to see us.
Get back in the car!

111
00:08:08,729 --> 00:08:10,354
This idiot is going
to ruin everything.

112
00:08:12,729 --> 00:08:14,270
- Hey!
- Get out there and handle him!

113
00:08:14,271 --> 00:08:15,271
Hey! Stop it!

114
00:08:16,021 --> 00:08:17,312
Hey! Stop it!

115
00:08:17,729 --> 00:08:18,770
Hey! Get back!

116
00:08:18,771 --> 00:08:20,146
You're right in the
middle of the road!

117
00:08:20,396 --> 00:08:21,895
Shouldn't we go?
Come back!

118
00:08:21,896 --> 00:08:23,061
Just leave him and get in!

119
00:08:23,062 --> 00:08:24,062
Peter! Hey!

120
00:08:25,437 --> 00:08:26,479
Start the car!

121
00:08:27,771 --> 00:08:30,062
[horns honking]

122
00:08:34,354 --> 00:08:35,811
Have you come
just to pick a fight?

123
00:08:35,812 --> 00:08:37,520
Don't you need to be at work
before this hits the news?

124
00:08:37,521 --> 00:08:39,061
How can I show up at work
looking like this?

125
00:08:39,062 --> 00:08:41,061
Just find a way!
Hey, get the car moving fast!

126
00:08:41,062 --> 00:08:42,270
We're already late.

127
00:08:42,271 --> 00:08:43,645
Is it my fault that we're late?

128
00:08:43,646 --> 00:08:45,728
- Was I supposed to spare him?
- You're the one who had to show off!

129
00:08:45,729 --> 00:08:46,854
Piss off!

130
00:08:46,979 --> 00:08:48,895
Wait... didn't your t-shirt have

131
00:08:48,896 --> 00:08:50,896
a nameplate on it?
The one with your name?

132
00:08:51,271 --> 00:08:52,312
Where is it?

133
00:08:54,396 --> 00:08:55,562
That scumbag!

134
00:08:58,646 --> 00:08:59,771
Turn the car around, man!

135
00:09:04,312 --> 00:09:05,811
Dude, turn the car around!

136
00:09:05,812 --> 00:09:08,729
[tires screech as car turns]

137
00:09:09,479 --> 00:09:11,021
[tires screech]

138
00:09:11,604 --> 00:09:13,271
[fast-paced music rising]

139
00:09:19,312 --> 00:09:21,021
[engine revving loudly]

140
00:09:22,312 --> 00:09:24,146
[chaotic pursuit sounds]

141
00:09:33,062 --> 00:09:34,437
Run that pig down!

142
00:09:38,021 --> 00:09:39,021
Finish him!

143
00:09:39,146 --> 00:09:40,146
[music stops abruptly]

144
00:09:40,562 --> 00:09:41,687
[engine roars]

145
00:09:42,229 --> 00:09:43,562
[loud truck horn]

146
00:09:48,187 --> 00:09:50,104
[heavy engine roaring]

147
00:09:55,479 --> 00:09:56,896
[tires screeching as car skids]

148
00:10:06,771 --> 00:10:08,479
[car crashes violently]

149
00:10:10,854 --> 00:10:12,604
[high-energy music swells]

150
00:10:14,354 --> 00:10:16,562
I, NOBODY

151
00:10:26,354 --> 00:10:28,021
[ambient hospital sounds]

152
00:10:28,979 --> 00:10:30,604
No one gave any names
or information.

153
00:10:30,729 --> 00:10:33,520
A few people dropped him off,
claiming they found him out on the road.

154
00:10:33,521 --> 00:10:35,228
He has been beaten up
pretty badly.

155
00:10:35,229 --> 00:10:37,062
His hands were tied
behind his back like this.

156
00:10:40,062 --> 00:10:42,021
[low hum of music]

157
00:10:42,146 --> 00:10:44,187
[distant ambulance sirens]

158
00:10:45,271 --> 00:10:47,021
[music becomes intriguing]

159
00:10:59,396 --> 00:11:01,229
[dramatic score intensifies]

160
00:11:17,271 --> 00:11:19,020
Sir, this isn't some
brawl or assault case.

161
00:11:19,021 --> 00:11:21,021
It's him.
The "nobody" you spoke of, sir.

162
00:11:21,187 --> 00:11:22,228
And sir...

163
00:11:22,229 --> 00:11:25,478
He handed over a restaurant badge,
saying it belongs to one of the thieves.

164
00:11:25,479 --> 00:11:27,229
The kind people wear
on their uniforms?

165
00:11:27,437 --> 00:11:29,396
Right. That sort of thing.

166
00:11:29,771 --> 00:11:31,146
It has one of their names on it.

167
00:11:31,354 --> 00:11:32,603
Peter Thomas.

168
00:11:32,604 --> 00:11:33,728
[ambulance door opens]

169
00:11:33,729 --> 00:11:35,145
[stretcher clicks and slides out]

170
00:11:35,146 --> 00:11:36,937
[ambulance sirens wailing]

171
00:11:45,312 --> 00:11:46,770
- What happened?
- Road accident.

172
00:11:46,771 --> 00:11:47,979
- An accident?
- Yes.

173
00:12:20,646 --> 00:12:22,354
Rajeevan, do you have
any trouble speaking?

174
00:12:22,646 --> 00:12:23,895
Do you need to rest
a bit longer?

175
00:12:23,896 --> 00:12:25,479
No... I'm fine.

176
00:12:26,979 --> 00:12:27,979
Alright.

177
00:12:28,854 --> 00:12:30,729
Then, how about we take it
from the top?

178
00:12:32,687 --> 00:12:33,436
Okay.

179
00:12:33,437 --> 00:12:35,729
You go into the bank for some work.

180
00:12:36,146 --> 00:12:38,604
Just then,
the three of them storm the bank.

181
00:12:38,812 --> 00:12:39,937
And then?

182
00:12:40,937 --> 00:12:42,104
And then they...

183
00:12:42,479 --> 00:12:45,936
[muffled sounds, faint emotional score]

184
00:12:45,937 --> 00:12:47,437
Sir, this is Rajeevan's wife.

185
00:12:51,312 --> 00:12:52,396
He is alright, Madam.

186
00:12:52,521 --> 00:12:53,729
Nothing to worry.

187
00:12:58,979 --> 00:13:00,146
What did the doctor say?

188
00:13:01,021 --> 00:13:02,229
I'm alright.

189
00:13:02,437 --> 00:13:04,021
Do we need to get any medicines?

190
00:13:05,104 --> 00:13:06,146
No.

191
00:13:06,562 --> 00:13:07,854
- Can I get you some food?
- No.

192
00:13:09,062 --> 00:13:10,354
I don't want anything right now.

193
00:13:14,062 --> 00:13:15,771
Are you discharged?
I can drop you home.

194
00:13:15,979 --> 00:13:17,062
I've been discharged.
But...

195
00:13:17,396 --> 00:13:18,396
They...

196
00:13:19,229 --> 00:13:20,896
We just need
a few more details, Ma'am.

197
00:13:21,229 --> 00:13:22,312
We'll be quick.

198
00:13:24,062 --> 00:13:25,646
Let me know when this is done.

199
00:13:27,229 --> 00:13:28,229
Okay.

200
00:13:39,937 --> 00:13:42,062
Rajeevan, if you're not comfortable
talking here...

201
00:13:42,229 --> 00:13:43,479
how about we go to the station?

202
00:13:45,687 --> 00:13:47,186
- Are you ready?
- Yes, sir.

203
00:13:47,187 --> 00:13:49,020
- Don't push for too many details.
- Got it.

204
00:13:49,021 --> 00:13:50,437
I'll tell you what
you need to know.

205
00:13:51,771 --> 00:13:54,062
Three people were directly
involved in the accident.

206
00:13:54,646 --> 00:13:56,396
Fleeing the bank after the heist,

207
00:13:56,729 --> 00:13:58,978
they met with an accident
and died on the spot.

208
00:13:58,979 --> 00:14:00,145
You already know this part.

209
00:14:00,146 --> 00:14:01,687
And we've identified
one of them.

210
00:14:02,937 --> 00:14:05,270
It's too early to say if there
are more players involved.

211
00:14:05,271 --> 00:14:07,270
The investigation is underway.
We will update you.

212
00:14:07,271 --> 00:14:10,020
The money stolen from the bank
has not been recovered yet.

213
00:14:10,021 --> 00:14:11,729
We're continuing
our efforts to find it.

214
00:14:11,896 --> 00:14:14,104
That is all I have
to say at the moment.

215
00:14:14,562 --> 00:14:16,353
If you have any questions,
I'll take them now.

216
00:14:16,354 --> 00:14:18,146
Any foul play suspected
in that accident?

217
00:14:18,979 --> 00:14:20,395
No signs of foul play so far.

218
00:14:20,396 --> 00:14:22,062
We have the truck driver in custody.

219
00:14:22,396 --> 00:14:23,270
We did question him.

220
00:14:23,271 --> 00:14:25,395
Sir, you mentioned
you've identified one of them.

221
00:14:25,396 --> 00:14:27,145
Any specifics you can give us?

222
00:14:27,146 --> 00:14:28,687
I can't disclose that
at this stage.

223
00:14:29,062 --> 00:14:30,979
I'll brief you when
the time is right. We good?

224
00:14:31,854 --> 00:14:32,936
Anas.

225
00:14:32,937 --> 00:14:34,687
- It's almost over. Come on over.
- For what?

226
00:14:36,146 --> 00:14:37,936
Every time a crime
hits this place...

227
00:14:37,937 --> 00:14:40,604
they aren't satisfied until
a couple of cops are suspended.

228
00:14:42,146 --> 00:14:44,437
I'm done b... begging people.

229
00:14:44,646 --> 00:14:45,729
I'm out of here.

230
00:14:46,479 --> 00:14:47,479
Anas!

231
00:14:47,771 --> 00:14:48,812
[car horn blares]

232
00:14:53,479 --> 00:14:55,229
- Have you got nothing to ask me?
- No.

233
00:14:56,271 --> 00:14:57,437
What should I ask?

234
00:15:00,437 --> 00:15:01,646
Fine, I'll tell you myself.

235
00:15:02,771 --> 00:15:04,104
I didn't go to the office today.

236
00:15:04,646 --> 00:15:07,020
I just wasn't in the mood.
I go there every day, right?

237
00:15:07,021 --> 00:15:10,146
So instead, I picked a bank
that looked ripe for a robbery today...

238
00:15:10,771 --> 00:15:11,937
and went and sat inside.

239
00:15:12,271 --> 00:15:13,729
And when that didn't
do it for me,

240
00:15:13,979 --> 00:15:15,854
I went out of my way
to piss off the robbers,

241
00:15:16,104 --> 00:15:17,521
got the crap beaten out of me,

242
00:15:18,021 --> 00:15:20,687
and created a situation where
they were forced to take me hostage.

243
00:15:22,146 --> 00:15:23,187
Satisfied?

244
00:15:29,271 --> 00:15:31,021
Oh, wait, sorry...
I forgot something else.

245
00:15:31,771 --> 00:15:34,353
Even though I knew exactly what was
going to happen at the bank today...

246
00:15:34,354 --> 00:15:36,646
it's completely my fault for walking
right into that specific bank, isn't it?

247
00:15:38,562 --> 00:15:39,687
So, sorry.

248
00:15:51,021 --> 00:15:52,687
[mysterious score plays]

249
00:15:56,562 --> 00:15:59,395
[news] Today, at the single busiest bank
branch in a city like Trivandrum...

250
00:15:59,396 --> 00:16:01,853
three men armed with just
two small handguns...

251
00:16:01,854 --> 00:16:04,061
managed to pull off a
massive daylight robbery.

252
00:16:04,062 --> 00:16:05,145
Give your Dad a salute!

253
00:16:05,146 --> 00:16:07,520
What we witnessed in
Vanchiyoor today really exposes...

254
00:16:07,521 --> 00:16:09,811
Actually, don't bother.
He's on suspension now anyway.

255
00:16:09,812 --> 00:16:11,478
...the state of security
at our banks.

256
00:16:11,479 --> 00:16:13,520
Until now, the largest bank
heist in Kerala's history...

257
00:16:13,521 --> 00:16:15,311
Have you called my brother yet?

258
00:16:15,312 --> 00:16:18,020
...was pulled off in Chelambra,
Malappuram, back in December 2007.

259
00:16:18,021 --> 00:16:20,936
Why can't you just call him?
Why do you have to stretch this out?

260
00:16:20,937 --> 00:16:22,770
However, today's robbery is set
to break that record.

261
00:16:22,771 --> 00:16:25,186
Do you even know how long it's
been since I last saw my mom?

262
00:16:25,187 --> 00:16:27,353
Venu, according to the
information we have right now,

263
00:16:27,354 --> 00:16:30,728
around Rs. 17 crores has
been stolen from the bank.

264
00:16:30,729 --> 00:16:33,520
To be precise,
it's Rs. 16 crore and 73 lakhs.

265
00:16:33,521 --> 00:16:35,395
And this is just an initial estimate.

266
00:16:35,396 --> 00:16:39,145
Did they hide the gold and cash
somewhere before the accident,

267
00:16:39,146 --> 00:16:41,020
or pass it on to an accomplice?

268
00:16:41,021 --> 00:16:43,229
That is the main question
confounding the police.

269
00:16:44,812 --> 00:16:46,812
[intriguing score intensifies]

270
00:16:58,146 --> 00:16:59,146
[music stops]

271
00:17:05,271 --> 00:17:07,521
Aren't you done eating yet?
What's taking so long?

272
00:17:08,479 --> 00:17:10,936
Mumma, she isn't eating
any of her vegetables.

273
00:17:10,937 --> 00:17:12,187
She's wasting all of it.

274
00:17:12,312 --> 00:17:15,062
Mumma, I don't want it.
I'm really not hungry.

275
00:17:32,979 --> 00:17:34,271
If you're not going to eat,
go wash your hands.

276
00:17:38,687 --> 00:17:39,937
Just leave it there.

277
00:17:40,229 --> 00:17:41,812
Go do your homework.

278
00:17:49,437 --> 00:17:50,479
Amala!

279
00:18:38,354 --> 00:18:40,603
[indistinct chatter]

280
00:18:40,604 --> 00:18:42,479
- Over there.
- Yes, right there.

281
00:18:42,604 --> 00:18:44,187
[mobile game sounds]

282
00:18:50,062 --> 00:18:51,311
- Mumma.
- Hm?

283
00:18:51,312 --> 00:18:52,561
Have you seen my Mickey?

284
00:18:52,562 --> 00:18:53,771
[mobile game sounds]

285
00:18:55,312 --> 00:18:56,354
Ah...

286
00:18:56,521 --> 00:18:57,603
He's outside.

287
00:18:57,604 --> 00:18:58,979
I'll go grab him real quick.

288
00:18:59,187 --> 00:19:01,187
[mobile game sounds]

289
00:19:06,396 --> 00:19:09,271
Mumma told me you got hurt
because you went looking for a fight.

290
00:19:09,396 --> 00:19:10,479
Is that true, Papa?

291
00:19:11,062 --> 00:19:12,186
Yeah.

292
00:19:12,187 --> 00:19:13,646
Me against a bunch of villains.

293
00:19:14,021 --> 00:19:15,104
And then?

294
00:19:15,937 --> 00:19:16,937
And then what?

295
00:19:17,729 --> 00:19:19,979
Not a single bad guy
who came to fight your Papa...

296
00:19:20,229 --> 00:19:21,521
is left alive now.

297
00:19:22,104 --> 00:19:23,896
Wait, did you kill all of them?

298
00:19:25,604 --> 00:19:28,479
Ugh, not that story again!
I'm sick of hearing it.

299
00:19:28,896 --> 00:19:30,311
Which one do you want instead?

300
00:19:30,312 --> 00:19:32,312
Hmm... tell me the
one about the Papa Rabbit.

301
00:19:32,521 --> 00:19:34,062
But it better not be about a race!

302
00:19:35,021 --> 00:19:36,021
Uh-oh.

303
00:19:36,312 --> 00:19:39,604
Well, well... A Papa Rabbit story
that isn't about a race, huh?

304
00:19:41,771 --> 00:19:43,437
[faint emotional score]

305
00:19:49,646 --> 00:19:51,021
- I've got one.
- Mm.

306
00:19:51,229 --> 00:19:52,479
- Ready for it?
- Yeah!

307
00:19:55,562 --> 00:19:57,396
So, our Papa Rabbit...

308
00:19:58,562 --> 00:20:00,229
- He has a family.
- Uh-huh.

309
00:20:00,854 --> 00:20:03,228
A Mama Rabbit and two little kids.

310
00:20:03,229 --> 00:20:04,396
Okay.

311
00:20:05,396 --> 00:20:07,146
One day, Papa Rabbit finds out...

312
00:20:07,812 --> 00:20:09,062
that Mama Rabbit...

313
00:20:09,854 --> 00:20:10,854
Mm.

314
00:20:11,521 --> 00:20:12,521
That Mama Rabbit...

315
00:20:14,146 --> 00:20:16,187
loves someone else
more than him.

316
00:20:16,604 --> 00:20:17,854
Oh? Who's that?

317
00:20:19,437 --> 00:20:20,521
It's...

318
00:20:22,021 --> 00:20:23,312
an Uncle Tortoise.

319
00:20:25,104 --> 00:20:26,312
Oh no.

320
00:20:27,771 --> 00:20:32,187
Figuring it would only cause more
trouble to ask Mama Rabbit about it,

321
00:20:34,229 --> 00:20:35,354
Papa Rabbit...

322
00:20:35,896 --> 00:20:38,396
decides to go and see
this Uncle Tortoise on his own.

323
00:20:40,312 --> 00:20:44,979
He went to ask Uncle Tortoise
to give Mama Rabbit back to him, you see.

324
00:20:47,937 --> 00:20:50,395
Other than that, the poor thing
meant no harm to anyone.

325
00:20:50,396 --> 00:20:52,646
[steady, heartbeat-like score]

326
00:20:58,354 --> 00:21:02,021
So, just as Papa Rabbit was walking up
to speak to Uncle Tortoise...

327
00:21:03,479 --> 00:21:05,437
suddenly, three jackals...

328
00:21:07,229 --> 00:21:08,646
Good morning everyone!

329
00:21:09,312 --> 00:21:11,061
Now, I'm sure we don't
need to spell out

330
00:21:11,062 --> 00:21:12,936
why we have shown up in
masks with guns, do we?

331
00:21:12,937 --> 00:21:15,228
All we need is five minutes
of your absolute cooperation.

332
00:21:15,229 --> 00:21:19,311
But... if any brave soul here wants to play
hero and hand us over to the cops...

333
00:21:19,312 --> 00:21:21,396
please, feel free
to step forward right now!

334
00:21:22,604 --> 00:21:23,770
Well, well!

335
00:21:23,771 --> 00:21:25,229
Do we have a volunteer?

336
00:21:27,604 --> 00:21:28,770
Huh?

337
00:21:28,771 --> 00:21:29,812
And then?

338
00:21:29,937 --> 00:21:30,937
Give it!

339
00:21:32,396 --> 00:21:33,396
Come on!

340
00:21:34,354 --> 00:21:37,520
Papa Rabbit lay there, wondering what
bad omen he'd crossed that morning...

341
00:21:37,521 --> 00:21:39,020
- And that's when...
- Shh.

342
00:21:39,021 --> 00:21:40,437
- Give it! Give me your phones!

343
00:21:40,729 --> 00:21:41,978
We should do something.

344
00:21:41,979 --> 00:21:42,979
Give it!

345
00:21:44,521 --> 00:21:45,521
Move!

346
00:21:46,187 --> 00:21:47,271
Give me your phone!

347
00:21:48,437 --> 00:21:49,562
Give me your phone!

348
00:21:51,562 --> 00:21:52,854
Where's your phone?

349
00:21:54,271 --> 00:21:55,271
Move!

350
00:21:58,729 --> 00:21:59,937
Hey!

351
00:22:01,729 --> 00:22:02,729
Hey, you!

352
00:22:06,562 --> 00:22:07,603
You!

353
00:22:07,604 --> 00:22:08,729
Making a phone call, huh?

354
00:22:09,812 --> 00:22:11,062
[alarming music]

355
00:22:15,021 --> 00:22:16,687
[unsettling score swells]

356
00:22:33,062 --> 00:22:34,271
Who are you?

357
00:22:34,396 --> 00:22:35,396
Tell me!

358
00:22:35,562 --> 00:22:37,603
Why are you carrying a gun?
Answer me!

359
00:22:37,604 --> 00:22:39,645
Who the hell let you in here?
What's your plan?

360
00:22:39,646 --> 00:22:41,146
- Tell me.
- Brother... Sorry...

361
00:22:41,437 --> 00:22:43,061
I... You've got
the wrong guy.

362
00:22:43,062 --> 00:22:44,811
- I'm here for... for something else.
- Spit the truth out!

363
00:22:44,812 --> 00:22:45,895
Dude, calm down.

364
00:22:45,896 --> 00:22:47,353
- Let's get out of here first.
- Are you kidding me?!

365
00:22:47,354 --> 00:22:48,728
Why would some guy walk
in here today with a gun?

366
00:22:48,729 --> 00:22:50,020
To store it in a locker or what?

367
00:22:50,021 --> 00:22:51,145
Did that other guy send him?

368
00:22:51,146 --> 00:22:52,770
Of course! It's not like
he read our minds!

369
00:22:52,771 --> 00:22:54,811
You morons, you're missing the point!

370
00:22:54,812 --> 00:22:56,145
No, you're the one
missing the point.

371
00:22:56,146 --> 00:22:57,186
There's a crowd
gathering outside.

372
00:22:57,187 --> 00:22:59,811
Didn't I tell you we'd handle
everything the second we clear out?

373
00:22:59,812 --> 00:23:00,603
Hey!

374
00:23:00,604 --> 00:23:02,854
Did you think you could play us for fools
and split the loot between the two of you?

375
00:23:03,187 --> 00:23:05,437
- Dude, this is that guy's plan!
- Hey! Knock it off!

376
00:23:07,146 --> 00:23:08,896
- Get the car!
- Seventy-One...

377
00:23:09,312 --> 00:23:10,521
Seventy...

378
00:23:11,187 --> 00:23:12,479
Sixty-Nine...

379
00:23:13,146 --> 00:23:14,562
Sixty-Eight...

380
00:23:15,104 --> 00:23:16,646
- Start the car! Quick!
- Sixty-Seven...

381
00:23:17,062 --> 00:23:18,062
Sixty-Six...

382
00:23:18,896 --> 00:23:20,521
- Come on, start the car!
- Sixty-Five...

383
00:23:21,062 --> 00:23:22,062
- Let's go!
- Sixty-Four...

384
00:23:22,646 --> 00:23:23,771
Sixty-Three...

385
00:23:24,062 --> 00:23:25,479
Sixty-Two...

386
00:23:26,062 --> 00:23:27,229
Sixty-One...

387
00:23:28,062 --> 00:23:29,187
Sixty...

388
00:24:20,354 --> 00:24:22,437
[upbeat, cheerful music starts]

389
00:24:31,979 --> 00:24:33,312
[Hindi song begins]

390
00:24:33,479 --> 00:24:36,354
♪ Every day is like a balloon ♪

391
00:24:36,646 --> 00:24:40,854
♪ In colours fresh and bright ♪

392
00:24:42,479 --> 00:24:44,103
♪ Like the spark of a firefly ♪

393
00:24:44,104 --> 00:24:45,229
Jiya!

394
00:24:46,521 --> 00:24:47,561
Jiya, get up.

395
00:24:47,562 --> 00:24:49,395
♪ It sways and twinkles in flight ♪

396
00:24:49,396 --> 00:24:50,603
Wake up, dear.

397
00:24:50,604 --> 00:24:52,145
Get up, get up!
Good morning.

398
00:24:52,146 --> 00:24:56,686
♪ Why hold on to yesterday's pain? ♪

399
00:24:56,687 --> 00:25:00,978
♪ Go shake hands with joy again ♪

400
00:25:00,979 --> 00:25:05,478
♪ Push the hands of time ahead ♪

401
00:25:05,479 --> 00:25:09,186
♪ Let the past be gone instead ♪

402
00:25:09,187 --> 00:25:11,229
♪ It's a bunch,
a lovely bunch ♪

403
00:25:11,646 --> 00:25:13,353
♪ A bunch of moments,
rich and rare ♪

404
00:25:13,354 --> 00:25:16,604
♪ This life that you
and I both share ♪

405
00:25:18,604 --> 00:25:19,687
Papa!

406
00:25:20,146 --> 00:25:21,312
Papa!

407
00:25:22,104 --> 00:25:23,312
Ah! Just a minute.

408
00:25:24,729 --> 00:25:26,021
[doorbell rings]

409
00:25:28,062 --> 00:25:29,228
[song stops abruptly]

410
00:25:29,229 --> 00:25:30,437
Is Mr. Rajeevan home?

411
00:25:32,271 --> 00:25:33,854
Sir, you need to come
with us to the SP's office.

412
00:25:36,187 --> 00:25:37,312
But I have to get to work.

413
00:25:38,479 --> 00:25:39,686
I'm already late.

414
00:25:39,687 --> 00:25:41,021
It won't take long, sir.
Just half an hour.

415
00:25:42,854 --> 00:25:45,271
- Sir, that Rajeevan guy has arrived.
- So?

416
00:25:46,646 --> 00:25:48,062
Just let him sit out there.

417
00:25:48,354 --> 00:25:49,354
Okay, sir.

418
00:25:53,812 --> 00:25:55,187
[phone rings]

419
00:25:59,354 --> 00:26:02,062
[rattling chair sound]

420
00:26:02,771 --> 00:26:06,271
[ambient police station sounds]

421
00:26:07,229 --> 00:26:09,104
[phone rings]

422
00:26:14,521 --> 00:26:15,562
[phone rings]

423
00:26:16,729 --> 00:26:17,854
I've been here for a while.

424
00:26:18,229 --> 00:26:19,145
Is Sir not in his office?

425
00:26:19,146 --> 00:26:21,521
Just take a seat over there.
He'll call you when it's time.

426
00:26:22,062 --> 00:26:23,354
[doorbell rings]

427
00:26:24,771 --> 00:26:26,271
Why the hell aren't you
answering our calls?

428
00:26:27,479 --> 00:26:29,062
[rattling chair sound]

429
00:26:31,937 --> 00:26:35,354
[ambient police station sounds]

430
00:26:35,729 --> 00:26:38,021
Sir, it's been two days since
I've gone to my office.

431
00:26:38,896 --> 00:26:39,979
Have a seat.

432
00:26:44,687 --> 00:26:48,604
[ambient police station sounds]

433
00:26:58,062 --> 00:27:01,062
[ambient police station sounds]

434
00:27:12,146 --> 00:27:13,520
[rumble of train passing]

435
00:27:13,521 --> 00:27:14,729
So where's the route map?

436
00:27:15,729 --> 00:27:16,729
Here.

437
00:27:21,062 --> 00:27:25,229
The thieves who broke into the bank
went right past the big church.

438
00:27:25,562 --> 00:27:27,729
From there, they drove
past the airport...

439
00:27:27,937 --> 00:27:31,061
crossed the railway crossing,
and hit Market Junction.

440
00:27:31,062 --> 00:27:34,646
Then, they went around Manakkal temple,
took Palace Road, and hit the highway.

441
00:27:35,229 --> 00:27:36,853
And this is where
the accident happened.

442
00:27:36,854 --> 00:27:38,437
Wait, that's my daily route,
isn't it?

443
00:27:38,562 --> 00:27:40,021
My thoughts exactly.

444
00:27:40,437 --> 00:27:41,728
What else does the paper say?

445
00:27:41,729 --> 00:27:43,562
The money they stole
from the bank...

446
00:27:44,062 --> 00:27:45,811
it wasn't in the van
they burned down...

447
00:27:45,812 --> 00:27:47,228
nor was it in the
car that crashed.

448
00:27:47,229 --> 00:27:48,353
What does that mean?

449
00:27:48,354 --> 00:27:49,437
That means...

450
00:27:49,562 --> 00:27:51,062
before the accident
even happened...

451
00:27:51,229 --> 00:27:53,146
somewhere within this
five-kilometre radius...

452
00:27:53,354 --> 00:27:54,896
they must have hidden the money.

453
00:27:55,437 --> 00:27:56,896
- The entire 17 crores?
- Yep.

454
00:27:58,854 --> 00:27:59,896
[intriguing score begins]

455
00:28:17,146 --> 00:28:21,021
[indistinct chatter]

456
00:28:21,687 --> 00:28:23,646
Let them come.
We'll find it ourselves.

457
00:28:24,771 --> 00:28:25,979
Dude, check that out!

458
00:28:26,146 --> 00:28:27,812
Seems like he's looking
for the money.

459
00:28:31,771 --> 00:28:32,811
Hey, Uncle!

460
00:28:32,812 --> 00:28:34,603
No use looking in there.
It's empty!

461
00:28:34,604 --> 00:28:35,812
We already checked it.

462
00:28:36,771 --> 00:28:38,646
[intriguing score continues]

463
00:28:46,812 --> 00:28:49,395
♪ Thieves roam around
freely everywhere ♪

464
00:28:49,396 --> 00:28:53,354
♪ With strength in their hands
and bones to spare ♪

465
00:28:53,771 --> 00:28:56,395
♪ Built on dark deeds
and black trades they share ♪

466
00:28:56,396 --> 00:28:58,686
♪ You, the common man,
are pushed below ♪

467
00:28:58,687 --> 00:29:05,854
♪ Left only with a slave's
status to show ♪

468
00:29:07,062 --> 00:29:09,270
♪ This is a kingdom
of force and command ♪

469
00:29:09,271 --> 00:29:11,646
♪ And you are just
a puppet in its hand ♪

470
00:29:11,812 --> 00:29:14,145
♪ This world is savage,
wild in every way ♪

471
00:29:14,146 --> 00:29:16,396
♪ Like bitter thorn-apple,
poisoned all the way ♪

472
00:29:16,854 --> 00:29:19,270
♪ The rich have gates
with corruption stained deep ♪

473
00:29:19,271 --> 00:29:21,770
♪ The common man is left
to clean and sweep ♪

474
00:29:21,771 --> 00:29:25,728
♪ But will these dark deeds
lose the stains they keep? ♪

475
00:29:25,729 --> 00:29:28,103
♪ The common folk run
left and right astray ♪

476
00:29:28,104 --> 00:29:30,645
♪ People rush in frenzy
while the wealthy laugh away ♪

477
00:29:30,646 --> 00:29:33,021
♪ The common man is Nobody ♪

478
00:29:33,437 --> 00:29:35,436
♪ The public too is Nobody ♪

479
00:29:35,437 --> 00:29:37,853
♪ The common folk run
left and right astray ♪

480
00:29:37,854 --> 00:29:40,436
♪ The weak always lose,
while the powerful win the day ♪

481
00:29:40,437 --> 00:29:42,812
♪ The common man is Nobody ♪

482
00:29:43,146 --> 00:29:45,062
♪ Those in power are all buddies ♪

483
00:29:48,437 --> 00:29:50,811
[news] Someone started this
search purely on a whim,

484
00:29:50,812 --> 00:29:56,270
and it has escalated into
a massive treasure hunt.

485
00:29:56,271 --> 00:30:00,979
A whole city is running frenzied,
desperate to try their luck.

486
00:30:25,771 --> 00:30:28,270
[news] The District Collector
has declared Section 144

487
00:30:28,271 --> 00:30:31,228
across Vanchiyoor station limits
for three days.

488
00:30:31,229 --> 00:30:33,561
Unlawful gatherings,
the carrying of weapons...

489
00:30:33,562 --> 00:30:35,353
as well as public demonstrations
of any kind...

490
00:30:35,354 --> 00:30:37,020
have been strictly prohibited

491
00:30:37,021 --> 00:30:39,895
until the 17th of this month,
according to the official order.

492
00:30:39,896 --> 00:30:42,187
[police siren wails]

493
00:30:54,979 --> 00:30:56,771
[mysterious score]

494
00:31:23,479 --> 00:31:25,145
Is it even safe to stash
the money here, bro?

495
00:31:25,146 --> 00:31:26,146
Exactly!

496
00:31:26,729 --> 00:31:29,604
Once we exit the bank, we can't be
moving around with all that cash.

497
00:31:30,062 --> 00:31:30,936
It's too risky.

498
00:31:30,937 --> 00:31:32,770
So? We should just
freaking dump it over here?

499
00:31:32,771 --> 00:31:36,146
Actually, there are n... no CCTVs
for at least 300 meters here.

500
00:31:36,646 --> 00:31:37,728
It's a proper blind spot.

501
00:31:37,729 --> 00:31:40,229
And there are no shops
or houses around either, see?

502
00:31:40,354 --> 00:31:41,728
- So?
- Hey.

503
00:31:41,729 --> 00:31:43,895
Our plan remains exactly the same!

504
00:31:43,896 --> 00:31:46,395
We hide the cash we take from
the bank right here, immediately.

505
00:31:46,396 --> 00:31:47,812
Then, we go our separate ways.

506
00:31:48,062 --> 00:31:49,146
He will...

507
00:31:49,354 --> 00:31:51,478
shift the entire haul somewhere
else perfectly on schedule.

508
00:31:51,479 --> 00:31:54,811
Your plan of escaping to another state
with the cash isn't really practical.

509
00:31:54,812 --> 00:31:56,937
- Anas, come.
- This plan isn't sitting right with me!

510
00:31:58,437 --> 00:31:59,437
Hey!

511
00:32:00,479 --> 00:32:01,479
Come here.

512
00:32:02,396 --> 00:32:04,020
Look, we can't really
trust a guy like him.

513
00:32:04,021 --> 00:32:05,895
In the end, a cop will
always show his true colours.

514
00:32:05,896 --> 00:32:07,020
Watch out!

515
00:32:07,021 --> 00:32:08,854
He brought him into this.
Let him deal with it.

516
00:32:09,437 --> 00:32:11,312
Wait and watch! He'll run away
with the whole haul by then!

517
00:32:16,521 --> 00:32:18,521
[intriguing score]

518
00:32:32,187 --> 00:32:33,187
[music stops]

519
00:32:33,479 --> 00:32:35,896
[indistinct chatter]

520
00:32:51,521 --> 00:32:52,521
Sir!

521
00:32:53,437 --> 00:32:54,604
Do you remember me?

522
00:32:55,896 --> 00:32:57,186
I already came to the police
station yesterday, right?

523
00:32:57,187 --> 00:32:59,187
No, no, this isn't about that.
Don't worry.

524
00:32:59,437 --> 00:33:00,771
I'm currently under suspension.

525
00:33:01,146 --> 00:33:03,479
I tried saving you, but in the end,
I also got screwed.

526
00:33:04,562 --> 00:33:07,104
My... A friend of mine works here.

527
00:33:07,729 --> 00:33:10,521
So I came to see if he could pull
some strings to get my job back.

528
00:33:11,021 --> 00:33:12,561
I'm trying everything I can, sir.

529
00:33:12,562 --> 00:33:14,312
I'm the sole breadwinner
in my family.

530
00:33:20,271 --> 00:33:22,521
- Are you in need of money?
- No, it's not about money.

531
00:33:22,896 --> 00:33:24,187
Could you...

532
00:33:24,312 --> 00:33:25,729
do me a favour, sir?

533
00:33:26,979 --> 00:33:28,021
What is it?

534
00:33:29,771 --> 00:33:32,771
If we can somehow find
out where the m...

535
00:33:32,896 --> 00:33:34,562
missing cash is,

536
00:33:34,854 --> 00:33:36,646
they might just
lift my suspension.

537
00:33:37,396 --> 00:33:38,604
Oh, shoot!

538
00:33:38,729 --> 00:33:40,937
I just remembered. My friend
is probably waiting for me.

539
00:33:41,104 --> 00:33:45,062
[unsettling music builds]

540
00:34:01,187 --> 00:34:03,187
[unsettling music intensifies]

541
00:34:15,229 --> 00:34:17,229
[Amala sings a nursery rhyme]

542
00:34:23,729 --> 00:34:25,479
[traffic sounds]

543
00:34:27,354 --> 00:34:29,562
[Amala continues singing]

544
00:34:29,896 --> 00:34:32,937
[unsettling music]

545
00:34:47,021 --> 00:34:49,021
[unsettling score intensifies]

546
00:34:54,646 --> 00:34:55,646
Papa!

547
00:34:56,104 --> 00:34:57,146
Come.

548
00:35:17,687 --> 00:35:19,437
[tense score builds]

549
00:35:24,854 --> 00:35:28,478
Man, that guy would charter a private jet
just to chase down trouble in the sky!

550
00:35:28,479 --> 00:35:29,645
- He's the ultimate trouble magnet.
- Sir.

551
00:35:29,646 --> 00:35:31,728
- But even he couldn't handle this.
- I think they are cops.

552
00:35:31,729 --> 00:35:34,604
Hard to tell if he went off the grid
or if someone made him disappear.

553
00:35:35,146 --> 00:35:37,479
It's been three to four weeks now.
There's no word on him.

554
00:35:37,812 --> 00:35:39,270
He looks like a real
gentleman on the outside.

555
00:35:39,271 --> 00:35:41,436
But show him the money,
and he'll pull off any scam.

556
00:35:41,437 --> 00:35:43,271
Well, there would be people
like that among us too, right?

557
00:35:45,437 --> 00:35:47,312
Brother! What's our total?

558
00:35:47,687 --> 00:35:49,854
Four teas... Guys, how many
cigarettes did we smoke?

559
00:35:50,229 --> 00:35:52,062
- But it's already been paid for.
- Who paid it?

560
00:35:52,646 --> 00:35:53,646
He paid.

561
00:35:54,104 --> 00:35:56,478
Why the hell would he pay for us?
Can't we pay for ourselves?

562
00:35:56,479 --> 00:35:59,187
Or will you just pocket cash from
anyone who throws it at you?!

563
00:36:00,354 --> 00:36:01,770
I insisted that
he take the money.

564
00:36:01,771 --> 00:36:04,270
You guys have been on escort duty
for me the last two days, right?

565
00:36:04,271 --> 00:36:06,021
The least I can do
is buy tea for everyone.

566
00:36:06,354 --> 00:36:08,062
Saji, don't take any more
money from them.

567
00:36:08,521 --> 00:36:09,562
Charge it to my tab.

568
00:36:13,229 --> 00:36:14,312
Hey!

569
00:36:14,437 --> 00:36:15,521
Stop right there.

570
00:36:20,062 --> 00:36:21,687
Here's your money.
Take it.

571
00:36:22,396 --> 00:36:24,104
It's alright, bro.
It's on me.

572
00:36:26,062 --> 00:36:27,146
I told you to take it.

573
00:36:28,271 --> 00:36:29,312
Get your hands off me.

574
00:36:31,562 --> 00:36:33,437
You're not walking away
until you take this.

575
00:36:33,562 --> 00:36:35,104
[unsettling score]

576
00:36:37,229 --> 00:36:38,271
Hey! Hey!

577
00:36:38,687 --> 00:36:40,562
Cut the attitude
and take the damn cash.

578
00:36:40,812 --> 00:36:41,979
Get out of my way, you jerk!

579
00:36:42,104 --> 00:36:43,729
- Hey! Hey!
- Hey!

580
00:36:49,396 --> 00:36:51,229
We're the freakin' police, moron!
Calm down!

581
00:36:53,229 --> 00:36:55,062
[unsettling music continues]

582
00:36:57,521 --> 00:36:58,854
[objects clattering down]

583
00:37:03,437 --> 00:37:05,021
- Where is Rajeevan?
- I don't know.

584
00:37:14,646 --> 00:37:16,686
They've been tailing me
for the last two days, sir.

585
00:37:16,687 --> 00:37:18,395
At the office, fine,
I won't complain.

586
00:37:18,396 --> 00:37:19,687
But if they try
to enter my home?

587
00:37:21,604 --> 00:37:23,478
Which bank do you hold
an account in, Rajeevan?

588
00:37:23,479 --> 00:37:25,062
- SSB.
- How about your wife?

589
00:37:26,104 --> 00:37:27,104
The same one.

590
00:37:27,229 --> 00:37:29,479
Then why did you go to ISFC Bank
that day, Rajeevan?

591
00:37:30,146 --> 00:37:31,604
[intriguing music]

592
00:37:32,229 --> 00:37:34,521
You were in there for about
half an hour, weren't you?

593
00:37:35,062 --> 00:37:36,728
Were you there to see someone?

594
00:37:36,729 --> 00:37:39,729
I did ask him
if he needed any help.

595
00:37:40,146 --> 00:37:42,479
But he told me he was just
waiting for someone.

596
00:37:42,646 --> 00:37:44,312
That man was quite upset.

597
00:37:44,979 --> 00:37:46,936
He was incredibly
tensed throughout.

598
00:37:46,937 --> 00:37:49,811
I could tell something was off
right from the start.

599
00:37:49,812 --> 00:37:51,603
This has been bugging me
ever since that day.

600
00:37:51,604 --> 00:37:53,937
There were about thirty people
inside the bank that day.

601
00:37:54,146 --> 00:37:55,896
There were elderly people
among them.

602
00:37:56,229 --> 00:37:57,396
And there were children too.

603
00:37:58,187 --> 00:37:59,853
Yet, out of everyone there,

604
00:37:59,854 --> 00:38:02,854
why did they choose a well-built
man like you as a hostage?

605
00:38:05,521 --> 00:38:07,521
If it were up to me,
I wouldn't take that risk.

606
00:38:07,771 --> 00:38:10,520
Just as they were leaving,
they were saying something to him.

607
00:38:10,521 --> 00:38:11,936
I couldn't catch what
they were saying.

608
00:38:11,937 --> 00:38:15,311
From what I saw, I felt that boy
had some connection with them.

609
00:38:15,312 --> 00:38:16,895
They were clearly
working as a team, sir.

610
00:38:16,896 --> 00:38:17,979
Okay.

611
00:38:18,229 --> 00:38:22,104
Didn't something fall off you
during the struggle that day?

612
00:38:22,604 --> 00:38:23,687
What was that?

613
00:38:25,062 --> 00:38:26,187
That was a gun!

614
00:38:27,687 --> 00:38:28,853
I'm damn sure.

615
00:38:28,854 --> 00:38:30,146
A freaking gun!

616
00:38:33,521 --> 00:38:36,312
Rajeevan, I wanted to discuss
a few more things with you.

617
00:38:36,854 --> 00:38:38,937
But, what's the point
if I'm the only one talking?

618
00:38:42,146 --> 00:38:43,936
Let him sit here.
I'll tell you what to do with him.

619
00:38:43,937 --> 00:38:44,937
Okay, sir.

620
00:38:49,146 --> 00:38:52,062
[indistinct chatter]

621
00:38:53,396 --> 00:38:55,061
[indistinct chatter]

622
00:38:55,062 --> 00:38:58,311
Sir, you've been holding a man named
Rajeevan here, right? I'm his wife.

623
00:38:58,312 --> 00:38:59,437
I got a call from here.

624
00:39:00,021 --> 00:39:02,061
Please wait there, Madam.
I'll inform the officer.

625
00:39:02,062 --> 00:39:03,187
Okay.

626
00:39:05,312 --> 00:39:06,979
[unsettling music builds]

627
00:39:17,562 --> 00:39:19,562
[unsettling score intensifies]

628
00:39:33,812 --> 00:39:35,062
Hey! Wake up!

629
00:39:36,771 --> 00:39:38,979
I just got bored
and dozed off, sir.

630
00:39:39,229 --> 00:39:42,854
[rhythmic ticking]

631
00:39:43,521 --> 00:39:49,437
[indistinct chatter]

632
00:39:51,354 --> 00:39:53,478
[ambient police station sounds]

633
00:39:53,479 --> 00:39:57,354
[rhythmic ticking continues]

634
00:40:09,604 --> 00:40:16,937
[indistinct chatter]

635
00:40:18,437 --> 00:40:20,436
Tell them we've taken him
into custody, Jomon!

636
00:40:20,437 --> 00:40:22,562
Or else they'll say we're doing
absolutely nothing--

637
00:40:26,812 --> 00:40:29,187
I had an affair with someone
who works at that bank.

638
00:40:30,312 --> 00:40:33,271
That might be why Rajeevan went
to the bank that day... to confront him.

639
00:40:34,229 --> 00:40:36,896
I don't know if Rajeevan
has mentioned this to you, sir.

640
00:40:37,187 --> 00:40:40,021
Or if he's still being held here
because he hasn't said it yet.

641
00:40:40,771 --> 00:40:43,771
Basically, I don't know anything,
and nobody here is telling me anything.

642
00:40:44,521 --> 00:40:47,396
I can give you all the details
I know about that man.

643
00:40:49,271 --> 00:40:50,979
You just have to verify
it with him, sir.

644
00:40:52,271 --> 00:40:54,229
He has a family.

645
00:40:55,062 --> 00:40:56,104
So...

646
00:41:00,104 --> 00:41:02,771
[poignant score]

647
00:41:13,521 --> 00:41:15,853
Meera, I had a word with Sreekanth,
whom you told us about.

648
00:41:15,854 --> 00:41:17,478
But he didn't admit to anything.

649
00:41:17,479 --> 00:41:18,937
He denied knowing you.

650
00:41:21,896 --> 00:41:23,979
Sir, my kids are home alone.
Can I leave now?

651
00:41:24,229 --> 00:41:26,646
We're letting Rajeevan go right now.
You can leave together.

652
00:41:49,896 --> 00:41:50,896
Shall we go?

653
00:41:57,396 --> 00:41:59,061
[indistinct chatter]

654
00:41:59,062 --> 00:42:00,521
[rapid camera clicks]

655
00:42:00,687 --> 00:42:03,521
[indistinct chatter]

656
00:42:04,479 --> 00:42:09,061
A major update is coming in right now
regarding the Vanchiyoor bank robbery case.

657
00:42:09,062 --> 00:42:11,811
We've just received word
that the police have questioned

658
00:42:11,812 --> 00:42:14,562
a Secretariat official
in connection with this case.

659
00:42:14,729 --> 00:42:16,395
The most intriguing fact
in this is that

660
00:42:16,396 --> 00:42:20,645
this same official was taken hostage
by the robbers on the day of the heist.

661
00:42:20,646 --> 00:42:23,770
Even when the police say
all suspects have been identified,

662
00:42:23,771 --> 00:42:25,520
they haven't been able to recover

663
00:42:25,521 --> 00:42:29,728
the nearly 17 crore rupees
stolen from the bank so far.

664
00:42:29,729 --> 00:42:31,479
Police are now investigating
the possibility

665
00:42:31,646 --> 00:42:36,353
that a fourth person could be involved,
rather than just three suspects.

666
00:42:36,354 --> 00:42:38,520
What remains to be seen now is,

667
00:42:38,521 --> 00:42:42,978
whether Rajeevan's interrogation
has yielded any further leads.

668
00:42:42,979 --> 00:42:48,311
Regardless, this probe is moving
in a completely unexpected direction.

669
00:42:48,312 --> 00:42:51,686
Even if some unexpected names
surface on the suspect list,

670
00:42:51,687 --> 00:42:53,811
it should come as no surprise.

671
00:42:53,812 --> 00:42:56,979
That is the inside information we have
from our sources within the police.

672
00:42:59,021 --> 00:43:03,062
Do you know what an ordinary
government employee's salary is?

673
00:43:04,271 --> 00:43:08,104
Can that salary actually sustain
a family of four nowadays?

674
00:43:09,146 --> 00:43:10,311
Absolutely not...

675
00:43:10,312 --> 00:43:13,270
and that's the reality this officer,
Rajeevan, is laying out for us.

676
00:43:13,271 --> 00:43:16,979
Somehow, this officer tracks down
three hardcore criminals.

677
00:43:17,521 --> 00:43:21,603
He lures them in with a share of the spoils
and convinces them to execute a robbery.

678
00:43:21,604 --> 00:43:26,061
During the heist, he poses as
a regular customer inside that very bank,

679
00:43:26,062 --> 00:43:28,603
overseeing the entire operation.

680
00:43:28,604 --> 00:43:29,728
Then,

681
00:43:29,729 --> 00:43:31,937
to put up a smokescreen
for the witnesses,

682
00:43:32,271 --> 00:43:36,270
he pretends to take a beating
from the robbers.

683
00:43:36,271 --> 00:43:40,061
He gets into their vehicle along with them,
as if he's being taken hostage.

684
00:43:40,062 --> 00:43:43,603
And boom... a flawless bank robbery
is executed right under our noses.

685
00:43:43,604 --> 00:43:45,020
As always...

686
00:43:45,021 --> 00:43:47,437
As always, the police
and the public...

687
00:43:47,687 --> 00:43:49,186
are left looking like fools.

688
00:43:49,187 --> 00:43:51,187
But this evil mastermind's cruelty...

689
00:43:51,729 --> 00:43:53,645
It doesn't end there, you know.

690
00:43:53,646 --> 00:43:57,061
He gets down on the way
with the stolen cash,

691
00:43:57,062 --> 00:44:00,395
and uses a truck driver
he had hired beforehand...

692
00:44:00,396 --> 00:44:04,896
to engineer a fatal crash, wiping
all three accomplices out for good.

693
00:44:05,229 --> 00:44:08,896
Zero evidence left behind.
No one to share the loot with!

694
00:44:10,062 --> 00:44:11,896
While the police and the public...

695
00:44:12,396 --> 00:44:15,645
were tearing the city apart
looking for that 17-crore haul,

696
00:44:15,646 --> 00:44:17,062
this officer...

697
00:44:17,271 --> 00:44:21,437
was living the high life
on that stolen loot... with his wife.

698
00:44:22,271 --> 00:44:23,437
Pretty smooth, right?

699
00:44:26,062 --> 00:44:27,354
[elevator dings]

700
00:44:28,396 --> 00:44:29,896
Mumma, come fast!

701
00:44:34,771 --> 00:44:36,021
Hold on, let's wait for Papa.

702
00:44:53,354 --> 00:44:55,021
[suspicious music plays]

703
00:45:09,771 --> 00:45:12,770
♪ Hey, have you heard
what's going around? ♪

704
00:45:12,771 --> 00:45:14,770
♪ Do you know what
they say he's done? ♪

705
00:45:14,771 --> 00:45:16,853
♪ People say he's dragged
his own name down ♪

706
00:45:16,854 --> 00:45:18,146
♪ Really? ♪

707
00:45:18,812 --> 00:45:20,978
♪ Looks like a thief,
doesn't he? ♪

708
00:45:20,979 --> 00:45:22,978
♪ Must be hiding some secret,
can't you see? ♪

709
00:45:22,979 --> 00:45:26,271
♪ They say he's woven
lies endlessly ♪

710
00:45:27,146 --> 00:45:30,312
♪ His clothes are neat,
his manners refined ♪

711
00:45:31,312 --> 00:45:34,978
♪ He keeps to himself,
so no secrets unwind ♪

712
00:45:34,979 --> 00:45:36,770
♪ To the world he says,
“I didn't do it” ♪

713
00:45:36,771 --> 00:45:39,395
♪ With an innocent face,
he thinks he'll get through it ♪

714
00:45:39,396 --> 00:45:41,936
♪ I'm sure he's throwing
dust in everyone's eyes ♪

715
00:45:41,937 --> 00:45:44,937
♪ And getting away
again and again with his lies ♪

716
00:45:46,562 --> 00:45:48,604
♪ Oh, just look at him. ♪

717
00:45:51,771 --> 00:45:54,895
♪ Look at those eyes,
watch closely and see ♪

718
00:45:54,896 --> 00:45:59,521
♪ Slithering like a snake,
moving wild and free ♪

719
00:45:59,937 --> 00:46:03,686
♪ Look at those eyes,
watch closely and see ♪

720
00:46:03,687 --> 00:46:08,062
♪ Just look how they move,
so restlessly ♪

721
00:46:32,562 --> 00:46:33,687
Sir!

722
00:46:34,354 --> 00:46:35,521
My name is Jose.

723
00:46:35,729 --> 00:46:37,729
You probably won't
recognise me by my name.

724
00:46:38,854 --> 00:46:40,437
But you'll know
my son-in-law's name.

725
00:46:41,229 --> 00:46:42,354
Peter.

726
00:46:43,521 --> 00:46:44,687
Once the job was done,

727
00:46:44,812 --> 00:46:47,479
you killed him and his friends
and put them six feet under.

728
00:46:48,062 --> 00:46:49,646
That's honestly none of my business.

729
00:46:50,187 --> 00:46:51,812
That just shows your expertise.

730
00:46:52,937 --> 00:46:54,020
But...

731
00:46:54,021 --> 00:46:57,771
you think you can hoard a fortune
everyone worked hard for, all for yourself?

732
00:46:58,229 --> 00:46:59,811
That's taking things way too far, sir.

733
00:46:59,812 --> 00:47:01,145
Peter has left
a wife and child behind.

734
00:47:01,146 --> 00:47:02,270
So, here's the deal...

735
00:47:02,271 --> 00:47:04,646
Give us half of everything you got.

736
00:47:06,896 --> 00:47:08,811
Everything I've got
is right here on me.

737
00:47:08,812 --> 00:47:10,061
Why settle for half?

738
00:47:10,062 --> 00:47:11,228
I'll give you
the whole damn lot.

739
00:47:11,229 --> 00:47:13,020
- How about that?
- No need to get angry, sir.

740
00:47:13,021 --> 00:47:14,645
Don't you have a shred
of common sense?!

741
00:47:14,646 --> 00:47:16,645
If some idiot
feeds you a bunch of garbage,

742
00:47:16,646 --> 00:47:19,437
you swallow it whole
and come here to ruin my peace!

743
00:47:19,937 --> 00:47:21,979
Step in front of me again
demanding a cut,

744
00:47:22,146 --> 00:47:23,396
- and I'll kick your--
- Hey, Rajeevan!

745
00:47:25,771 --> 00:47:28,396
You aren't doing any work here,
and you're disrupting everyone else too.

746
00:47:29,062 --> 00:47:30,187
Sign out and go.

747
00:47:30,479 --> 00:47:31,896
You're on half-day leave for today.

748
00:47:36,021 --> 00:47:37,396
This is a paid leave, right, sir?

749
00:47:42,062 --> 00:47:43,062
[car door unlocks]

750
00:47:47,062 --> 00:47:48,854
It's spreading like wildfire, sir.

751
00:47:49,229 --> 00:47:52,020
I personally saw it in, like,
thr... three or four WhatsApp groups.

752
00:47:52,021 --> 00:47:54,396
They're literally exposing your
entire life history, sir.

753
00:47:55,479 --> 00:47:57,520
Do you know where this
Palanaadan Varghese's office is?

754
00:47:57,521 --> 00:48:00,061
Sir, please don't make
an issue out of this.

755
00:48:00,062 --> 00:48:01,645
The internet is full
of guys like him.

756
00:48:01,646 --> 00:48:02,895
If not him,
it'll be someone else.

757
00:48:02,896 --> 00:48:04,021
You know how it is, sir.

758
00:48:04,229 --> 00:48:05,312
I didn't, until now.

759
00:48:06,146 --> 00:48:07,229
Now I do.

760
00:48:08,479 --> 00:48:09,521
Sir...

761
00:48:09,729 --> 00:48:12,229
In all honesty... the two of us
are the ones stuck in a mess.

762
00:48:12,562 --> 00:48:16,104
You lost your peace of mind, sir.
And I... lost my job.

763
00:48:17,312 --> 00:48:20,853
I hoped finding those robbers
would win my job back,

764
00:48:20,854 --> 00:48:23,021
but those guys...
m-m... they're dead and gone.

765
00:48:25,604 --> 00:48:28,896
The only way left is to find
the cash they stole.

766
00:48:29,521 --> 00:48:31,812
But at this point, there's literally
nowhere left to look.

767
00:48:33,646 --> 00:48:35,187
I don't even know
what to do anymore.

768
00:48:37,146 --> 00:48:39,687
Sir, what if we try to track
down the money together?

769
00:48:40,187 --> 00:48:42,895
I mean, you were in the car with them
for a bit, weren't you, sir?

770
00:48:42,896 --> 00:48:45,312
If you manage
to remember anything,

771
00:48:45,437 --> 00:48:46,771
I can take it over from there.

772
00:48:47,104 --> 00:48:49,896
You'll get your peace of mind back, sir.
And as for me, my job.

773
00:48:51,229 --> 00:48:52,937
- What was your name again?
- Anas.

774
00:48:55,687 --> 00:48:58,729
Anas, hunting down thieves
and recovering cash isn't my job.

775
00:48:59,187 --> 00:49:01,521
Isn't that what the system
and you cops are here for?

776
00:49:01,646 --> 00:49:03,311
You just do your own job
properly first.

777
00:49:03,312 --> 00:49:05,312
Then my peace of mind
will return on its own.

778
00:49:07,146 --> 00:49:08,353
Brother!

779
00:49:08,354 --> 00:49:09,687
- One tea, on my tab.
- Okay.

780
00:49:13,062 --> 00:49:15,395
- Should we do it?
- Let's just give it a shot.

781
00:49:15,396 --> 00:49:17,895
Is that even going to work?
What if he does something?

782
00:49:17,896 --> 00:49:18,896
No way, man.

783
00:49:19,146 --> 00:49:20,728
Let's just try.
What do you say?

784
00:49:20,729 --> 00:49:22,312
Nothing's gonna happen.
Let's try.

785
00:49:25,437 --> 00:49:26,479
Uncle!

786
00:49:27,021 --> 00:49:29,562
- Hi! We're from Jiya's school.
- Hi!

787
00:49:29,812 --> 00:49:31,187
Uncle, could you help us out?

788
00:49:31,396 --> 00:49:32,979
- Could you give us some cash?
- What?

789
00:49:33,271 --> 00:49:34,896
Like, ten thousand rupees.

790
00:49:36,562 --> 00:49:37,686
What do you need
all that money for?

791
00:49:37,687 --> 00:49:39,270
Well... to party, Uncle.

792
00:49:39,271 --> 00:49:40,812
And then to grab some food.

793
00:49:43,437 --> 00:49:44,437
Oh.

794
00:49:45,146 --> 00:49:46,896
You can go ask for that
at your own homes.

795
00:49:47,187 --> 00:49:50,395
But it's not like our homes have
stolen bank money lying around, Uncle.

796
00:49:50,396 --> 00:49:53,061
You've got 17 crores, right?
Can't you share a little with us too?

797
00:49:53,062 --> 00:49:55,604
He has two daughters, right?
Must be saving it for their dowries.

798
00:49:57,771 --> 00:49:59,436
Uncle, if you don't have
the cash, never mind.

799
00:49:59,437 --> 00:50:01,479
But could you teach us how you
pulled off the job instead?

800
00:50:04,354 --> 00:50:06,521
Sure thing! You boys can
join me for my next hit.

801
00:50:06,896 --> 00:50:08,436
I've already scouted
out another bank.

802
00:50:08,437 --> 00:50:10,646
Oh no, Uncle! Will you kill us
once the job is done?

803
00:50:11,437 --> 00:50:13,271
Well, that's just how
my modus operandi is.

804
00:50:13,479 --> 00:50:15,103
Once the job is done,
I have to get rid of you.

805
00:50:15,104 --> 00:50:16,646
Ah! Just give us the cash then.

806
00:50:16,979 --> 00:50:18,104
In your dreams!

807
00:50:18,521 --> 00:50:20,187
Come on, Uncle!
Don't storm off like that.

808
00:50:20,396 --> 00:50:23,479
After all, your daughter
is my schoolmate, right?

809
00:50:23,687 --> 00:50:25,937
Can't you at least show me
some consideration for that?

810
00:50:26,104 --> 00:50:27,687
One of them is named Jiya, right?

811
00:50:28,062 --> 00:50:29,604
What's the younger one's name?

812
00:50:29,937 --> 00:50:31,937
Doesn't matter,
she's still Uncle's blood, right?

813
00:50:32,229 --> 00:50:34,978
Just like how Uncle loves his child,
we can show her some love too.

814
00:50:34,979 --> 00:50:37,479
But Uncle just doesn't seem
very affectionate, man.

815
00:50:37,646 --> 00:50:39,437
So we don't need to show
her any love either.

816
00:50:39,771 --> 00:50:42,146
Oh boy... Sir is getting
really pissed off.

817
00:50:44,896 --> 00:50:45,979
Get lost.

818
00:50:47,896 --> 00:50:49,353
Hey! His hand!

819
00:50:49,354 --> 00:50:51,061
- Sorry!
- Get him out of his car!

820
00:50:51,062 --> 00:50:52,395
Hey, you better pay us!

821
00:50:52,396 --> 00:50:53,395
[indistinct clamouring]

822
00:50:53,396 --> 00:50:55,061
- Move aside!
- Hurl that stone at him!

823
00:50:55,062 --> 00:50:57,729
[indistinct clamouring]

824
00:50:59,354 --> 00:51:01,896
[dog barking in distance]

825
00:51:07,396 --> 00:51:08,478
[door closes]

826
00:51:08,479 --> 00:51:10,021
[Amala hums a tune]

827
00:51:20,896 --> 00:51:24,771
[ambient school sounds]

828
00:51:29,729 --> 00:51:30,771
Mumma, Papa! Bye!

829
00:51:37,979 --> 00:51:40,271
[unsettling music]

830
00:51:45,771 --> 00:51:48,354
[unsettling music intensifies]

831
00:51:50,896 --> 00:51:52,146
It's getting late.
Let's go.

832
00:52:10,812 --> 00:52:14,271
[unsettling music intensifies]

833
00:52:15,271 --> 00:52:16,354
[music stops]

834
00:52:17,687 --> 00:52:19,812
[school bell rings]

835
00:52:19,937 --> 00:52:23,812
[children playing in schoolyard]

836
00:52:27,062 --> 00:52:29,396
[unsettling music]

837
00:52:39,437 --> 00:52:40,562
Take this.

838
00:52:41,229 --> 00:52:42,354
Thanks, Uncle.

839
00:52:42,854 --> 00:52:44,186
Whoa!

840
00:52:44,187 --> 00:52:45,521
Dude!

841
00:52:45,812 --> 00:52:48,104
- Let's hurry.
- Come on, come on.

842
00:52:53,729 --> 00:52:56,020
They're just kids, man!
High-schoolers!

843
00:52:56,021 --> 00:52:57,395
They gave him a tiny scare,

844
00:52:57,396 --> 00:52:59,229
and he pulled 10,000 from
the ATM and gave it to them.

845
00:53:04,146 --> 00:53:05,603
Didn't I tell you, bro?

846
00:53:05,604 --> 00:53:08,271
He definitely has the money.
I am 150% certain.

847
00:53:09,146 --> 00:53:11,853
[Anas] You're in a bigger
mess than I am, sir.

848
00:53:11,854 --> 00:53:14,562
In all honesty... the two of us
are the ones stuck in a mess.

849
00:53:14,854 --> 00:53:18,562
The only way left is to find
the cash they stole.

850
00:53:18,812 --> 00:53:21,646
You'll get your peace of mind back, sir.
And as for me, my job.

851
00:53:22,062 --> 00:53:23,937
What if we try to track
down the money together?

852
00:53:29,812 --> 00:53:30,812
Sir...

853
00:53:35,646 --> 00:53:38,187
[muffled street traffic sounds]

854
00:53:42,896 --> 00:53:44,312
[car engine starts]

855
00:53:51,437 --> 00:53:52,479
Here you go.

856
00:53:55,562 --> 00:53:56,896
Sir... Are you ready?

857
00:53:57,646 --> 00:53:59,312
[intriguing score builds]

858
00:54:04,354 --> 00:54:05,479
Ready.

859
00:54:06,146 --> 00:54:10,521
100... 99... 98... 97...

860
00:54:10,646 --> 00:54:12,812
96... 95...

861
00:54:14,604 --> 00:54:17,229
77... 76...

862
00:54:17,729 --> 00:54:20,311
[continues counting down]

863
00:54:20,312 --> 00:54:21,771
Go, go, go!

864
00:54:22,354 --> 00:54:23,354
Hey!

865
00:54:23,687 --> 00:54:24,978
Step on it, man!

866
00:54:24,979 --> 00:54:26,353
- Go fast!
- Left or right, sir?

867
00:54:26,354 --> 00:54:27,521
Speed up!

868
00:54:27,771 --> 00:54:29,646
Sir! Left or right?

869
00:54:29,896 --> 00:54:31,021
68...

870
00:54:31,562 --> 00:54:32,562
67...

871
00:54:37,479 --> 00:54:38,687
Left.

872
00:54:41,187 --> 00:54:42,936
Can you all just shut up?!
I'll handle the wheel.

873
00:54:42,937 --> 00:54:44,686
- Just go faster, man!
- Drive faster!

874
00:54:44,687 --> 00:54:45,603
Can you guys just calm down?

875
00:54:45,604 --> 00:54:47,061
Turn left!
There's a U-turn ahead!

876
00:54:47,062 --> 00:54:48,145
I can see that!

877
00:54:48,146 --> 00:54:49,312
They're right behind us!

878
00:54:49,979 --> 00:54:51,979
Stop swerving and just floor it!

879
00:54:53,021 --> 00:54:54,437
- Just go, man!
- 76...

880
00:54:54,604 --> 00:54:55,812
75...

881
00:54:56,396 --> 00:54:58,228
- 74...
- They're right behind us, gun it!

882
00:54:58,229 --> 00:54:59,645
- 73...
- They're gaining on us, man!

883
00:54:59,646 --> 00:55:00,646
72...

884
00:55:03,229 --> 00:55:04,229
71...

885
00:55:04,979 --> 00:55:05,979
70...

886
00:55:06,896 --> 00:55:07,896
69...

887
00:55:08,896 --> 00:55:09,896
68...

888
00:55:10,187 --> 00:55:11,604
- Sir...
- 67...

889
00:55:12,687 --> 00:55:13,687
66...

890
00:55:14,646 --> 00:55:15,646
65...

891
00:55:16,729 --> 00:55:17,729
64...

892
00:55:18,646 --> 00:55:20,354
[ambient traffic sounds]

893
00:55:31,896 --> 00:55:35,437
[traffic sounds get louder]

894
00:55:56,187 --> 00:55:59,186
Didn't I tell you a thousand times
that we didn't need any outsiders?!

895
00:55:59,187 --> 00:56:02,311
Look, you're the sole reason
we're running for our lives right now!

896
00:56:02,312 --> 00:56:03,979
Dude, it's true that he's a cop.

897
00:56:04,146 --> 00:56:06,228
I brought him in thinking
he'd be useful to us in the future.

898
00:56:06,229 --> 00:56:07,270
Yeah, real useful!

899
00:56:07,271 --> 00:56:08,978
Do you know what would've
happened if I hadn't seen his gun?

900
00:56:08,979 --> 00:56:10,646
These two would've run off
with everything we got!

901
00:56:11,187 --> 00:56:13,937
Dude, just calm down! Let's get
to safety first, then we can talk.

902
00:56:14,104 --> 00:56:16,895
Talk about what? I have
absolutely nothing to say to you.

903
00:56:16,896 --> 00:56:18,936
Just take your share
of the cut and get lost.

904
00:56:18,937 --> 00:56:20,686
Bro, just hear me out!

905
00:56:20,687 --> 00:56:24,812
I know exactly how to ensure
he never pulls a stunt like this again.

906
00:56:25,396 --> 00:56:27,020
He's not going to pull
anymore stunts, dude!

907
00:56:27,021 --> 00:56:29,353
I knew it the moment I saw him
giving that lecture yesterday.

908
00:56:29,354 --> 00:56:30,436
His damn CCTV!

909
00:56:30,437 --> 00:56:33,645
C... c... camera...
B... b... b... blind spot.

910
00:56:33,646 --> 00:56:34,812
Ugh! To hell with him!

911
00:56:35,312 --> 00:56:36,312
Sheesh!

912
00:56:37,312 --> 00:56:39,437
[score intensifies dramatically]

913
00:56:42,354 --> 00:56:43,436
Stop!

914
00:56:43,437 --> 00:56:45,062
[music fades out]

915
00:56:47,437 --> 00:56:48,521
What is it, sir?

916
00:56:50,729 --> 00:56:53,729
Sir, d... did... did
anything ring a bell?

917
00:56:56,021 --> 00:56:58,103
- Let me think.
- Dude, he's a cop.

918
00:56:58,104 --> 00:56:59,270
His damn CCTV!

919
00:56:59,271 --> 00:57:02,062
C... c... camera...
B... b... b... blind spot.

920
00:57:06,146 --> 00:57:08,812
Well... did you remember anything?

921
00:57:11,187 --> 00:57:12,271
Yes, I did.

922
00:57:13,229 --> 00:57:14,646
But nothing useful to you.

923
00:57:16,771 --> 00:57:18,104
Th... Then...

924
00:57:18,312 --> 00:57:20,521
It's just a little bit further.
Shall we go and see the rest?

925
00:57:21,354 --> 00:57:22,771
No. Let's call it a day.

926
00:57:23,187 --> 00:57:24,396
I've got a bit of a headache.

927
00:57:32,146 --> 00:57:33,479
Sir, just a little further--

928
00:57:39,312 --> 00:57:40,396
Or I can...

929
00:57:42,812 --> 00:57:43,854
Hey!

930
00:57:45,229 --> 00:57:47,062
[sound of car driving away]

931
00:57:47,521 --> 00:57:48,645
Damn it.

932
00:57:48,646 --> 00:57:50,562
[lift whirring and operating]

933
00:57:58,104 --> 00:57:59,104
[elevator dings]

934
00:58:04,062 --> 00:58:05,521
[elevator doors closing]

935
00:58:06,479 --> 00:58:07,812
[tapping on door]

936
00:58:16,479 --> 00:58:17,896
[knocking on door]

937
00:58:20,146 --> 00:58:21,146
[door opens]

938
00:58:24,896 --> 00:58:25,896
Hey!

939
00:58:28,104 --> 00:58:29,562
[unsettling music]

940
00:58:31,896 --> 00:58:32,896
Hey!

941
00:58:33,062 --> 00:58:34,354
[elevator dings]

942
00:58:37,062 --> 00:58:38,979
[in Hindi] Shut the door quickly!
He's coming!

943
00:58:39,104 --> 00:58:41,437
[loud beeping sound]

944
00:59:23,896 --> 00:59:24,896
[elevator dings]

945
01:00:02,521 --> 01:00:03,521
[glass cracks]

946
01:00:06,437 --> 01:00:08,146
[rapidly pressing all elevator buttons]

947
01:00:15,604 --> 01:00:16,979
[elevator dings, loud thud]

948
01:00:27,521 --> 01:00:28,646
My bat!
Oh no!

949
01:00:37,062 --> 01:00:38,979
[lift whirring]

950
01:00:48,479 --> 01:00:50,271
[lift door opens]

951
01:00:53,562 --> 01:00:56,853
Surely you're aware of what's being said
about Rajeevan on social media, right?

952
01:00:56,854 --> 01:00:58,854
Isn't he partly
responsible for that?

953
01:00:59,396 --> 01:01:01,686
This isn't a first-time
incident, Meera.

954
01:01:01,687 --> 01:01:03,812
The police have been marching
in and out of here constantly.

955
01:01:03,937 --> 01:01:06,812
And it has caused a huge inconvenience
for your neighbours.

956
01:01:07,354 --> 01:01:09,853
They've already filed
complaints multiple times now.

957
01:01:09,854 --> 01:01:12,811
If anything like this happens again,
you will have to find another flat.

958
01:01:12,812 --> 01:01:13,978
We're making ourselves clear.

959
01:01:13,979 --> 01:01:15,187
How is that even fair, Rinny?

960
01:01:15,896 --> 01:01:17,770
Just because I stayed quiet
and let you talk,

961
01:01:17,771 --> 01:01:19,229
you think you can
walk all over me?

962
01:01:19,354 --> 01:01:21,645
Wasn't this security guard
appointed by the association?

963
01:01:21,646 --> 01:01:24,728
He's the one who broke into our flat!
Is that also our fault now?

964
01:01:24,729 --> 01:01:26,561
- But it was Rajeevan who got--
- Enough!

965
01:01:26,562 --> 01:01:29,270
If the association doesn't compensate
us for the damages we faced,

966
01:01:29,271 --> 01:01:31,646
I will be the one to file
a police complaint against you.

967
01:01:33,146 --> 01:01:34,187
Excuse me!

968
01:01:38,187 --> 01:01:39,646
Rajeevan, come inside for a second.

969
01:01:43,979 --> 01:01:45,062
[music fades out]

970
01:01:50,896 --> 01:01:51,896
[door shuts]

971
01:01:52,312 --> 01:01:53,312
Rajeevan...

972
01:01:53,604 --> 01:01:55,646
This is the room where
my children and I sleep.

973
01:01:56,062 --> 01:01:57,936
For a complete stranger
to break in here...

974
01:01:57,937 --> 01:01:59,311
do you know how
violating that feels?

975
01:01:59,312 --> 01:02:01,728
How are we supposed to sleep
peacefully in here anymore?

976
01:02:01,729 --> 01:02:04,354
How many times will I have to check
if someone is hiding in here?

977
01:02:06,771 --> 01:02:09,062
This was the one space in this entire house
that we could actually call ours.

978
01:02:13,146 --> 01:02:14,771
Don't you have anything
to say, Rajeevan?

979
01:02:15,771 --> 01:02:16,853
Fine, just go!

980
01:02:16,854 --> 01:02:19,771
Go spin another story to our daughter
and put the blame on me again.

981
01:02:20,271 --> 01:02:22,937
[unsettling score]

982
01:02:33,437 --> 01:02:34,479
Sir...

983
01:02:35,146 --> 01:02:36,687
Just show this note at the store.

984
01:02:37,271 --> 01:02:39,271
I've listed out everything
you need on it.

985
01:02:40,771 --> 01:02:43,146
Once you buy them,
just give me a call, sir.

986
01:02:44,979 --> 01:02:45,979
Let's go.

987
01:02:51,604 --> 01:02:53,229
[car engine running]

988
01:03:00,062 --> 01:03:01,479
[auto-rickshaw honks and crashes]

989
01:03:05,021 --> 01:03:07,187
[disturbing score intensifies]

990
01:03:07,854 --> 01:03:09,228
[handbrake engages with a click]

991
01:03:09,229 --> 01:03:10,312
[engine turns off]

992
01:03:10,604 --> 01:03:12,021
[indistinct chatter]

993
01:03:17,812 --> 01:03:19,521
[disturbing music swells]

994
01:03:24,187 --> 01:03:25,187
Come out!

995
01:03:27,771 --> 01:03:29,478
[heartbeat intensifies]

996
01:03:29,479 --> 01:03:30,479
Come out!

997
01:03:35,771 --> 01:03:38,479
[indistinct chatter]

998
01:03:41,062 --> 01:03:42,395
Hey, how's that fair?

999
01:03:42,396 --> 01:03:43,853
I saw it happen
right before my eyes.

1000
01:03:43,854 --> 01:03:45,686
He's the one who rammed into
the auto rickshaw, right?

1001
01:03:45,687 --> 01:03:47,228
And now you're claiming
it's the auto driver's fault?

1002
01:03:47,229 --> 01:03:48,103
That's rich!

1003
01:03:48,104 --> 01:03:50,061
Look, sir already agreed
to pay for the repairs!

1004
01:03:50,062 --> 01:03:51,061
So, what's your problem now?

1005
01:03:51,062 --> 01:03:52,561
This auto is a poor man's
livelihood, isn't it?

1006
01:03:52,562 --> 01:03:54,728
Stop dragging this out.
Just give him some cash and settle it here.

1007
01:03:54,729 --> 01:03:55,686
That would be for the best, sir.

1008
01:03:55,687 --> 01:03:57,687
Why get caught up
in a headache like this, sir?

1009
01:03:57,812 --> 01:03:59,521
Alright, how much do I owe you?

1010
01:04:00,562 --> 01:04:02,562
[whispering secretly]

1011
01:04:03,771 --> 01:04:04,937
Go on, give him five, sir.

1012
01:04:05,271 --> 01:04:07,021
- Five as in?
- As in five lakhs.

1013
01:04:10,062 --> 01:04:11,062
Five lakhs?

1014
01:04:17,437 --> 01:04:18,437
Oh.

1015
01:04:20,479 --> 01:04:21,812
That's a bit too low, isn't it?

1016
01:04:22,354 --> 01:04:23,936
How about I buy him
a brand-new auto instead?

1017
01:04:23,937 --> 01:04:26,311
He can decide that himself.
Just pay up and settle this.

1018
01:04:26,312 --> 01:04:27,936
Just give it, sir!
Let them feast on it.

1019
01:04:27,937 --> 01:04:30,061
Sir, it's best to just pay up
and be done with it.

1020
01:04:30,062 --> 01:04:32,561
Otherwise, dealing with courts
and cops will be a massive mess.

1021
01:04:32,562 --> 01:04:34,770
Look how many people are here
waiting for this to be settled, sir.

1022
01:04:34,771 --> 01:04:36,395
Stop wasting our time.

1023
01:04:36,396 --> 01:04:38,186
It's not like you're short
on cash anyway, right sir?

1024
01:04:38,187 --> 01:04:40,562
Just tell us where the cash is.
We'll go grab it ourselves.

1025
01:04:40,896 --> 01:04:42,437
Where is it kept, sir?
At your house?

1026
01:04:46,187 --> 01:04:47,646
I'll pay for the actual repairs.

1027
01:04:48,229 --> 01:04:49,770
If not, let the cops handle it.

1028
01:04:49,771 --> 01:04:51,062
I'm ready to deal with the mess.

1029
01:04:51,646 --> 01:04:53,146
Why bring the police into this, sir?

1030
01:04:54,146 --> 01:04:56,186
- Sir, I don't have it with me.
- Bring it later.

1031
01:04:56,187 --> 01:04:57,187
Sir.

1032
01:04:58,854 --> 01:04:59,896
No, I was alone.

1033
01:05:00,396 --> 01:05:01,145
What's this about?

1034
01:05:01,146 --> 01:05:03,146
He got into a street fight, sir.
With those guys over there.

1035
01:05:04,687 --> 01:05:07,271
[commotion and grunting as a fight ensues]

1036
01:05:29,062 --> 01:05:30,229
[rear-view mirror shatters]

1037
01:05:39,896 --> 01:05:42,771
[disturbing music slows
down distortionally]

1038
01:05:47,937 --> 01:05:49,479
[music rises again]

1039
01:06:00,646 --> 01:06:01,896
[windshield shatters loudly]

1040
01:06:03,729 --> 01:06:05,646
[disturbing music slows down]

1041
01:06:08,396 --> 01:06:09,937
[music intensifies]

1042
01:06:46,479 --> 01:06:47,771
[stabbing sound]

1043
01:06:55,354 --> 01:06:56,646
[stabbing sound]

1044
01:07:11,812 --> 01:07:13,521
[repeated stabbing sounds]

1045
01:07:38,021 --> 01:07:39,354
[music fades out]

1046
01:07:40,062 --> 01:07:42,436
If you keep stirring up
new problems every single day,

1047
01:07:42,437 --> 01:07:44,146
it's gonna put us cops
in a major fix, man!

1048
01:07:44,479 --> 01:07:47,062
If a crime happens, isn't it
your job to catch the criminals?

1049
01:07:47,562 --> 01:07:48,646
Isn't it?

1050
01:07:49,021 --> 01:07:50,271
But instead of doing your job,

1051
01:07:50,646 --> 01:07:52,436
you throw me, the victim
of that very crime,

1052
01:07:52,437 --> 01:07:54,479
to the media, the public and...

1053
01:07:54,604 --> 01:07:56,520
criminals like these?
What kind of policing is that, sir?

1054
01:07:56,521 --> 01:07:58,145
Shut your mouth
and wait over there!

1055
01:07:58,146 --> 01:07:59,187
Come with me, Rajeevan.

1056
01:08:03,062 --> 01:08:05,646
Haven't you learned about
the food chain in school, Rajeevan?

1057
01:08:05,771 --> 01:08:06,771
The food chain.

1058
01:08:07,562 --> 01:08:09,354
You must have forgotten.
Let me make it simple for you.

1059
01:08:10,437 --> 01:08:11,812
A grasshopper eats grass.

1060
01:08:12,062 --> 01:08:13,854
[intense music]

1061
01:08:16,396 --> 01:08:18,062
That grasshopper
gets eaten by a frog.

1062
01:08:20,271 --> 01:08:22,062
The frog is then eaten
by a snake.

1063
01:08:25,062 --> 01:08:26,771
And the snake
is eaten by an eagle.

1064
01:08:28,687 --> 01:08:30,145
When that eagle dies,

1065
01:08:30,146 --> 01:08:32,562
it turns into fertiliser for
the very grass we started with.

1066
01:08:36,771 --> 01:08:39,687
Our society works just like
a food chain, Rajeevan.

1067
01:08:39,979 --> 01:08:43,561
And that includes
me, you, the media...

1068
01:08:43,562 --> 01:08:46,479
the police, the public...
and even the criminals.

1069
01:08:47,312 --> 01:08:48,771
But there's one difference here.

1070
01:08:49,271 --> 01:08:51,354
To survive in this
societal food chain,

1071
01:08:51,562 --> 01:08:53,771
a grasshopper cannot
survive on grass alone.

1072
01:08:54,062 --> 01:08:55,396
It has to consume the frog too.

1073
01:09:00,437 --> 01:09:02,146
[music slowly fades out]

1074
01:09:04,437 --> 01:09:09,479
[phone rings]

1075
01:09:10,021 --> 01:09:11,437
- Hello.
- Hello!

1076
01:09:11,729 --> 01:09:13,728
Madam, we're calling from
the Vanchiyoor police station.

1077
01:09:13,729 --> 01:09:15,353
Rajeevan sir got into
an altercation on the road,

1078
01:09:15,354 --> 01:09:16,854
and he's currently being
held here at the station.

1079
01:09:17,729 --> 01:09:19,853
If you can come down right away,
we can release him on bail.

1080
01:09:19,854 --> 01:09:21,312
[Meera sighs]

1081
01:09:23,229 --> 01:09:24,646
[unsettling music]

1082
01:09:26,146 --> 01:09:27,312
[intense music]

1083
01:09:28,146 --> 01:09:31,479
[Jomon] So I must prey on guys
like you, Rajeevan!

1084
01:09:31,979 --> 01:09:34,854
Because those further up the chain
are constantly feeding on me.

1085
01:09:35,354 --> 01:09:39,229
Now, you choose for yourself...
who becomes your prey next?

1086
01:09:39,354 --> 01:09:40,854
Hey! You may leave.

1087
01:09:46,396 --> 01:09:47,771
[music fades out]

1088
01:09:53,104 --> 01:09:54,521
I've had this with me for a while.

1089
01:09:56,146 --> 01:09:58,021
I delayed it on purpose.

1090
01:10:00,646 --> 01:10:02,104
Let's get divorced, Rajeevan.

1091
01:10:03,771 --> 01:10:05,312
If we keep dragging this out,

1092
01:10:05,937 --> 01:10:09,646
neither of us will have time
to start over again.

1093
01:10:16,771 --> 01:10:19,021
What change are we waiting for
by delaying this anyway?

1094
01:10:20,271 --> 01:10:22,311
I spent so long trying to fix you,

1095
01:10:22,312 --> 01:10:23,686
just like you tried to fix me.

1096
01:10:23,687 --> 01:10:24,854
Look where that got us.

1097
01:10:25,479 --> 01:10:27,812
There's no point going
on like this, Rajeevan.

1098
01:10:28,021 --> 01:10:31,853
Why live like this,
trapped in blame and forced adjustments?

1099
01:10:31,854 --> 01:10:33,729
I can't bear this pressure
anymore, Rajeevan!

1100
01:10:34,187 --> 01:10:36,146
I just want some peace
for me and my children.

1101
01:10:36,854 --> 01:10:40,562
[highly dramatic operatic score]

1102
01:10:45,062 --> 01:10:47,396
[sweeping, intense operatic score]

1103
01:11:09,729 --> 01:11:11,437
[flower vase shatters]

1104
01:11:25,729 --> 01:11:28,521
[emotional score]

1105
01:11:51,812 --> 01:11:52,812
You can give it inside.

1106
01:11:54,229 --> 01:11:55,396
Hey, Anas!

1107
01:11:55,896 --> 01:11:57,978
Man, it's been ages!
Where are you these days?

1108
01:11:57,979 --> 01:11:59,437
- I'm still around.
- Right.

1109
01:12:00,812 --> 01:12:01,812
You alright, man?

1110
01:12:02,521 --> 01:12:03,311
Is s... sir here?

1111
01:12:03,312 --> 01:12:05,436
He was just here.
He just stepped out.

1112
01:12:05,437 --> 01:12:06,103
Where to?

1113
01:12:06,104 --> 01:12:08,061
Some guy broke open
a temple donation box.

1114
01:12:08,062 --> 01:12:09,645
Just wait inside.
He will be back soon.

1115
01:12:09,646 --> 01:12:11,062
W... Where exactly
did this happen?

1116
01:12:13,146 --> 01:12:14,521
Which are the temples nearby?

1117
01:12:14,646 --> 01:12:16,228
The closest is a Murugan temple.

1118
01:12:16,229 --> 01:12:17,853
The next one is two kilometres away.

1119
01:12:17,854 --> 01:12:19,436
What should I even do with you?

1120
01:12:19,437 --> 01:12:21,979
How many years has it been
since you joined the force?

1121
01:12:22,271 --> 01:12:24,646
Yet the complaints against you
just keep piling up.

1122
01:12:25,854 --> 01:12:28,311
You're still lining your pockets
with bribes, aren't you?

1123
01:12:28,312 --> 01:12:30,312
No, sir. I don't really
do that any more.

1124
01:12:31,646 --> 01:12:33,604
- What's the update?
- It's totally absurd, sir.

1125
01:12:33,937 --> 01:12:36,562
No temple or committee exists
by this name anywhere here.

1126
01:12:36,812 --> 01:12:40,062
No one even has a clue
who placed the donation box here.

1127
01:12:40,271 --> 01:12:42,311
Anyway, it's been sitting
here for a few weeks now.

1128
01:12:42,312 --> 01:12:43,979
Passers-by kept dropping
money into it too.

1129
01:12:44,437 --> 01:12:46,353
So, what are we supposed
to do about this now?

1130
01:12:46,354 --> 01:12:49,771
Should we track down the scammers who
planted the fake box to cheat the locals...

1131
01:12:49,896 --> 01:12:50,811
or...

1132
01:12:50,812 --> 01:12:52,771
catch the thieves
who robbed the box?

1133
01:12:55,354 --> 01:12:57,187
[dramatic score intensifies]

1134
01:12:59,062 --> 01:13:00,312
[bell chimes]

1135
01:13:06,521 --> 01:13:08,187
[dramatic music swells]

1136
01:13:15,729 --> 01:13:18,062
[music shifts to a revelatory tone]

1137
01:13:38,521 --> 01:13:39,521
Stop.

1138
01:13:50,604 --> 01:13:52,687
[dramatic score intensifies]

1139
01:14:06,979 --> 01:14:08,062
Anas!

1140
01:14:08,271 --> 01:14:10,353
What are you daydreaming about
in the middle of all this?

1141
01:14:10,354 --> 01:14:11,395
Sorry, sir.

1142
01:14:11,396 --> 01:14:13,436
Anas, if you cause more trouble,
I am not getting involved.

1143
01:14:13,437 --> 01:14:14,562
Is that clear?

1144
01:14:14,854 --> 01:14:17,478
No, sir. Th... There won't
be any more problems.

1145
01:14:17,479 --> 01:14:18,479
Hmm.

1146
01:14:19,479 --> 01:14:20,479
Wait...

1147
01:14:21,146 --> 01:14:22,604
Why are you
so desperate for money?

1148
01:14:24,021 --> 01:14:26,478
Isn't your salary enough
to provide for your wife and kid?

1149
01:14:26,479 --> 01:14:28,311
Didn't you marry a girl
from a wealthy family?

1150
01:14:28,312 --> 01:14:30,021
But he eloped with her, sir!

1151
01:14:30,146 --> 01:14:32,646
Now he keeps that poor girl
starving in our police quarters!

1152
01:14:33,312 --> 01:14:34,978
Doesn't she have
a couple of brothers?

1153
01:14:34,979 --> 01:14:36,311
Won't they help you out at all?

1154
01:14:36,312 --> 01:14:37,770
Oh, he's far too proud for that.

1155
01:14:37,771 --> 01:14:39,271
Asking for help is beneath him.

1156
01:14:40,437 --> 01:14:43,771
Even after marriage and a child,
her family doesn't respect him, sir.

1157
01:14:44,062 --> 01:14:46,270
He's basically stuck in limbo,
neither here nor there.

1158
01:14:46,271 --> 01:14:48,061
That's why he's this
desperate to make money,

1159
01:14:48,062 --> 01:14:49,729
even if it means taking bribes.

1160
01:14:51,854 --> 01:14:53,896
Come on, brother-in-law.
Stay and have some food.

1161
01:14:54,062 --> 01:14:55,062
Nope!

1162
01:14:56,396 --> 01:14:57,728
If he eats anything from here,

1163
01:14:57,729 --> 01:14:59,312
his ego will give him
a stomach ache.

1164
01:14:59,687 --> 01:15:00,729
- Come on.
- Let's go?

1165
01:15:25,896 --> 01:15:27,396
How many times do I
have to tell them!

1166
01:15:30,896 --> 01:15:31,896
Amala!

1167
01:15:35,896 --> 01:15:36,896
Jiya, where's Amala?

1168
01:15:37,479 --> 01:15:38,479
In Papa's room.

1169
01:15:39,979 --> 01:15:40,979
Amala!

1170
01:15:50,896 --> 01:15:52,896
[dramatic score slowly swells]

1171
01:15:58,771 --> 01:16:00,729
Uncle, I'll take this.
And this, too.

1172
01:16:01,229 --> 01:16:02,271
This one too.

1173
01:16:05,187 --> 01:16:06,896
[energetic track pulses]

1174
01:16:08,896 --> 01:16:10,062
A quarter kilo of this.

1175
01:16:17,646 --> 01:16:19,896
Uncle, half a kilo of this.

1176
01:16:20,687 --> 01:16:22,062
Uncle, this one too.

1177
01:16:22,479 --> 01:16:23,604
I'm taking this, too.

1178
01:16:24,437 --> 01:16:25,437
Yes, this one.

1179
01:16:32,646 --> 01:16:34,021
These too.

1180
01:16:42,687 --> 01:16:44,437
[Amala] Don't you have small onions?

1181
01:17:00,354 --> 01:17:01,729
[music fades out]

1182
01:17:05,187 --> 01:17:06,728
What? Prices went up again?

1183
01:17:06,729 --> 01:17:09,604
At this rate, how are ordinary
people going to survive?

1184
01:17:11,021 --> 01:17:12,061
Now give me my change.

1185
01:17:12,062 --> 01:17:13,062
Mumma!

1186
01:17:13,271 --> 01:17:14,437
Is this real?

1187
01:17:17,521 --> 01:17:19,562
I was playing "Mommy and baby."

1188
01:17:34,687 --> 01:17:36,521
[dramatic music plays]

1189
01:17:45,271 --> 01:17:46,979
This is where I found it.

1190
01:17:47,812 --> 01:17:49,603
Did Papa actually commit
the robbery, Mumma?

1191
01:17:49,604 --> 01:17:51,896
No! Papa just happened
to find it by accident.

1192
01:17:58,896 --> 01:17:59,979
[doorbell rings]

1193
01:18:01,479 --> 01:18:03,479
Oh shit! Is that the police, Mumma?

1194
01:18:19,562 --> 01:18:20,895
- Yeah.
- Dear...

1195
01:18:20,896 --> 01:18:22,854
Is it possible to clear
the newspaper bill now?

1196
01:18:23,229 --> 01:18:24,604
Err... Yes.

1197
01:18:24,729 --> 01:18:25,937
- I'll go get it.
- Okay.

1198
01:18:35,937 --> 01:18:38,354
[unsettling music]

1199
01:18:49,854 --> 01:18:52,229
Do you think that uncle
got suspicious, Mumma?

1200
01:18:52,396 --> 01:18:53,478
Will you keep quiet?

1201
01:18:53,479 --> 01:18:54,770
[Amala] How much is it, Uncle?

1202
01:18:54,771 --> 01:18:56,478
[music swells with rising tension]

1203
01:18:56,479 --> 01:18:58,646
[Amala] What? Prices went up again?

1204
01:19:04,479 --> 01:19:06,021
Make sure you give me
my change, okay?

1205
01:19:09,021 --> 01:19:11,187
Wait, those are fake!
It's only toy paper.

1206
01:19:11,896 --> 01:19:14,312
Her papa bought it
for her to play with.

1207
01:19:16,354 --> 01:19:17,562
I understand, dear.

1208
01:19:17,896 --> 01:19:19,937
Who would ever let a kid
play with actual money?

1209
01:19:23,479 --> 01:19:24,479
Bye.

1210
01:19:30,229 --> 01:19:32,646
[shrill, unsettling score plays]

1211
01:19:45,937 --> 01:19:48,729
[insightful, slow-tempo score plays]

1212
01:19:58,354 --> 01:20:00,396
[score quickens in tempo]

1213
01:20:01,979 --> 01:20:04,229
[elevator doors opening]

1214
01:20:15,479 --> 01:20:16,812
[music fades out]

1215
01:20:18,312 --> 01:20:19,354
I can explain.

1216
01:20:19,729 --> 01:20:20,729
Ra--

1217
01:20:22,396 --> 01:20:24,603
Everyone was targeting me for
absolutely no reason, right?

1218
01:20:24,604 --> 01:20:25,478
Did I do anything to deserve it?

1219
01:20:25,479 --> 01:20:26,770
And is this the way you
handle it, Rajeevan?

1220
01:20:26,771 --> 01:20:28,311
This is just what
I felt like doing.

1221
01:20:28,312 --> 01:20:29,603
That's so easy for you to say!

1222
01:20:29,604 --> 01:20:31,478
You didn't think about me and
our two kids here, did you?

1223
01:20:31,479 --> 01:20:32,270
So?

1224
01:20:32,271 --> 01:20:33,936
So what, I shouldn't react
to anything?!

1225
01:20:33,937 --> 01:20:36,228
Every loser plots it out in advance
to come and mess with me, Meera!

1226
01:20:36,229 --> 01:20:38,020
- Rajeevan, you're not a--
- There's a limit to my patience!

1227
01:20:38,021 --> 01:20:39,396
You are not a teenager anymore!

1228
01:20:40,896 --> 01:20:42,479
You should think
these things through.

1229
01:20:42,687 --> 01:20:44,103
If you keep reacting to
every little thing like this...

1230
01:20:44,104 --> 01:20:46,104
Little thing?!
Really? Again?

1231
01:20:46,312 --> 01:20:47,603
As always, none of my
issues matter to you!

1232
01:20:47,604 --> 01:20:49,061
Then tell me what a big deal is!

1233
01:20:49,062 --> 01:20:50,561
My family! My kids!

1234
01:20:50,562 --> 01:20:51,978
That's my big deal!

1235
01:20:51,979 --> 01:20:53,186
- Okay?!
- There you go again!

1236
01:20:53,187 --> 01:20:54,729
As if I'm not
concerned about them!

1237
01:20:55,604 --> 01:20:57,187
[footsteps receding]

1238
01:20:58,062 --> 01:21:00,354
You can't fix the things you destroy,
can you, Rajeevan?

1239
01:21:04,937 --> 01:21:06,646
[faint, emotional score]

1240
01:21:10,312 --> 01:21:12,270
[Jomon] But there's
one difference here.

1241
01:21:12,271 --> 01:21:14,562
To survive in this
societal food chain,

1242
01:21:14,729 --> 01:21:16,896
a grasshopper cannot
survive on grass alone.

1243
01:21:17,271 --> 01:21:18,645
It has to consume the frog too.

1244
01:21:18,646 --> 01:21:20,936
♪ The wolves are circling ♪

1245
01:21:20,937 --> 01:21:24,229
So I must feed on the brains
of guys like you, Rajeevan!

1246
01:21:24,979 --> 01:21:27,561
Because those further up the chain
are constantly eating my head.

1247
01:21:27,562 --> 01:21:30,311
♪ I'm crying out ♪

1248
01:21:30,312 --> 01:21:33,686
Now, you choose for yourself...
whose heads will you eat next?

1249
01:21:33,687 --> 01:21:36,062
♪ But nobody's listenin' ♪

1250
01:21:38,562 --> 01:21:41,854
♪ The fools and cruel ♪

1251
01:21:42,896 --> 01:21:46,771
♪ They swallow you whole ♪

1252
01:21:49,187 --> 01:21:54,895
♪ With a smile on their faces ♪

1253
01:21:54,896 --> 01:21:59,895
♪ Taste their pride ♪

1254
01:21:59,896 --> 01:22:02,854
♪ Put on the circus ♪

1255
01:22:04,104 --> 01:22:08,979
♪ It's nobody's game here ♪

1256
01:22:09,854 --> 01:22:14,854
♪ So I'll put on my show ♪

1257
01:22:15,604 --> 01:22:20,187
♪ Look out for my Kingdom come now ♪

1258
01:22:44,062 --> 01:22:46,229
♪ Tell me what is real? ♪

1259
01:22:47,271 --> 01:22:49,603
♪ They carve their greed into your soul ♪

1260
01:22:49,604 --> 01:22:51,604
♪ Tell me what is real? ♪

1261
01:22:52,562 --> 01:22:54,645
♪ The puppets you control ♪

1262
01:22:54,646 --> 01:22:58,187
♪ Tell me who is here? ♪

1263
01:22:59,229 --> 01:23:05,521
♪ We're burning our own kingdoms
to the ground ♪

1264
01:23:06,146 --> 01:23:07,771
[lock breaks open]

1265
01:23:12,062 --> 01:23:15,021
♪ Put on the circus ♪

1266
01:23:16,146 --> 01:23:21,021
♪ It's nobody's game here ♪

1267
01:23:22,104 --> 01:23:26,854
♪ So I'll put on my show ♪

1268
01:23:27,771 --> 01:23:32,354
♪ Look out for my Kingdom come now ♪

1269
01:23:33,479 --> 01:23:36,437
♪ Put on the circus ♪

1270
01:23:37,604 --> 01:23:42,479
♪ It's nobody's game here ♪

1271
01:23:43,479 --> 01:23:48,479
♪ So I'll put on my show ♪

1272
01:23:49,062 --> 01:23:53,729
♪ Look out for my Kingdom come now ♪

1273
01:23:54,854 --> 01:23:57,062
♪ Tell me what is real? ♪

1274
01:23:58,187 --> 01:24:00,478
♪ They carve their greed into your soul ♪

1275
01:24:00,479 --> 01:24:03,229
♪ Tell me what is real? ♪

1276
01:24:03,396 --> 01:24:05,436
♪ The puppets you control ♪

1277
01:24:05,437 --> 01:24:08,687
♪ Tell me who is here? ♪

1278
01:24:09,979 --> 01:24:15,771
♪ We're burning our own kingdoms
to the ground ♪

1279
01:24:16,062 --> 01:24:19,062
♪ Put on the circus ♪

1280
01:24:20,187 --> 01:24:25,062
♪ It's nobody's game here ♪

1281
01:24:26,021 --> 01:24:31,062
♪ So I'll put on my show ♪

1282
01:24:31,729 --> 01:24:36,312
♪ Look out for my Kingdom come now ♪

1283
01:24:37,062 --> 01:24:41,604
♪ Look out for my Kingdom come now ♪

1284
01:24:41,812 --> 01:24:43,271
[intriguing music]

1285
01:24:50,896 --> 01:24:52,271
It's not like that at all, bro.

1286
01:24:52,437 --> 01:24:55,228
Rajeevan just knew where those
guys had stashed the stolen money.

1287
01:24:55,229 --> 01:24:57,145
The moment he got a chance,
he went and grabbed it.

1288
01:24:57,146 --> 01:24:57,978
That's all.

1289
01:24:57,979 --> 01:25:01,771
He's not the dangerous criminal
the media is making him out to be!

1290
01:25:02,229 --> 01:25:04,687
But bro... isn't this a case
the police are investigating?

1291
01:25:05,271 --> 01:25:06,770
Won't we end up getting
into trouble for this?

1292
01:25:06,771 --> 01:25:08,062
What trouble?

1293
01:25:08,187 --> 01:25:10,729
Anyway, how far are they really
g... going to get with it, bro?

1294
01:25:10,979 --> 01:25:12,061
I mean,

1295
01:25:12,062 --> 01:25:14,603
a case only stands if they
actually catch the robbers!

1296
01:25:14,604 --> 01:25:15,811
Or if they find the loot.

1297
01:25:15,812 --> 01:25:20,811
In five or six years, this will
just be a true crime episode on TV!

1298
01:25:20,812 --> 01:25:21,979
Nothing more...

1299
01:25:24,062 --> 01:25:25,062
Brother.

1300
01:25:26,604 --> 01:25:28,229
I only came to you

1301
01:25:28,479 --> 01:25:32,353
because I wanted my own people to get
a cut when the money gets divided.

1302
01:25:32,354 --> 01:25:33,728
If I wanted to look elsewhere,

1303
01:25:33,729 --> 01:25:36,229
I'd have a h... hundred people
lining up to back me on this.

1304
01:25:36,479 --> 01:25:37,479
Don't you think so?

1305
01:25:38,854 --> 01:25:40,521
Why would you need a hundred guys?

1306
01:25:41,562 --> 01:25:42,562
We've got your back, bro.

1307
01:25:44,396 --> 01:25:46,812
By the way... how much cash
does he have on him altogether?

1308
01:25:48,396 --> 01:25:50,687
[music slowly builds in intensity]

1309
01:26:32,062 --> 01:26:34,854
What he's going to do
with all that money

1310
01:26:35,187 --> 01:26:36,271
is a complete mystery.

1311
01:26:37,062 --> 01:26:38,437
But I'll tell you this much.

1312
01:26:39,312 --> 01:26:42,312
It's not like he's just going
to hand it over.

1313
01:26:43,312 --> 01:26:45,271
We're really going to have
to sweat for this one.

1314
01:26:45,854 --> 01:26:47,562
[powerful score swells]

1315
01:26:57,312 --> 01:27:00,062
[phone rings]

1316
01:27:02,062 --> 01:27:03,062
Hello.

1317
01:27:03,604 --> 01:27:05,229
- Hello, who is this?
- Sir.

1318
01:27:06,604 --> 01:27:08,354
We actually see each other
almost every day.

1319
01:27:08,771 --> 01:27:11,645
But... you wouldn't recognise me
even if I told you my name.

1320
01:27:11,646 --> 01:27:12,936
Then don't bother. Get lost.

1321
01:27:12,937 --> 01:27:14,479
I know you have that money, sir.

1322
01:27:22,437 --> 01:27:23,686
What money?

1323
01:27:23,687 --> 01:27:25,312
The money stolen
from Vanchiyoor Bank.

1324
01:27:25,521 --> 01:27:26,604
Who told you that?

1325
01:27:27,062 --> 01:27:30,728
Don't waste my time late at night with
whatever nonsense you read on WhatsApp...

1326
01:27:30,729 --> 01:27:32,312
No! I saw it earlier
with my own eyes.

1327
01:27:33,021 --> 01:27:34,396
That cash is sitting right
inside your apartment, sir.

1328
01:27:35,729 --> 01:27:38,562
I don't know if it's proper
to demand a share of stolen money.

1329
01:27:39,812 --> 01:27:41,603
But times are tough for
everyone, right sir?

1330
01:27:41,604 --> 01:27:43,478
You need to give me
a share of that money, sir.

1331
01:27:43,479 --> 01:27:44,479
Of course, why not?

1332
01:27:45,187 --> 01:27:46,187
I'd be glad to.

1333
01:27:46,771 --> 01:27:47,896
How much do you need, sir?

1334
01:27:49,771 --> 01:27:51,187
I need 70 lakhs, sir.

1335
01:27:51,646 --> 01:27:54,396
Who the hell are you?
How do you people even get my number?

1336
01:27:55,062 --> 01:27:57,812
As of now, I don't know what
I'll do if you don't pay up.

1337
01:27:58,646 --> 01:28:00,854
I know I can't exactly
take it from you by force.

1338
01:28:01,396 --> 01:28:02,561
But believe me, sir...

1339
01:28:02,562 --> 01:28:04,061
I'll have to do whatever I can.

1340
01:28:04,062 --> 01:28:05,604
Wait, are you calling to--

1341
01:28:06,187 --> 01:28:07,187
Hello?

1342
01:28:08,229 --> 01:28:09,937
[music gradually swells]

1343
01:28:20,521 --> 01:28:21,521
[music stops]

1344
01:28:22,062 --> 01:28:23,437
For the time being,

1345
01:28:24,312 --> 01:28:25,604
let's just move into a PG.

1346
01:28:26,229 --> 01:28:27,229
Hmm.

1347
01:28:28,062 --> 01:28:29,562
I've already found a place.

1348
01:28:31,521 --> 01:28:32,979
It's only a single room, though.

1349
01:28:34,146 --> 01:28:35,936
The three of us will have
to manage somehow, okay?

1350
01:28:35,937 --> 01:28:37,020
Mm.

1351
01:28:37,021 --> 01:28:38,687
Tomorrow morning around eleven,

1352
01:28:38,896 --> 01:28:40,062
I'll come to your school.

1353
01:28:41,812 --> 01:28:43,854
I'll make up some excuse
for the school authorities.

1354
01:28:44,312 --> 01:28:45,354
Mm.

1355
01:28:46,062 --> 01:28:48,021
We must shift out of here
before noon.

1356
01:28:50,562 --> 01:28:52,853
Until then, don't tell Amala
anything about this, alright?

1357
01:28:52,854 --> 01:28:53,854
Okay.

1358
01:28:53,979 --> 01:28:55,979
[emotional score]

1359
01:29:04,021 --> 01:29:05,311
A bit late today, Mr. Jacob?

1360
01:29:05,312 --> 01:29:07,436
Yeah, had some extra work today.
Just wrapped it up.

1361
01:29:07,437 --> 01:29:08,771
Bro, give me a cigarette.

1362
01:29:11,771 --> 01:29:14,061
- Are you open all night?
- No, closing in ten minutes.

1363
01:29:14,062 --> 01:29:15,062
Oh, really?

1364
01:29:15,187 --> 01:29:17,021
In that case, give
me two full packs.

1365
01:29:17,396 --> 01:29:18,437
- Two?
- Yeah.

1366
01:29:20,479 --> 01:29:22,436
- That'll be 358.
- How much?

1367
01:29:22,437 --> 01:29:23,437
358 rupees.

1368
01:29:25,562 --> 01:29:26,895
- I've paid it.
- Okay, okay.

1369
01:29:26,896 --> 01:29:28,354
[intriguing music]

1370
01:29:42,729 --> 01:29:43,896
[doorbell rings]

1371
01:29:58,479 --> 01:29:59,479
Sir!

1372
01:29:59,771 --> 01:30:01,562
I noticed a few
suspicious guys downstairs.

1373
01:30:01,687 --> 01:30:02,687
Sitting inside a car.

1374
01:30:02,812 --> 01:30:04,396
[sound of bike]

1375
01:30:04,729 --> 01:30:06,729
I think they're after you, sir.

1376
01:30:09,062 --> 01:30:10,729
Please stay safe up here.

1377
01:30:11,062 --> 01:30:12,229
I'll keep watch downstairs.

1378
01:30:24,896 --> 01:30:26,562
[music slowly builds]

1379
01:30:57,062 --> 01:30:58,312
Where are they?

1380
01:30:59,062 --> 01:31:00,729
Sir! Sir!

1381
01:31:04,937 --> 01:31:06,062
That's not gonna work, man.

1382
01:31:07,687 --> 01:31:10,271
Look, it's a solid plan.
Take it or leave it.

1383
01:31:10,771 --> 01:31:12,021
Isn't that him, Ajas?

1384
01:31:12,271 --> 01:31:13,271
Who?

1385
01:31:14,271 --> 01:31:15,812
The guy we're staking out.

1386
01:31:21,021 --> 01:31:22,062
- Start the car.
- Huh?

1387
01:31:22,562 --> 01:31:23,728
Turn the engine on!

1388
01:31:23,729 --> 01:31:25,061
- Move it!
- Bro, it's not starting!

1389
01:31:25,062 --> 01:31:27,103
- Shift to P and step on it!
- It's not kicking in!

1390
01:31:27,104 --> 01:31:28,895
Just slam it into Park and start it!

1391
01:31:28,896 --> 01:31:30,521
- Why the hell won't it start?!
- MOVE IT!

1392
01:31:34,479 --> 01:31:35,646
Bro, run!

1393
01:31:42,021 --> 01:31:43,729
[intense music swells]

1394
01:31:50,937 --> 01:31:51,937
[car starts]

1395
01:31:52,062 --> 01:31:53,437
Hey! Let's go!
Move it!

1396
01:32:01,479 --> 01:32:02,812
[music fades out]

1397
01:32:07,604 --> 01:32:08,646
[eerie music]

1398
01:32:11,021 --> 01:32:12,021
What's your name?

1399
01:32:12,479 --> 01:32:13,479
Jacob.

1400
01:32:17,562 --> 01:32:18,604
What would you do, Jacob?

1401
01:32:19,062 --> 01:32:20,062
What, sir?

1402
01:32:21,812 --> 01:32:24,562
That 17 crore loot stolen
from the Vanchiyoor bank...

1403
01:32:25,646 --> 01:32:27,229
If you suspect
I have it with me,

1404
01:32:27,479 --> 01:32:28,978
what will you do, Jacob?

1405
01:32:28,979 --> 01:32:30,271
So you actually have it, sir.

1406
01:32:31,437 --> 01:32:32,479
And what if I do?

1407
01:32:32,937 --> 01:32:34,062
What can I even do, sir?

1408
01:32:35,437 --> 01:32:36,646
I'd probably go to the police.

1409
01:32:38,604 --> 01:32:39,604
You won't do that.

1410
01:32:39,854 --> 01:32:41,062
What would you
even gain from it?

1411
01:32:42,312 --> 01:32:43,437
So instead, maybe you'll...

1412
01:32:44,479 --> 01:32:46,187
call me up
and try to threaten me.

1413
01:32:46,521 --> 01:32:47,521
Right?

1414
01:32:49,896 --> 01:32:52,062
But do you think I'll just
hand you the cash right away?

1415
01:32:53,979 --> 01:32:54,979
No.

1416
01:32:55,521 --> 01:32:57,311
I've survived
much worse than that.

1417
01:32:57,312 --> 01:32:58,604
What will you do then, Jacob?

1418
01:32:59,062 --> 01:33:00,396
What else can I do, sir?

1419
01:33:00,812 --> 01:33:02,312
It's not like I can fight you.

1420
01:33:02,437 --> 01:33:05,061
I'll just think luck is on your side
and go about my own business.

1421
01:33:05,062 --> 01:33:06,604
So, you don't want the money?

1422
01:33:07,771 --> 01:33:08,771
Those seventy lakhs?

1423
01:33:14,396 --> 01:33:16,979
Some random people are coming there,
looking for him, Molly.

1424
01:33:17,646 --> 01:33:20,729
I saw a whole bunch of them
at the flat earlier today.

1425
01:33:23,771 --> 01:33:26,062
As for Rajeevan sir,
he is completely shaken up.

1426
01:33:29,062 --> 01:33:30,771
One threatening phone call...

1427
01:33:31,771 --> 01:33:33,437
and he'll cave in and part
with the cash.

1428
01:33:34,646 --> 01:33:36,978
You already tried calling and
threatening him, didn't you?

1429
01:33:36,979 --> 01:33:38,437
And did he give you
a single cent?

1430
01:33:40,396 --> 01:33:41,771
This time is different, Moly!

1431
01:33:42,062 --> 01:33:43,229
This time, he'll pay up.

1432
01:33:45,354 --> 01:33:46,603
Oh, really?

1433
01:33:46,604 --> 01:33:47,604
Different how?

1434
01:33:48,812 --> 01:33:49,812
Listen, Molly...

1435
01:33:50,062 --> 01:33:51,854
[intense music builds]

1436
01:34:05,062 --> 01:34:07,062
[Jacob] This plan of yours
is way too extreme, sir.

1437
01:34:09,021 --> 01:34:11,021
The mess I'm in
is far worse, Jacob.

1438
01:34:12,979 --> 01:34:14,437
So, sir... you really think

1439
01:34:15,562 --> 01:34:17,271
the men who are
after the money...

1440
01:34:17,521 --> 01:34:19,062
are going to target
your children?

1441
01:34:34,812 --> 01:34:35,812
So,

1442
01:34:35,937 --> 01:34:37,562
as per our plan...

1443
01:34:38,479 --> 01:34:40,479
I'll kidnap your daughter.

1444
01:34:42,062 --> 01:34:43,187
Okay.

1445
01:34:43,354 --> 01:34:44,520
And then what?

1446
01:34:44,521 --> 01:34:45,646
Then the police will arrive.

1447
01:34:48,312 --> 01:34:50,271
The media will show up,
the neighbourhood too.

1448
01:34:54,896 --> 01:34:56,896
A few of them will inevitably
start digging into my history.

1449
01:34:57,021 --> 01:34:59,229
And they'll say this
whole ordeal is my fault.

1450
01:35:01,521 --> 01:35:04,646
In the middle of all that chaos, you need
to call me from a fake number, Jacob.

1451
01:35:06,854 --> 01:35:08,062
[Jacob] I know the rest, sir.

1452
01:35:08,771 --> 01:35:11,687
Your daughter will be home
tomorrow evening. Perfectly safe.

1453
01:35:12,396 --> 01:35:14,521
So, to the guys hunting you down,

1454
01:35:15,062 --> 01:35:18,021
it will look like you paid
that cash to save your kid.

1455
01:35:18,771 --> 01:35:19,771
Right?

1456
01:35:21,062 --> 01:35:22,312
That's one way to look at it.

1457
01:35:24,062 --> 01:35:26,062
Once that money
leaves your hands,

1458
01:35:26,604 --> 01:35:27,979
who will even want you?

1459
01:35:32,354 --> 01:35:34,062
[mysterious music]

1460
01:36:08,479 --> 01:36:12,729
[rhythmic ticking]

1461
01:36:31,354 --> 01:36:33,937
[score intensifies
with rising tension]

1462
01:36:51,771 --> 01:36:53,436
Excuse me!
Where are my kids?

1463
01:36:53,437 --> 01:36:54,770
School got let out
early today, madam.

1464
01:36:54,771 --> 01:36:57,353
Some lunatic called and said
there's a bomb in the building.

1465
01:36:57,354 --> 01:36:59,936
On top of that, they found
a dead snake in a classroom.

1466
01:36:59,937 --> 01:37:02,062
All the kids were already
sent home on the school bus.

1467
01:37:03,187 --> 01:37:04,061
Hello?

1468
01:37:04,062 --> 01:37:06,353
Hello, this is the Sub-Inspector
from Vanchiyoor station.

1469
01:37:06,354 --> 01:37:08,646
Can you head over to your flat
immediately, madam?

1470
01:37:08,896 --> 01:37:10,187
This isn't a request.
You must come right now.

1471
01:37:13,604 --> 01:37:15,271
[distant traffic sounds]

1472
01:37:30,937 --> 01:37:33,895
Sir, do you know how many times
the cops have come here for Rajeevan?

1473
01:37:33,896 --> 01:37:36,646
Respectable families live here.
Imagine the nuisance of all this.

1474
01:37:39,271 --> 01:37:41,395
[indistinct chatter]

1475
01:37:41,396 --> 01:37:43,187
Sir, what's going on?
What's the issue?

1476
01:37:43,687 --> 01:37:45,271
Have you spoken
to Rajeevan, Meera?

1477
01:37:47,062 --> 01:37:49,062
I tried calling him,
but he didn't answer.

1478
01:37:50,604 --> 01:37:52,021
- What happened, sir?
- Okay.

1479
01:37:52,479 --> 01:37:53,812
Have a seat, Meera.
I'll explain.

1480
01:37:54,729 --> 01:37:56,853
Sir, no matter what it is,

1481
01:37:56,854 --> 01:37:58,145
my kids and I...

1482
01:37:58,146 --> 01:37:59,521
we don't know anything about it.

1483
01:38:00,062 --> 01:38:01,687
We're not involved, sir.
Where's Jiya?

1484
01:38:03,646 --> 01:38:04,646
Jiya!

1485
01:38:06,896 --> 01:38:07,896
Jiya!

1486
01:38:08,396 --> 01:38:10,021
Amala, where's Jiya?

1487
01:38:12,271 --> 01:38:16,311
We have a major update reaching us
from Vellayani, Thiruvananthapuram.

1488
01:38:16,312 --> 01:38:19,436
A young schoolgirl has reportedly
been kidnapped on her way home.

1489
01:38:19,437 --> 01:38:21,520
A gang in a car intercepted her
and sped away.

1490
01:38:21,521 --> 01:38:23,561
The police investigation has
established one clear detail.

1491
01:38:23,562 --> 01:38:27,061
Eyewitnesses report seeing
two people inside that vehicle.

1492
01:38:27,062 --> 01:38:31,020
We hope to bring you news
of her safe rescue very soon.

1493
01:38:31,021 --> 01:38:34,062
Police are currently interrogating
everyone in person right now.

1494
01:38:34,604 --> 01:38:36,312
[dramatic music builds]

1495
01:38:44,979 --> 01:38:47,396
Wouldn't you cry
in a situation like that, dear?

1496
01:38:48,062 --> 01:38:49,270
Wouldn't you scream for help?

1497
01:38:49,271 --> 01:38:51,478
But you just walked home
as if nothing had happened.

1498
01:38:51,479 --> 01:38:53,104
And you've kept quiet
this entire time.

1499
01:38:54,396 --> 01:38:55,937
Why did you do that, sweetie?

1500
01:38:56,604 --> 01:38:58,687
It was your older sister
who got kidnapped, right?

1501
01:38:58,812 --> 01:39:00,479
Why didn't you tell
anybody about it?

1502
01:39:00,937 --> 01:39:01,937
Huh?

1503
01:39:02,062 --> 01:39:05,062
I thought he was
a friend of Papa's.

1504
01:39:06,812 --> 01:39:07,854
A friend of Papa's?

1505
01:39:08,437 --> 01:39:09,479
Which friend?

1506
01:39:10,062 --> 01:39:11,437
I don't know.

1507
01:39:14,062 --> 01:39:16,021
Then what made you
think that, dear?

1508
01:39:18,437 --> 01:39:19,478
Well...

1509
01:39:19,479 --> 01:39:22,312
Papa didn't mention
which friend it would be. Right?

1510
01:39:22,687 --> 01:39:23,687
Yeah.

1511
01:39:25,562 --> 01:39:27,062
What else did... did Papa say?

1512
01:39:27,937 --> 01:39:30,021
Papa told me that...

1513
01:39:31,062 --> 01:39:33,354
this is all a game.

1514
01:39:33,646 --> 01:39:34,646
What kind of game?

1515
01:39:35,229 --> 01:39:36,646
I don't know that.

1516
01:39:38,187 --> 01:39:39,270
So...

1517
01:39:39,271 --> 01:39:42,062
did Papa tell you Jiya
was going to be kidnapped?

1518
01:39:42,812 --> 01:39:44,895
Kidnap?
No, Papa didn't say that.

1519
01:39:44,896 --> 01:39:45,937
Seriously, sir!?

1520
01:39:46,937 --> 01:39:48,270
She's just turning five.

1521
01:39:48,271 --> 01:39:50,436
Are you trying to find Jiya
by questioning a toddler?!

1522
01:39:50,437 --> 01:39:51,979
Why are you making them confused?

1523
01:39:52,229 --> 01:39:54,311
You think this is some
game you play with Papa?!

1524
01:39:54,312 --> 01:39:56,896
Mumma... may I go to toilet?

1525
01:40:07,396 --> 01:40:09,062
What the hell are you
and your father up to?

1526
01:40:09,229 --> 01:40:10,687
Amala, tell me where Jiya is!

1527
01:40:11,396 --> 01:40:13,854
Jiya is with a friend of Papa's.

1528
01:40:14,771 --> 01:40:15,896
Damn your papa...

1529
01:40:16,396 --> 01:40:17,771
Tell me the rest
of it right now!

1530
01:40:17,937 --> 01:40:20,145
I'm feeling sleepy, Papa...

1531
01:40:20,146 --> 01:40:22,479
Can we do this tomorrow?

1532
01:40:23,021 --> 01:40:24,062
Just once.

1533
01:40:24,229 --> 01:40:25,229
Just one more time.

1534
01:40:25,604 --> 01:40:26,896
After that, you can go to sleep.

1535
01:40:27,312 --> 01:40:28,312
Hmm.

1536
01:40:28,521 --> 01:40:29,521
So...

1537
01:40:29,646 --> 01:40:31,521
tomorrow, on your way back
from school...

1538
01:40:32,062 --> 01:40:33,062
an uncle...

1539
01:40:33,187 --> 01:40:35,312
will pull up in a car
and take you inside.

1540
01:40:36,271 --> 01:40:37,603
You must go with him,

1541
01:40:37,604 --> 01:40:39,229
do exactly what he says,

1542
01:40:39,521 --> 01:40:41,103
and wait at his house
for a little bit.

1543
01:40:41,104 --> 01:40:42,104
That's the game.

1544
01:40:42,521 --> 01:40:44,021
Which uncle is it?

1545
01:40:44,521 --> 01:40:45,645
Well, that uncle...

1546
01:40:45,646 --> 01:40:47,561
You don't know him.
He's Papa's friend.

1547
01:40:47,562 --> 01:40:48,896
Is Jiya playing the game too?

1548
01:40:49,771 --> 01:40:51,145
Jiya isn't part of this game.

1549
01:40:51,146 --> 01:40:52,396
What kind of game is it then?

1550
01:40:52,854 --> 01:40:54,312
I don't like it.

1551
01:40:56,521 --> 01:40:58,437
Guess what the prize is
once the game is over.

1552
01:41:00,312 --> 01:41:01,437
A bicycle!

1553
01:41:03,062 --> 01:41:04,396
PlayStation.

1554
01:41:06,687 --> 01:41:07,687
A bicycle!

1555
01:41:08,354 --> 01:41:09,854
PlayStation.

1556
01:41:10,687 --> 01:41:11,729
Bicycle!

1557
01:41:12,021 --> 01:41:14,187
Then I'm not playing this game.

1558
01:41:17,437 --> 01:41:18,646
Fine, you get a PlayStation.

1559
01:41:19,437 --> 01:41:20,437
Okay.

1560
01:41:26,062 --> 01:41:28,062
This whole thing
smells fishy, Jomon!

1561
01:41:28,521 --> 01:41:29,603
Sir...

1562
01:41:29,604 --> 01:41:33,229
the two of them have actually filed
for divorce in Vanchiyoor Court.

1563
01:41:34,271 --> 01:41:35,646
I suspected as much.

1564
01:41:36,062 --> 01:41:37,562
Wasn't she the one
having an affair?

1565
01:41:38,979 --> 01:41:40,354
I can't understand
any of this...

1566
01:41:45,521 --> 01:41:46,604
Rajeevan.

1567
01:41:46,812 --> 01:41:47,854
Where is Jiya?

1568
01:41:50,021 --> 01:41:51,062
Did you hear what I asked?!

1569
01:41:51,437 --> 01:41:53,562
- Where's Jiya?!
- Meera, our daughter is safe.

1570
01:41:55,062 --> 01:41:57,062
Then put her on the phone.
I need to speak to her.

1571
01:41:57,437 --> 01:41:59,395
Trust me, Meera.
She is perfectly okay.

1572
01:41:59,396 --> 01:42:00,811
- Rajeevan, stop playing games.
- I'll bring her back home...

1573
01:42:00,812 --> 01:42:01,812
Let me talk to her!

1574
01:42:02,437 --> 01:42:03,478
I...

1575
01:42:03,479 --> 01:42:04,771
I made a single mistake.

1576
01:42:05,187 --> 01:42:06,478
And I'll fix it myself.

1577
01:42:06,479 --> 01:42:08,437
- But I need some time.
- How exactly are you going to fix it?

1578
01:42:08,646 --> 01:42:10,061
This mistake of yours?

1579
01:42:10,062 --> 01:42:12,062
Every single cop here
has already figured it out.

1580
01:42:13,437 --> 01:42:14,436
What will you do now?

1581
01:42:14,437 --> 01:42:16,229
Your darling daughter
told them everything herself.

1582
01:42:17,271 --> 01:42:18,395
Can you hear me?!

1583
01:42:18,396 --> 01:42:19,437
- Sir?
- Hmm?

1584
01:42:19,687 --> 01:42:20,854
I have a feeling...

1585
01:42:21,062 --> 01:42:24,229
they've been fighting
over the children, sir.

1586
01:42:24,854 --> 01:42:27,896
After the divorce, Rajeevan won't get
custody of the kids, right?

1587
01:42:28,687 --> 01:42:30,603
Given the kind of man he is,

1588
01:42:30,604 --> 01:42:33,854
he must have kidnapped
the older girl himself.

1589
01:42:34,812 --> 01:42:37,187
That's why the mother
and kid are acting fishy.

1590
01:42:38,062 --> 01:42:39,353
That's a possibility, sir.

1591
01:42:39,354 --> 01:42:40,896
Did you try contacting Rajeevan?

1592
01:42:41,437 --> 01:42:42,978
We tried multiple times.

1593
01:42:42,979 --> 01:42:44,604
But he isn't answering.

1594
01:42:45,479 --> 01:42:47,562
Sir, Rajeevan went
to work this morning.

1595
01:42:47,896 --> 01:42:49,771
And I heard he slipped
away from his desk later.

1596
01:42:50,937 --> 01:42:52,646
Trace Rajeevan first.

1597
01:42:52,896 --> 01:42:54,646
Inform everyone in our circle.

1598
01:42:55,312 --> 01:42:57,311
- Okay, sir!
- That's all for now.

1599
01:42:57,312 --> 01:43:00,062
Let's figure out first if this
is just a domestic issue or not.

1600
01:43:00,646 --> 01:43:01,687
Sir.

1601
01:43:02,021 --> 01:43:03,021
Hey!

1602
01:43:04,562 --> 01:43:05,562
What's your name?

1603
01:43:07,187 --> 01:43:08,271
Huh?

1604
01:43:08,854 --> 01:43:09,770
Anas.

1605
01:43:09,771 --> 01:43:11,979
Easy for you to say!
You can just go to jail!

1606
01:43:12,187 --> 01:43:13,436
My children and I...

1607
01:43:13,437 --> 01:43:15,604
Forget about me!
You've never bothered about that.

1608
01:43:15,854 --> 01:43:18,686
The children's safety! Their future!
Couldn't you think of that?!

1609
01:43:18,687 --> 01:43:20,354
That's exactly why I--

1610
01:43:22,479 --> 01:43:24,061
No matter what happens,
I'll handle it. Okay?

1611
01:43:24,062 --> 01:43:26,021
How? How exactly are
you going to handle this?

1612
01:43:26,229 --> 01:43:28,354
- You just rush into things!
- Meera, didn't I tell you?

1613
01:43:28,729 --> 01:43:31,062
I will bring her back.
Just... trust me.

1614
01:43:32,062 --> 01:43:33,062
"Trust me!"

1615
01:43:47,979 --> 01:43:49,521
[score intensifies]

1616
01:43:53,896 --> 01:43:55,729
[indistinct chatter]

1617
01:43:57,771 --> 01:44:00,437
[indistinct chatter]

1618
01:44:03,229 --> 01:44:04,478
Just cross-check this as well.

1619
01:44:04,479 --> 01:44:05,854
- Yes, sir.
- Quick!

1620
01:44:12,979 --> 01:44:14,437
Why did you follow me?

1621
01:44:14,896 --> 01:44:15,979
Shush!

1622
01:44:18,312 --> 01:44:19,854
[inquisitive score]

1623
01:44:30,062 --> 01:44:31,396
[music ends abruptly]

1624
01:44:32,396 --> 01:44:34,437
Have you lost something, Madam?

1625
01:44:35,687 --> 01:44:38,062
If you tell me what it is,
I'll help you search for it.

1626
01:44:38,396 --> 01:44:41,561
No, it's... My daughter lost a toy.
I was just searching for it.

1627
01:44:41,562 --> 01:44:42,603
Oh.

1628
01:44:42,604 --> 01:44:46,728
I thought it might be gold,
or cash... something like that.

1629
01:44:46,729 --> 01:44:48,020
No, it's nothing like that.

1630
01:44:48,021 --> 01:44:49,062
I found it, Mumma.

1631
01:44:51,021 --> 01:44:52,021
Come.

1632
01:44:56,646 --> 01:44:58,854
[Anas] Bro, I can guarantee it!

1633
01:44:58,979 --> 01:45:00,770
I'm that certain the cash
was inside this house.

1634
01:45:00,771 --> 01:45:02,062
Or it's still hidden here.

1635
01:45:02,562 --> 01:45:05,021
The... The entire family
knows about it.

1636
01:45:05,896 --> 01:45:06,896
Super.

1637
01:45:07,062 --> 01:45:09,604
We will squeeze every
single cent out of them now.

1638
01:45:09,812 --> 01:45:10,854
Just wait and see, bro.

1639
01:45:11,229 --> 01:45:12,728
[dramatic music builds]

1640
01:45:12,729 --> 01:45:14,354
By the way, didn't you
call Rajeevan yet?

1641
01:45:15,062 --> 01:45:17,687
[rhythmic, pulsating score intensifies]

1642
01:45:27,229 --> 01:45:29,271
Oh, and here's the funny part.

1643
01:45:29,604 --> 01:45:30,979
We weren't alone today.

1644
01:45:31,771 --> 01:45:33,229
We actually had some competition.

1645
01:45:43,229 --> 01:45:44,728
- Hello.
- She's gone, sir!

1646
01:45:44,729 --> 01:45:46,312
Someone else has
taken the child!

1647
01:45:46,771 --> 01:45:48,187
Sir, can you please
get here fast?!

1648
01:45:51,521 --> 01:45:52,521
I'm coming.

1649
01:46:00,187 --> 01:46:02,354
- Hello?
- Am I speaking to Rajeevan?

1650
01:46:03,187 --> 01:46:03,978
Yes.

1651
01:46:03,979 --> 01:46:06,896
I won't threaten you with words
like kidnapping or custody.

1652
01:46:08,812 --> 01:46:10,604
One of your daughters
is currently with me.

1653
01:46:13,062 --> 01:46:16,062
You've got some serious wealth
on you that you never earned, right?

1654
01:46:18,187 --> 01:46:19,271
- Yes, I do.
- Right.

1655
01:46:20,604 --> 01:46:21,811
Just hand it over to me.

1656
01:46:21,812 --> 01:46:23,728
That way, you won't
suffer any other losses...

1657
01:46:23,729 --> 01:46:25,187
and your child
comes home safely.

1658
01:46:25,437 --> 01:46:27,021
- Happy ending.
- I'll give it to you.

1659
01:46:28,354 --> 01:46:30,021
I'll bring it wherever
you tell me to.

1660
01:46:30,271 --> 01:46:32,604
But don't you want to verify
if I'm lying or not, Rajeevan?

1661
01:46:34,062 --> 01:46:35,812
Don't you want to
speak to your daughter?

1662
01:46:40,437 --> 01:46:41,479
34.

1663
01:46:41,937 --> 01:46:43,062
No, it's okay.

1664
01:46:43,479 --> 01:46:44,479
There's no need for that.

1665
01:46:44,979 --> 01:46:46,853
Alright then, Rajeevan.
Get the cash ready.

1666
01:46:46,854 --> 01:46:48,062
I'll ring you in half an hour.

1667
01:46:48,979 --> 01:46:50,729
I'll tell you where to
bring the money, then.

1668
01:46:54,229 --> 01:46:55,312
32.

1669
01:46:57,062 --> 01:46:58,187
31.

1670
01:47:07,271 --> 01:47:08,312
Jacob!

1671
01:47:08,479 --> 01:47:09,811
We need to get that cash.

1672
01:47:09,812 --> 01:47:10,854
Right now!

1673
01:47:11,312 --> 01:47:12,312
Hurry!

1674
01:47:12,646 --> 01:47:14,354
[pulsating music swells]

1675
01:47:20,812 --> 01:47:24,978
We have breaking updates
on the Vellayani kidnapping case.

1676
01:47:24,979 --> 01:47:29,728
Police confirm that the car used to kidnap
Jiya Rajeevan in broad daylight

1677
01:47:29,729 --> 01:47:32,103
- was using a fake license plate.
- Hey!

1678
01:47:32,104 --> 01:47:35,520
Police discovered this through
investigating CCTV cameras.

1679
01:47:35,521 --> 01:47:36,562
Stop right there!

1680
01:47:37,896 --> 01:47:40,061
A strikingly similar case
occurred...

1681
01:47:40,062 --> 01:47:40,936
What's this?

1682
01:47:40,937 --> 01:47:42,645
It's just waste, sir.
Someone will pick it up shortly.

1683
01:47:42,646 --> 01:47:44,478
Let them clear it later.
First, show me what's inside.

1684
01:47:44,479 --> 01:47:47,396
[news reporting continues]

1685
01:47:47,687 --> 01:47:49,396
[suspenseful music swells]

1686
01:47:52,937 --> 01:47:54,021
Open every single one.

1687
01:47:54,187 --> 01:47:57,145
[news reporting continues]

1688
01:47:57,146 --> 01:47:58,146
This one?

1689
01:47:59,896 --> 01:48:00,937
This one too.

1690
01:48:10,271 --> 01:48:11,520
- Hmm. You can leave.

1691
01:48:11,521 --> 01:48:14,437
With cameraman Benny Balakrishnan,
I'm Snehamol Ninan.

1692
01:48:17,312 --> 01:48:19,478
No, bro! He hasn't showed
up in this area yet.

1693
01:48:19,479 --> 01:48:20,645
We're still keeping watch.

1694
01:48:20,646 --> 01:48:22,395
If something pops up,
give Anas a call.

1695
01:48:22,396 --> 01:48:23,437
Oh, okay.

1696
01:48:25,604 --> 01:48:27,395
[suspenseful music swells]

1697
01:48:27,396 --> 01:48:28,687
Bro, wait... isn't that our car?

1698
01:48:30,562 --> 01:48:32,062
Get the vehicle.
Come on!

1699
01:48:32,729 --> 01:48:36,020
Tch. They are just wasting our time.

1700
01:48:36,021 --> 01:48:37,520
How long are we supposed
to wait? The kid...

1701
01:48:37,521 --> 01:48:38,521
Hello!

1702
01:48:38,687 --> 01:48:40,937
- Which channel are you guys with?
- Why do you want to know, sir?

1703
01:48:42,437 --> 01:48:44,271
I've got an explosive
scoop to drop right now.

1704
01:48:44,646 --> 01:48:48,270
We have a highly explosive update
on the Vellayani kidnapping case.

1705
01:48:48,271 --> 01:48:51,770
In the shocking kidnapping
of nine-year-old Jiya Rajeevan,

1706
01:48:51,771 --> 01:48:53,603
crucial details have now emerged.

1707
01:48:53,604 --> 01:48:56,436
The police's prime suspect
is the child's own father, Rajeevan.

1708
01:48:56,437 --> 01:48:58,228
Rajeevan has gone into hiding.

1709
01:48:58,229 --> 01:49:01,145
The police have ramped up
their search for Rajeevan.

1710
01:49:01,146 --> 01:49:04,604
Police suspect that he may have
already fled the state.

1711
01:49:06,229 --> 01:49:07,479
Damn! Where is he?!

1712
01:49:10,354 --> 01:49:13,603
This isn't the first time Rajeevan
has become the centre of media attention.

1713
01:49:13,604 --> 01:49:15,062
Rajeevan is a total menace.

1714
01:49:15,354 --> 01:49:18,020
He even attacked our previous
security guard inside the elevator.

1715
01:49:18,021 --> 01:49:20,271
And when we tried to question them,
Meera snapped right back at us.

1716
01:49:20,979 --> 01:49:22,021
Stop the car!

1717
01:49:22,479 --> 01:49:23,521
Stop the damn car!

1718
01:49:24,396 --> 01:49:25,603
Stop it, you jerk!

1719
01:49:25,604 --> 01:49:27,021
How dare you steal my car!

1720
01:49:27,437 --> 01:49:29,061
Other residents have
to live here as well.

1721
01:49:29,062 --> 01:49:31,020
Our association warned
him multiple times.

1722
01:49:31,021 --> 01:49:33,062
- They must sell their flat.
- This can't continue here!

1723
01:49:33,312 --> 01:49:35,853
In the Vanchiyoor bank robbery
that took place last month,

1724
01:49:35,854 --> 01:49:38,979
police had initially investigated
Rajeevan's involvement.

1725
01:49:39,187 --> 01:49:41,895
Meanwhile, the manhunt for Rajeevan
has been heavily intensified.

1726
01:49:41,896 --> 01:49:44,603
Keeping in mind the possibility
of him leaving the district,

1727
01:49:44,604 --> 01:49:47,020
police personnel have been
deployed at the district borders.

1728
01:49:47,021 --> 01:49:48,687
[triumphant score swells]

1729
01:49:59,854 --> 01:50:01,312
The owner took the car back, sir!

1730
01:50:04,312 --> 01:50:06,061
I told them I had
something in the trunk,

1731
01:50:06,062 --> 01:50:08,478
and practically begged
them to let me take it,

1732
01:50:08,479 --> 01:50:09,646
but they refused.

1733
01:50:11,062 --> 01:50:13,270
Did you seriously pick
a random car on the street...

1734
01:50:13,271 --> 01:50:14,437
to pull off a job like this?!

1735
01:50:14,979 --> 01:50:17,395
You came up with a plan last night
and went right to bed.

1736
01:50:17,396 --> 01:50:19,479
Where am I going to find
a ride late at night, sir?

1737
01:50:23,479 --> 01:50:24,479
Sir.

1738
01:50:24,646 --> 01:50:27,229
She was on the phone with Rajeevan
for about a minute and a half.

1739
01:50:27,812 --> 01:50:29,062
What did Rajeevan say, Meera?

1740
01:50:30,062 --> 01:50:31,187
Is Jiya with him?

1741
01:50:32,271 --> 01:50:34,021
Where did Rajeevan say he was?

1742
01:50:34,979 --> 01:50:36,729
Meera, I think you
should give up on him.

1743
01:50:37,771 --> 01:50:39,437
After everything he has done,

1744
01:50:40,021 --> 01:50:41,520
please don't protect
him any longer.

1745
01:50:41,521 --> 01:50:43,062
[indistinct chatter]

1746
01:50:44,062 --> 01:50:45,937
[steady hum of a car engine]

1747
01:50:49,021 --> 01:50:50,646
Sir, look! That's the car!
There it goes!

1748
01:50:51,812 --> 01:50:53,479
[music turns powerful]

1749
01:51:15,979 --> 01:51:17,604
- Pull over.
- Move it to the side.

1750
01:51:17,979 --> 01:51:18,979
Come on!

1751
01:51:19,771 --> 01:51:21,853
[dramatic score]

1752
01:51:21,854 --> 01:51:23,646
Is this a routine check, sir?
Is it a breathalyser test?

1753
01:51:24,937 --> 01:51:26,062
Calm down, boy.

1754
01:51:29,312 --> 01:51:31,354
That missing kid still hasn't
been found yet, right sir?

1755
01:51:37,812 --> 01:51:39,061
Sir!

1756
01:51:39,062 --> 01:51:40,437
Our cash is in that boot.

1757
01:51:45,521 --> 01:51:47,229
What is this?
Garbage?

1758
01:51:47,687 --> 01:51:50,061
I don't know, sir.
My relative was using the car.

1759
01:51:50,062 --> 01:51:51,396
Don't play dumb with me.

1760
01:51:51,937 --> 01:51:53,062
Is there weed in these bags?

1761
01:51:53,729 --> 01:51:54,729
Open it.

1762
01:51:58,437 --> 01:52:00,062
[dramatic music builds]

1763
01:52:03,437 --> 01:52:05,812
[tires screeching to a sudden start]

1764
01:52:08,896 --> 01:52:09,896
Hey!

1765
01:52:10,604 --> 01:52:11,645
[loud crash]

1766
01:52:11,646 --> 01:52:12,646
Hey!

1767
01:52:13,354 --> 01:52:14,979
[indistinct chatter]

1768
01:52:16,937 --> 01:52:19,729
[dramatic score]

1769
01:52:20,229 --> 01:52:21,646
Move the vehicle in front.

1770
01:52:22,354 --> 01:52:24,021
Ah! Look who we have here.

1771
01:52:24,354 --> 01:52:25,562
Get out of the vehicle!

1772
01:52:27,187 --> 01:52:29,187
Sir, we have Rajeevan in custody!

1773
01:52:30,187 --> 01:52:31,229
Yes!

1774
01:52:31,729 --> 01:52:32,979
Is the kid with him?

1775
01:52:33,187 --> 01:52:35,020
No, sir. He's alone.

1776
01:52:35,021 --> 01:52:36,146
[siren sounds]

1777
01:52:40,062 --> 01:52:43,062
[dramatic score]

1778
01:52:43,979 --> 01:52:45,061
No, don't bring him here.

1779
01:52:45,062 --> 01:52:46,729
I need to talk to
him in detail first.

1780
01:52:46,854 --> 01:52:49,061
See if there's a police station
nearby that's convenient.

1781
01:52:49,062 --> 01:52:51,811
And... his capture must not be
leaked under any circumstances.

1782
01:52:51,812 --> 01:52:53,521
- Understood?
- Okay, sir.

1783
01:52:54,396 --> 01:52:55,521
- Jomon!
- Yes, sir.

1784
01:52:56,062 --> 01:52:57,854
All of you can leave!
No need to stall.

1785
01:52:58,562 --> 01:53:00,062
Hey! Keep me updated.

1786
01:53:00,187 --> 01:53:01,270
Sir!

1787
01:53:01,271 --> 01:53:02,979
Even if you have to
take extreme steps,

1788
01:53:03,187 --> 01:53:05,062
I'll handle the fallout.
Don't worry about it.

1789
01:53:05,354 --> 01:53:06,396
Okay, sir.

1790
01:53:11,479 --> 01:53:13,229
[auto-rickshaw engine sounds]

1791
01:53:14,687 --> 01:53:16,312
Keep following that car, son.

1792
01:53:16,854 --> 01:53:18,854
I've only ever heard
that line in the movies!

1793
01:53:19,062 --> 01:53:20,354
Let's follow them, then.

1794
01:53:21,062 --> 01:53:22,562
Bro, you can't just say that.

1795
01:53:22,896 --> 01:53:24,395
Who are we supposed to
ask for our money now?

1796
01:53:24,396 --> 01:53:26,771
Bro, please calm down.
Just let me think!

1797
01:53:26,979 --> 01:53:28,645
There's no time to think.

1798
01:53:28,646 --> 01:53:30,186
If you've got another
option, tell me!

1799
01:53:30,187 --> 01:53:30,895
Bro.

1800
01:53:30,896 --> 01:53:33,396
Forget about getting anything
out of Ra... Rajeevan now.

1801
01:53:33,729 --> 01:53:35,271
He's n... not getting
out anytime soon.

1802
01:53:35,896 --> 01:53:37,187
What about his wife?

1803
01:53:37,479 --> 01:53:39,228
She doesn't have a
care in the world, bro.

1804
01:53:39,229 --> 01:53:41,229
She thinks the kid is safe
with Rajeevan, right?

1805
01:53:42,312 --> 01:53:44,062
Shall we give
her a reason to panic?

1806
01:53:45,187 --> 01:53:46,479
Do you think that'll work, bro?

1807
01:53:46,604 --> 01:53:47,812
[phone rings]

1808
01:53:49,187 --> 01:53:50,896
Sir, we've traced Rajeevan.

1809
01:53:51,646 --> 01:53:53,271
Our team is already
on their way there.

1810
01:53:53,562 --> 01:53:54,771
[phone rings]

1811
01:53:55,646 --> 01:53:57,312
Sir, this is Meera's phone.

1812
01:53:57,687 --> 01:53:59,396
- Okay, okay.
- It's an unknown number.

1813
01:54:00,771 --> 01:54:02,521
- Where is she?
- In the room, sir.

1814
01:54:03,562 --> 01:54:04,604
Call her!

1815
01:54:05,062 --> 01:54:08,103
[Anas] Remember, the call will
will be on speaker.

1816
01:54:08,104 --> 01:54:10,604
So, don't say a word out of line.

1817
01:54:12,562 --> 01:54:13,562
Hello?

1818
01:54:15,104 --> 01:54:17,354
Are you and your husband
playing games with me?

1819
01:54:17,479 --> 01:54:20,854
You don't want to find out what
happens if you push me past my limit.

1820
01:54:21,146 --> 01:54:22,187
Hello, who is this?

1821
01:54:23,687 --> 01:54:25,396
I'm giving you one last chance.

1822
01:54:26,354 --> 01:54:30,021
I've made my demands perfectly
clear to your husband.

1823
01:54:31,229 --> 01:54:32,479
Do not delay this any further!

1824
01:54:33,479 --> 01:54:35,229
I'm not calling
a second time for this.

1825
01:54:35,771 --> 01:54:36,811
Am I clear?

1826
01:54:36,812 --> 01:54:38,437
Who... who is speaking?

1827
01:54:41,146 --> 01:54:43,020
- [Jiya] Mumma!
- Jiya!

1828
01:54:43,021 --> 01:54:44,061
Uh?

1829
01:54:44,062 --> 01:54:45,395
- Jiya, baby!
- Mumma!

1830
01:54:45,396 --> 01:54:46,646
I'm okay, Mumma.

1831
01:54:46,979 --> 01:54:49,062
- Jiya, where are you now?
- I don't know.

1832
01:54:49,312 --> 01:54:50,687
I'm with an uncle.

1833
01:54:50,896 --> 01:54:52,770
- Jiya, listen to me.
- Don't be stressed, Mumma.

1834
01:54:52,771 --> 01:54:54,062
Tell Amala I called.

1835
01:54:54,312 --> 01:54:55,312
May I?

1836
01:54:56,229 --> 01:54:57,229
Thanks.

1837
01:54:57,729 --> 01:54:58,729
Check it.

1838
01:55:04,437 --> 01:55:06,812
[dramatic music]

1839
01:55:24,062 --> 01:55:25,520
[reporters asking questions]

1840
01:55:25,521 --> 01:55:27,103
Ma'am, can you come with me?

1841
01:55:27,104 --> 01:55:29,436
Now, the doubt is whether
Rajeevan himself made the call.

1842
01:55:29,437 --> 01:55:30,687
We're still checking on that.

1843
01:55:31,562 --> 01:55:32,270
Yes, sir.

1844
01:55:32,271 --> 01:55:34,478
Madam, please come inside.
I need a quick word with you.

1845
01:55:34,479 --> 01:55:35,520
Understood sir.

1846
01:55:35,521 --> 01:55:36,561
Got it.

1847
01:55:36,562 --> 01:55:38,061
[reporter] Please let us in, sir.

1848
01:55:38,062 --> 01:55:40,146
Madam, do you have anything to say?

1849
01:55:40,354 --> 01:55:42,229
Who called you now?

1850
01:55:43,354 --> 01:55:47,270
[clamour of reporters arguing with police]

1851
01:55:47,271 --> 01:55:48,271
Could you close the door?

1852
01:55:48,479 --> 01:55:53,312
[reporters and police arguing]

1853
01:55:54,104 --> 01:55:55,020
Madam...

1854
01:55:55,021 --> 01:55:57,770
No one else here is going
to tell you the truth.

1855
01:55:57,771 --> 01:56:00,853
And I'm just too worried
to keep quiet about it.

1856
01:56:00,854 --> 01:56:02,396
Because I've got a child
of my own at home.

1857
01:56:03,979 --> 01:56:04,979
Madam...

1858
01:56:05,104 --> 01:56:07,562
Rajeevan was arrested
a little while ago.

1859
01:56:07,937 --> 01:56:09,937
But... your daughter
wasn't with him.

1860
01:56:10,521 --> 01:56:11,521
It's been confirmed.

1861
01:56:13,021 --> 01:56:15,270
Ma'am, this is... this is
definitely a kidnapping.

1862
01:56:15,271 --> 01:56:17,729
You heard that caller
e... earlier, right?

1863
01:56:18,146 --> 01:56:19,645
You know it's real, don't you?

1864
01:56:19,646 --> 01:56:20,728
So do I.

1865
01:56:20,729 --> 01:56:22,604
But Ajith sir doesn't get it.

1866
01:56:23,312 --> 01:56:26,145
We've thrown away precious
time chasing after Rajeevan.

1867
01:56:26,146 --> 01:56:27,646
Waiting any longer
is risky, Madam.

1868
01:56:30,896 --> 01:56:33,104
Rajeevan is arrested anyway.

1869
01:56:33,604 --> 01:56:35,896
Right now, you're the only
one who can save her, madam.

1870
01:56:36,687 --> 01:56:37,812
What do we do now?

1871
01:56:40,937 --> 01:56:43,812
The caller demanded
something, didn't he?

1872
01:56:44,104 --> 01:56:45,146
Do you know where that is?

1873
01:56:45,479 --> 01:56:47,979
It's better to deal
with them directly.

1874
01:56:48,479 --> 01:56:50,854
Relying on the police
to save her is just too risky.

1875
01:56:55,104 --> 01:56:56,354
Do you know where it is, Madam?

1876
01:56:58,104 --> 01:56:59,146
Huh?

1877
01:57:09,062 --> 01:57:11,061
[sound of rummaging through items]

1878
01:57:11,062 --> 01:57:12,146
Madam, keep it down.

1879
01:57:14,771 --> 01:57:16,353
- It was right here.
- Shh... quiet...

1880
01:57:16,354 --> 01:57:17,646
Now it's missing.

1881
01:57:17,979 --> 01:57:20,145
Do this, Madam.
Call Rajeevan.

1882
01:57:20,146 --> 01:57:22,686
He'll tell you where it is.
We can send someone to collect it.

1883
01:57:22,687 --> 01:57:23,687
Or I'll go myself.

1884
01:57:24,521 --> 01:57:25,978
But, will she be
safe until then?

1885
01:57:25,979 --> 01:57:27,353
She'll be perfectly safe, Madam.

1886
01:57:27,354 --> 01:57:29,396
Don't worry.
Nothing will happen to her.

1887
01:57:30,396 --> 01:57:32,645
Shouldn't we let them know?
Only then will she be safe.

1888
01:57:32,646 --> 01:57:35,354
But how do we even contact them?
We don't have their number!

1889
01:57:35,854 --> 01:57:37,521
[anxious music builds]

1890
01:57:40,146 --> 01:57:41,604
Madam! Madam!

1891
01:57:44,729 --> 01:57:47,312
[score intensifies with rising anxiety]

1892
01:57:48,146 --> 01:57:50,937
[reporters shouting indistinct questions]

1893
01:57:55,146 --> 01:57:58,186
[reporters shouting indistinct questions]

1894
01:57:58,187 --> 01:58:00,228
Are the police
on the right track, Ma'am?

1895
01:58:00,229 --> 01:58:01,312
Please let me speak.

1896
01:58:02,104 --> 01:58:03,437
Just let me speak, please.

1897
01:58:05,062 --> 01:58:06,395
This is...

1898
01:58:06,396 --> 01:58:08,729
This is for the person
who just called me.

1899
01:58:08,937 --> 01:58:10,271
I don't know who you are.

1900
01:58:10,729 --> 01:58:11,812
But...

1901
01:58:12,104 --> 01:58:13,521
If you're watching
this right now...

1902
01:58:13,646 --> 01:58:15,812
I know what you
demanded from Rajeevan.

1903
01:58:16,312 --> 01:58:17,979
I'll deliver it to you
anywhere you say.

1904
01:58:18,396 --> 01:58:19,604
I have it.
It's with me.

1905
01:58:20,729 --> 01:58:22,395
But I just need some time.

1906
01:58:22,396 --> 01:58:24,521
Until then, please
don't hurt my daughter.

1907
01:58:25,687 --> 01:58:26,729
Please.

1908
01:58:28,771 --> 01:58:29,936
[Anas] Bro.

1909
01:58:29,937 --> 01:58:31,104
That plan flopped too.

1910
01:58:31,521 --> 01:58:34,229
Look, we have no choice left.
We have to get Rajeevan out.

1911
01:58:34,479 --> 01:58:35,812
Yes! From the police station!

1912
01:58:41,146 --> 01:58:42,812
Sir, I need to speak to Rajeevan.

1913
01:58:42,979 --> 01:58:44,146
Tell me what I have to do.

1914
01:58:45,646 --> 01:58:46,771
What did you do, Meera?

1915
01:58:48,312 --> 01:58:51,104
[police jeep brakes
squealing as it stops]

1916
01:58:52,271 --> 01:58:54,103
Sir, we're here to sign in
for our daily bail reporting.

1917
01:58:54,104 --> 01:58:55,186
Hold your horses.

1918
01:58:55,187 --> 01:58:56,936
But sir, we have other work to do.

1919
01:58:56,937 --> 01:58:58,896
Like what, scamming more people?
Stand right there!

1920
01:59:01,729 --> 01:59:02,937
How long do we have to wait?

1921
01:59:05,396 --> 01:59:09,521
[phone rings]

1922
01:59:10,229 --> 01:59:11,604
- Hello, Jacob.
- Sir!

1923
01:59:11,729 --> 01:59:13,521
We're right by the car now.

1924
01:59:14,437 --> 01:59:16,729
Luckily, those guys haven't
found our money yet.

1925
01:59:17,729 --> 01:59:19,104
I'll tell you where I am, sir.

1926
01:59:20,562 --> 01:59:22,062
Can you get here quickly?

1927
01:59:24,271 --> 01:59:25,271
Wh... where?

1928
01:59:26,021 --> 01:59:27,687
Didn't you confiscate
his phone yet?!

1929
01:59:29,021 --> 01:59:30,062
Don't you have any sense?!

1930
01:59:31,479 --> 01:59:33,104
- Sir... I...
- Shut up!

1931
01:59:34,562 --> 01:59:36,271
Hello, who is speaking?

1932
01:59:37,229 --> 01:59:38,604
- Hello!
- Sir.

1933
01:59:40,271 --> 01:59:41,353
- Sir...
- Who did you call?

1934
01:59:41,354 --> 01:59:42,937
- My...
- Unlock the phone.

1935
01:59:44,646 --> 01:59:46,146
- Open it, man.
- Sir...

1936
01:59:46,812 --> 01:59:48,187
I'll do whatever you say, sir.

1937
01:59:49,146 --> 01:59:51,021
But you have to let me out
of here just for a little while.

1938
01:59:51,854 --> 01:59:54,061
Is this your in-laws' house
to stroll in and out of?

1939
01:59:54,062 --> 01:59:55,396
- Get lost!
- Sir.

1940
01:59:56,021 --> 01:59:57,771
Sir! I promise I'll come back.

1941
01:59:58,104 --> 02:00:00,312
- I'll sign any confession you want.
- Just go and sit over there!

1942
02:00:00,979 --> 02:00:02,062
My daughter is not with me.

1943
02:00:02,479 --> 02:00:04,312
I've been saying that
ever since I got here!

1944
02:00:04,937 --> 02:00:06,895
Do you know how long it's
been since they took her, sir?

1945
02:00:06,896 --> 02:00:08,186
You are doing nothing about it.

1946
02:00:08,187 --> 02:00:09,771
And now you're
holding me here too?

1947
02:00:11,771 --> 02:00:14,146
You think putting on a sob story
is going to make me let you go?

1948
02:00:19,271 --> 02:00:20,396
Did you really think...

1949
02:00:21,146 --> 02:00:22,354
I was that naive, sir?

1950
02:00:22,729 --> 02:00:24,937
[score gains tempo and intensity]

1951
02:00:26,937 --> 02:00:28,937
What the hell are you guys
even good for?!

1952
02:00:30,146 --> 02:00:31,146
Hey!

1953
02:00:32,646 --> 02:00:33,854
How dare you hit the Police!

1954
02:00:38,396 --> 02:00:41,062
Jomon... I want Rajeevan back in
that cell within thirty minutes.

1955
02:00:41,396 --> 02:00:43,437
Or you can tell your men
to hand in their badges.

1956
02:00:49,146 --> 02:00:50,146
Hello!

1957
02:00:50,437 --> 02:00:53,145
Bro! No matter what,
do not let the cops get Rajeevan.

1958
02:00:53,146 --> 02:00:54,437
Don't be scared, bro.

1959
02:00:54,979 --> 02:00:56,729
This is way easier than
snatching him from the station.

1960
02:00:57,312 --> 02:00:59,396
[rousing, dramatic music plays]

1961
02:01:20,396 --> 02:01:21,978
Hey! Stop!

1962
02:01:21,979 --> 02:01:23,396
Catch him!

1963
02:01:27,062 --> 02:01:30,020
Reports are coming in that Rajeevan
has escaped police custody.

1964
02:01:30,021 --> 02:01:31,728
We have yet to confirm
this officially.

1965
02:01:31,729 --> 02:01:34,770
Aside from the police, groups of
civilians are chasing Rajeevan...

1966
02:01:34,771 --> 02:01:35,853
according to reports.

1967
02:01:35,854 --> 02:01:38,686
The fortune meant for you and the kid
will be grabbed by random scumbags.

1968
02:01:38,687 --> 02:01:41,395
While we're left stuck with
the shame of being a thief's family!

1969
02:01:41,396 --> 02:01:42,728
[news continues]

1970
02:01:42,729 --> 02:01:44,437
Rajesh, I need to use your bus.

1971
02:01:44,646 --> 02:01:45,936
[dramatic music]

1972
02:01:45,937 --> 02:01:48,687
[phone rings]

1973
02:01:49,979 --> 02:01:51,395
- Hello?
- [Jacob] Sir...

1974
02:01:51,396 --> 02:01:53,146
The car and the cash
are still here, sir.

1975
02:01:53,687 --> 02:01:55,062
But if you're not here soon...

1976
02:01:55,437 --> 02:01:56,728
and someone spots it...

1977
02:01:56,729 --> 02:01:58,520
there is absolutely
nothing I can do.

1978
02:01:58,521 --> 02:02:00,521
I'm almost there, Jacob!
Ten minutes flat, I'll be there.

1979
02:02:01,979 --> 02:02:02,979
Okay.

1980
02:02:03,396 --> 02:02:06,604
[emotional score]

1981
02:02:08,396 --> 02:02:09,853
Bro, we won't get
another chance like this.

1982
02:02:09,854 --> 02:02:12,395
Call everyone who will join us.
We'll give them whatever share it takes.

1983
02:02:12,396 --> 02:02:14,771
[roar of motorbike engines]

1984
02:02:37,271 --> 02:02:38,271
Step on it!

1985
02:02:49,896 --> 02:02:51,146
Move in close!

1986
02:02:52,354 --> 02:02:53,812
Box him in!

1987
02:02:54,437 --> 02:02:56,479
[loud crash as car hits a wall]

1988
02:02:58,021 --> 02:03:03,729
Do you know what an average
government employee earns a month?

1989
02:03:04,604 --> 02:03:06,479
If one of his children

1990
02:03:06,771 --> 02:03:08,771
is kidnapped for ransom,

1991
02:03:09,021 --> 02:03:12,104
what's the absolute most
he can shell out to get them back?

1992
02:03:12,479 --> 02:03:13,854
[emotional score]

1993
02:03:15,479 --> 02:03:16,978
Drag him out of there!

1994
02:03:16,979 --> 02:03:17,979
You!

1995
02:03:26,229 --> 02:03:31,103
Yet, if someone takes such a massive
risk to kidnap his daughter...

1996
02:03:31,104 --> 02:03:34,062
they must know for a fact
that he's sitting on serious money.

1997
02:03:35,937 --> 02:03:37,062
But what money?

1998
02:03:43,562 --> 02:03:45,812
[dramatic music building steadily]

1999
02:03:51,979 --> 02:03:53,311
Who are these guys?
Did you call them?

2000
02:03:53,312 --> 02:03:54,729
I don't know.
Go after him!

2001
02:03:55,687 --> 02:03:56,854
Meera, call Rajeevan.

2002
02:03:57,354 --> 02:03:59,812
Tell him to stop making
things worse and just surrender.

2003
02:04:00,354 --> 02:04:02,603
And then?
Will you go save my daughter?

2004
02:04:02,604 --> 02:04:05,729
Sir, Jiya is not with Rajeevan.
Why don't you believe me?!

2005
02:04:05,937 --> 02:04:09,021
Stop wasting time chasing him!
Please, just find my daughter!

2006
02:04:12,021 --> 02:04:13,021
Come on!

2007
02:04:18,854 --> 02:04:20,229
Okay. I trust you, Meera.

2008
02:04:20,771 --> 02:04:24,021
She's not with him, and the ransom call
wasn't made on his behalf.

2009
02:04:24,437 --> 02:04:25,437
Yes, sir!

2010
02:04:26,146 --> 02:04:28,187
In that case, what exactly did
they demand from him?

2011
02:04:28,812 --> 02:04:31,228
What exactly did they want
you to arrange, Meera?

2012
02:04:31,229 --> 02:04:32,229
Huh?

2013
02:04:47,562 --> 02:04:48,562
Oh no!

2014
02:04:48,687 --> 02:04:49,854
His wife...

2015
02:04:50,271 --> 02:04:51,896
What did she tell the media?

2016
02:04:52,271 --> 02:04:54,271
"We have what you want."

2017
02:04:54,479 --> 02:04:56,312
"I will deliver it
anywhere you say."

2018
02:04:56,812 --> 02:04:58,146
Deliver what exactly?

2019
02:04:59,104 --> 02:05:00,437
[sound of approaching motorbike]

2020
02:05:16,854 --> 02:05:18,061
[Ajith] Meera, answer me!

2021
02:05:18,062 --> 02:05:19,146
Was the stolen cash here?

2022
02:05:20,354 --> 02:05:21,937
Meera, Rajeevan is a criminal.

2023
02:05:22,062 --> 02:05:23,646
And you know that too.

2024
02:05:23,896 --> 02:05:26,229
This isn't a random kidnapping
done because an opportunity arose.

2025
02:05:39,937 --> 02:05:41,979
They came looking
for your children, Meera!

2026
02:05:42,229 --> 02:05:43,645
More such people
will keep coming here!

2027
02:05:43,646 --> 02:05:45,354
And you and the kids will
be the ones who suffer.

2028
02:05:50,646 --> 02:05:52,561
Meera... this is your last chance.

2029
02:05:52,562 --> 02:05:54,396
At least save those
children from Rajeevan!

2030
02:05:58,812 --> 02:06:00,562
Don't waste your time, sir.

2031
02:06:02,521 --> 02:06:05,104
You're not getting
anything out of me.

2032
02:06:08,771 --> 02:06:11,146
This is the last chance...
I'm giving Rajeevan.

2033
02:06:13,771 --> 02:06:17,104
[intense score]

2034
02:07:02,562 --> 02:07:05,604
[indistinct chatter]

2035
02:07:08,604 --> 02:07:12,604
If you happen to spot Rajeevan
on the street, keep a close eye on him.

2036
02:07:14,396 --> 02:07:17,562
He might just have
those 17 crores on him.

2037
02:07:28,604 --> 02:07:31,312
He is a moving treasure now.

2038
02:07:32,187 --> 02:07:35,021
A moving treasure
worth 17 crores.

2039
02:07:36,229 --> 02:07:39,354
♪ Lay myself all on the ground ♪

2040
02:07:41,812 --> 02:07:45,812
♪ Don't you try to break me down ♪

2041
02:07:47,604 --> 02:07:50,937
♪ All in but it took it's toll ♪

2042
02:07:52,896 --> 02:07:56,062
♪ We lost our homes in search for gold ♪

2043
02:07:58,271 --> 02:08:00,562
♪ Where do I go now? ♪

2044
02:08:00,896 --> 02:08:03,146
♪ How far should I fall? ♪

2045
02:08:03,812 --> 02:08:06,561
♪ They're taking everything that I own,
Now they're taking my soul ♪

2046
02:08:06,562 --> 02:08:07,729
Stop right there!

2047
02:08:08,479 --> 02:08:09,936
What did you do
to that poor child?

2048
02:08:09,937 --> 02:08:12,062
♪ Where do I go?
Where do I? ♪

2049
02:08:12,187 --> 02:08:14,521
♪ How far should I fall? ♪

2050
02:08:15,396 --> 02:08:18,145
♪ I've given everything that I own ♪

2051
02:08:18,146 --> 02:08:21,396
♪ Can't give you my soul,
can't give you my soul ♪

2052
02:08:22,521 --> 02:08:25,146
♪ They're closing in,
I'm fighting on ♪

2053
02:08:25,396 --> 02:08:28,270
♪ Facing it all,
I'll run no more ♪

2054
02:08:28,271 --> 02:08:30,937
♪ They're watching me,
I'm in the deep ♪

2055
02:08:33,937 --> 02:08:36,436
♪ Where do I go?
Where do I? ♪

2056
02:08:36,437 --> 02:08:38,604
♪ How far should I fall? ♪

2057
02:08:39,354 --> 02:08:42,062
♪ I've given everything that I own ♪

2058
02:08:42,312 --> 02:08:45,604
♪ Can't give you my soul,
can't give you my soul ♪

2059
02:08:46,812 --> 02:08:49,312
♪ They're closing in,
I'm fighting on ♪

2060
02:08:49,687 --> 02:08:52,271
♪ Facing it all,
I'll run no more ♪

2061
02:08:52,437 --> 02:08:55,021
♪ They're watching me,
I'm in the deep ♪

2062
02:09:06,812 --> 02:09:08,854
This was in my car's boot, bro!

2063
02:09:09,312 --> 02:09:11,062
My head started
spinning when I saw it.

2064
02:09:15,187 --> 02:09:17,062
- How did this get in the boot?
- No idea...

2065
02:09:17,979 --> 02:09:19,104
I don't know.

2066
02:09:23,562 --> 02:09:24,562
Shall I call Anas?

2067
02:09:25,396 --> 02:09:26,396
No.

2068
02:09:27,437 --> 02:09:28,562
Call Safeer instead.

2069
02:09:28,771 --> 02:09:29,771
Yes, bro?

2070
02:09:31,604 --> 02:09:32,771
We lost him, bro.

2071
02:09:59,021 --> 02:10:01,395
Jacob, I'm on my
way there right now.

2072
02:10:01,396 --> 02:10:03,562
Sir, don't bother
coming here anymore.

2073
02:10:04,437 --> 02:10:06,186
Sharper guys walked off
with the money, sir!

2074
02:10:06,187 --> 02:10:07,645
I've been waiting forever, sir!

2075
02:10:07,646 --> 02:10:09,437
Couldn't you have
gotten here a bit faster?

2076
02:10:11,062 --> 02:10:12,312
Hello? Hel...

2077
02:10:18,229 --> 02:10:19,436
Where the hell are you all?

2078
02:10:19,437 --> 02:10:21,478
Sir, we're at the shopping complex.

2079
02:10:21,479 --> 02:10:23,270
But... we lost Rajeevan.

2080
02:10:23,271 --> 02:10:24,895
We're trying to track him down.

2081
02:10:24,896 --> 02:10:26,354
Don't make me swear at you!

2082
02:10:26,812 --> 02:10:28,561
The whole damn city
is tracking him!

2083
02:10:28,562 --> 02:10:30,478
Just moments ago on this very street,

2084
02:10:30,479 --> 02:10:32,395
people in the area
caught sight of Rajeevan.

2085
02:10:32,396 --> 02:10:35,186
They tried to detain him and
hand him over to the police.

2086
02:10:35,187 --> 02:10:38,645
We hear that the crowd chased
him into this shopping complex.

2087
02:10:38,646 --> 02:10:41,729
But the public couldn't
manage to subdue him there.

2088
02:10:45,854 --> 02:10:48,437
[persistent whirring
of a tracking drone]

2089
02:11:05,687 --> 02:11:07,271
Wait, where did he go?

2090
02:11:08,062 --> 02:11:09,146
We've lost him.

2091
02:11:14,062 --> 02:11:15,437
[music fades out]

2092
02:11:24,229 --> 02:11:25,271
Come on!

2093
02:11:28,771 --> 02:11:29,937
Go back inside!

2094
02:11:36,437 --> 02:11:37,604
Get out of my way!

2095
02:11:38,187 --> 02:11:40,437
Bro, let me say something
before you blow up.

2096
02:11:40,604 --> 02:11:43,061
Is there any place in Kerala
safer than this?

2097
02:11:43,062 --> 02:11:44,979
Bro, don't you know
what place this is?

2098
02:11:46,021 --> 02:11:48,061
What if someone saw you
bringing the kid here?

2099
02:11:48,062 --> 02:11:49,521
Nobody saw a thing, bro.

2100
02:11:49,812 --> 02:11:50,854
Don't worry!

2101
02:11:51,521 --> 02:11:53,562
Bro, there are cops
all over this place!

2102
02:11:53,687 --> 02:11:55,312
That's exactly my point.

2103
02:11:55,437 --> 02:11:56,812
This place is totally safe.

2104
02:12:02,104 --> 02:12:04,104
Why didn't y... you
answer my calls?

2105
02:12:04,979 --> 02:12:06,687
Weren't you supposed
to catch Rajeevan?

2106
02:12:07,687 --> 02:12:09,604
Don't any of you
want this m... money?

2107
02:12:10,021 --> 02:12:11,396
I called him back myself.

2108
02:12:11,562 --> 02:12:12,604
It's too risky now, bro.

2109
02:12:13,021 --> 02:12:15,686
If anyone identifies them,
it will be a huge embarrassment.

2110
02:12:15,687 --> 02:12:16,687
Ha!

2111
02:12:17,437 --> 02:12:20,562
Meaning... none of you
want to take any risks,

2112
02:12:20,812 --> 02:12:22,021
but you still want the cash.

2113
02:12:22,521 --> 02:12:24,478
No embarrassment
about that, huh?

2114
02:12:24,479 --> 02:12:27,228
Look, we backed you up
when you needed us, bro!

2115
02:12:27,229 --> 02:12:28,728
Don't give us that kind of
garbage talk, okay?!

2116
02:12:28,729 --> 02:12:29,729
Shush!

2117
02:12:30,687 --> 02:12:31,729
Keep your voice down!

2118
02:12:31,854 --> 02:12:33,021
Calm down, bro.

2119
02:12:33,979 --> 02:12:35,271
Listen to me for a second.

2120
02:12:35,646 --> 02:12:36,937
You already know this, right?

2121
02:12:37,104 --> 02:12:40,021
I don't need to resort to stealing
just to make a buck.

2122
02:12:40,271 --> 02:12:42,604
I've got my own businesses
and ventures to run.

2123
02:12:42,854 --> 02:12:44,604
That embarrassment
I mentioned...

2124
02:12:44,812 --> 02:12:46,687
will damage my reputation
in that circle.

2125
02:12:47,812 --> 02:12:49,812
You won't get it
even if I tell you, bro.

2126
02:12:50,687 --> 02:12:52,396
Anyway, no use
bringing it up now.

2127
02:12:54,021 --> 02:12:55,521
You're on your own, bro.
Deal with it.

2128
02:12:55,771 --> 02:12:58,312
We don't want the millions,
nor do we need the jewels.

2129
02:12:59,312 --> 02:13:00,312
- Ajas...
- Yeah?

2130
02:13:00,479 --> 02:13:01,854
Gather everything.
Let's head out.

2131
02:13:03,979 --> 02:13:06,229
I'm only saying this since
you're married to my sister.

2132
02:13:06,479 --> 02:13:09,271
It's not safe to step outside
with the kid anymore.

2133
02:13:09,646 --> 02:13:11,896
So don't get all
emotional about this now.

2134
02:13:12,271 --> 02:13:14,104
Watch your back and do
what needs to be done.

2135
02:13:14,646 --> 02:13:16,604
Try to save your own skin.

2136
02:13:18,271 --> 02:13:19,271
Brother-in-law!

2137
02:13:20,562 --> 02:13:22,687
If I go down,
I'm taking you all down with me.

2138
02:13:23,021 --> 02:13:24,021
You know, right?

2139
02:13:24,896 --> 02:13:25,937
I am a police officer.

2140
02:13:27,187 --> 02:13:31,354
I'll use the CCTV, the car, and this kid's
statement to tighten a noose around you.

2141
02:13:32,687 --> 02:13:35,104
The damage you face then
will be much worse.

2142
02:13:38,771 --> 02:13:40,104
- Safeer.
- Yes, bro.

2143
02:13:41,854 --> 02:13:43,479
Let's settle this
before we leave.

2144
02:13:46,104 --> 02:13:47,354
Thirteen...

2145
02:13:49,062 --> 02:13:50,271
Twelve...

2146
02:13:53,646 --> 02:13:54,646
Eleven...

2147
02:13:55,062 --> 02:13:57,062
[bus speeding through traffic]

2148
02:13:59,562 --> 02:14:01,271
Grab him and pin him down!

2149
02:14:11,562 --> 02:14:13,521
[rap song begins]

2150
02:14:58,854 --> 02:15:00,312
Beat him to a pulp!

2151
02:15:17,729 --> 02:15:19,104
[glass breaks]

2152
02:16:01,646 --> 02:16:03,271
[screaming in panic]

2153
02:16:05,312 --> 02:16:08,354
[screaming in terror]

2154
02:16:09,437 --> 02:16:11,604
[loud crash, glass shattering]

2155
02:16:14,604 --> 02:16:16,312
[screaming out in intense pain]

2156
02:16:19,354 --> 02:16:21,271
Where is Jiya, Mumma?

2157
02:16:21,812 --> 02:16:23,562
It's been quite a while.

2158
02:16:23,896 --> 02:16:25,771
Why isn't she here yet?

2159
02:16:28,687 --> 02:16:29,687
Come.

2160
02:16:33,396 --> 02:16:35,146
[suspenseful music builds]

2161
02:16:48,604 --> 02:16:49,729
I don't know.

2162
02:16:49,854 --> 02:16:52,520
If you come to know,
please let me know.

2163
02:16:52,521 --> 02:16:53,521
Okay.

2164
02:16:55,479 --> 02:16:57,604
What can be done now?
Didn't I tell you earlier?

2165
02:16:57,729 --> 02:16:59,312
[indistinct chatter]

2166
02:17:00,354 --> 02:17:03,103
Sir, those are just media rumours!
Don't buy into it, please.

2167
02:17:03,104 --> 02:17:04,811
In the end, it happened
exactly as we said, right?

2168
02:17:04,812 --> 02:17:05,853
That's true.

2169
02:17:05,854 --> 02:17:08,771
Sir, the crowd suddenly turned
violent and attacked Rajeevan.

2170
02:17:09,979 --> 02:17:10,979
Sir?

2171
02:17:11,854 --> 02:17:14,521
Sir, the missing child is definitely
with Rajeevan. I'm sure of it.

2172
02:17:14,687 --> 02:17:16,353
He's the one who called us...

2173
02:17:16,354 --> 02:17:17,854
- and tried to confuse us.
- Sir!

2174
02:17:18,937 --> 02:17:19,978
I'll keep you updated, sir!

2175
02:17:19,979 --> 02:17:21,978
Sir, my daughter has
been missing for so long...

2176
02:17:21,979 --> 02:17:22,979
Meera...

2177
02:17:23,229 --> 02:17:24,729
Our priority right now is Rajeevan.

2178
02:17:25,562 --> 02:17:26,936
You might trust him,

2179
02:17:26,937 --> 02:17:27,937
but we don't.

2180
02:17:28,354 --> 02:17:30,021
So let us do our job!

2181
02:17:30,479 --> 02:17:31,562
Please.

2182
02:17:33,271 --> 02:17:34,896
[jeep drives away]

2183
02:17:54,771 --> 02:17:56,646
[song begins]

2184
02:18:19,771 --> 02:18:22,729
♪ I'm a nobody, Hear me out! ♪

2185
02:18:24,729 --> 02:18:29,353
♪ The streets rain fire,
with battle cries and darkened skies ♪

2186
02:18:29,354 --> 02:18:31,021
♪ Hear me out! ♪

2187
02:18:32,521 --> 02:18:37,770
♪ Fierce as a ritual fire,
they burn and smoulder as they rise ♪

2188
02:18:37,771 --> 02:18:39,687
♪ Hear me out! ♪

2189
02:18:41,604 --> 02:18:44,729
♪ A rage has surged
like ocean waves that roar ♪

2190
02:18:44,854 --> 02:18:49,479
♪ A deep-set vengeance sits in dreams,
etched forevermore ♪

2191
02:18:50,187 --> 02:18:54,062
♪ It blazes like never before ♪

2192
02:18:55,687 --> 02:18:58,062
♪ Without an answer in sight ♪

2193
02:18:58,521 --> 02:19:03,021
♪ I won't flinch,
I won't turn from this fight ♪

2194
02:19:22,896 --> 02:19:25,562
Excuse me, brother!
My daughter is missing.

2195
02:19:25,687 --> 02:19:28,771
- Have you seen her anywhere?
- Oh no I haven't, sister.

2196
02:19:29,062 --> 02:19:30,146
Sir?

2197
02:19:30,521 --> 02:19:32,520
♪ Who speaks justice?
What is right? ♪

2198
02:19:32,521 --> 02:19:34,103
Honourable Chief Minister,

2199
02:19:34,104 --> 02:19:35,395
I have a question for you.

2200
02:19:35,396 --> 02:19:37,145
What else should Rajeevan
and Meera have done,

2201
02:19:37,146 --> 02:19:39,520
to snap the officials
out of their slumber, sir?

2202
02:19:39,521 --> 02:19:41,771
♪ Who stands beside us
in this fight? ♪

2203
02:19:41,896 --> 02:19:44,353
♪ Who speaks justice?
What is right? ♪

2204
02:19:44,354 --> 02:19:47,104
Hours have passed since his
beloved daughter went missing.

2205
02:19:47,354 --> 02:19:50,187
What more should this
poor mother Meera have done?

2206
02:19:52,812 --> 02:19:57,229
Did Meera halt all these vehicles
hoping her daughter was inside one?

2207
02:19:57,604 --> 02:19:58,771
Absolutely not!

2208
02:19:58,937 --> 02:20:01,395
This mother was forced
out onto the streets

2209
02:20:01,396 --> 02:20:03,771
simply to prove
to the State and the police...

2210
02:20:03,896 --> 02:20:06,479
that they are failing
to do their duty.

2211
02:20:08,021 --> 02:20:11,270
Rajeevan went inside the bank,
but he didn't attempt a robbery.

2212
02:20:11,271 --> 02:20:13,311
He didn't try to harm anyone.

2213
02:20:13,312 --> 02:20:15,853
Even as he raced to rescue
his kidnapped daughter,

2214
02:20:15,854 --> 02:20:20,646
today we saw the stark protest
of a common man hunted by police.

2215
02:20:23,437 --> 02:20:24,562
Boom!

2216
02:20:25,521 --> 02:20:27,978
Meera's protest gained massive
support from the public,

2217
02:20:27,979 --> 02:20:30,603
both on social media
and out on the streets.

2218
02:20:30,604 --> 02:20:32,228
We want justice from the police!

2219
02:20:32,229 --> 02:20:34,895
Moments ago, the leader
of the opposition arrived in person

2220
02:20:34,896 --> 02:20:37,270
to extend his full support
to Meera and the family.

2221
02:20:37,271 --> 02:20:39,145
Look at the plight of a mother
in our very own land!

2222
02:20:39,146 --> 02:20:41,478
To save her missing child,

2223
02:20:41,479 --> 02:20:43,436
she is forced onto the streets,

2224
02:20:43,437 --> 02:20:45,895
carrying her other
child on her shoulders.

2225
02:20:45,896 --> 02:20:49,521
And a father in our own land...
A government official, no less...

2226
02:20:49,687 --> 02:20:55,103
has to break into a bank to raise
the ransom money to rescue his daughter.

2227
02:20:55,104 --> 02:20:56,979
What a shameful state of affairs!

2228
02:20:59,562 --> 02:21:01,770
This entire saga began
at that very bank.

2229
02:21:01,771 --> 02:21:04,812
Rajeevan must have figured
it should end there as well.

2230
02:21:05,812 --> 02:21:07,021
It's just a replica, sir!

2231
02:21:07,437 --> 02:21:09,479
I don't think he came here
to steal anything.

2232
02:21:09,937 --> 02:21:11,312
His plan is to surrender.

2233
02:21:13,021 --> 02:21:15,020
Honourable Chief Minister...

2234
02:21:15,021 --> 02:21:16,811
Until your eyes finally open,

2235
02:21:16,812 --> 02:21:19,771
we will stand with this mother
in her fight!

2236
02:21:22,604 --> 02:21:24,895
[articles criticising the Chief Minister]

2237
02:21:24,896 --> 02:21:28,686
Despite numerous protests erupting
across the streets of Kerala...

2238
02:21:28,687 --> 02:21:32,645
neither the CM nor his office
has offered a single response.

2239
02:21:32,646 --> 02:21:35,145
The Chief Minister, who also handles
the Home Department,

2240
02:21:35,146 --> 02:21:37,520
continues to maintain absolute
silence on this issue.

2241
02:21:37,521 --> 02:21:41,103
Rajeevan was escorted from the bank
under a heavy police cordon.

2242
02:21:41,104 --> 02:21:46,228
However, there is no clarity on
where he was shifted to.

2243
02:21:46,229 --> 02:21:49,853
Streets across Kerala witnessed
widespread protests today.

2244
02:21:49,854 --> 02:21:52,853
The police may be able
to crush this protest,

2245
02:21:52,854 --> 02:21:57,021
but no force can break the spirit
this brave mother showed today.

2246
02:22:04,646 --> 02:22:07,561
Hours have passed since Meera
was taken into police custody.

2247
02:22:07,562 --> 02:22:10,020
It remains unclear if the police
have invoked other sections

2248
02:22:10,021 --> 02:22:12,020
to record her official arrest.

2249
02:22:12,021 --> 02:22:16,936
We must wait to see if this mother's
solitary crusade to get her child back

2250
02:22:16,937 --> 02:22:20,353
will shake the authorities
out of their slumber.

2251
02:22:20,354 --> 02:22:23,520
A child barely nine years old
remains missing out there.

2252
02:22:23,521 --> 02:22:25,895
And both her parents
are locked in police custody.

2253
02:22:25,896 --> 02:22:29,020
Public sentiment against the Chief Minister
is growing incredibly strong.

2254
02:22:29,021 --> 02:22:32,145
It is obvious to those who have
seen recent social media posts.

2255
02:22:32,146 --> 02:22:35,770
Today, the whole of Kerala
is asking just one question:

2256
02:22:35,771 --> 02:22:37,771
"Where are you, Chief Minister?"

2257
02:22:42,146 --> 02:22:49,354
[cameras clicking continuously]

2258
02:22:50,979 --> 02:22:53,229
[dramatic music builds]

2259
02:22:55,521 --> 02:22:58,062
To all those who asked
where the Chief Minister is...

2260
02:22:58,312 --> 02:23:00,021
Here I am!

2261
02:23:01,354 --> 02:23:04,187
To those who demanded
I break my silence...

2262
02:23:04,437 --> 02:23:05,479
Consider it broken.

2263
02:23:06,479 --> 02:23:07,479
And...

2264
02:23:07,979 --> 02:23:10,604
to those demanding the Chief
Minister's resignation...

2265
02:23:11,521 --> 02:23:13,021
Well, keep dreaming.

2266
02:23:14,479 --> 02:23:16,021
Anyway...

2267
02:23:16,354 --> 02:23:19,186
The reason I called you all here
so early this morning...

2268
02:23:19,187 --> 02:23:21,062
is to inform you of something.

2269
02:23:23,687 --> 02:23:28,479
Jiya Rajeevan, the child kidnapped
from Vellayani yesterday afternoon--

2270
02:23:29,187 --> 02:23:30,354
Who is this girl?

2271
02:23:31,729 --> 02:23:32,771
What's the issue?

2272
02:23:33,437 --> 02:23:36,354
That was a truly
painful piece of news.

2273
02:23:37,187 --> 02:23:38,436
Just like all of you...

2274
02:23:38,437 --> 02:23:41,062
I too have been deeply concerned
since yesterday.

2275
02:23:41,812 --> 02:23:43,521
What is going on, DGP?

2276
02:23:43,854 --> 02:23:47,021
Is the Kerala Police incapable
of handling a minor kidnapping case?

2277
02:23:47,437 --> 02:23:49,061
Must I call in the CBI for this?

2278
02:23:49,062 --> 02:23:50,020
Not required, sir.

2279
02:23:50,021 --> 02:23:52,062
We have some solid leads.

2280
02:23:52,271 --> 02:23:53,521
Give us just two hours...

2281
02:23:53,812 --> 02:23:57,604
Are you certain that Rajeevan
kidnapped his own child?

2282
02:23:57,896 --> 02:23:59,103
I don't know, sir.

2283
02:23:59,104 --> 02:24:01,270
I mean...
I'm not so sure now.

2284
02:24:01,271 --> 02:24:02,354
Ah, terrific!

2285
02:24:03,062 --> 02:24:04,521
"Failure of the Home Department!"

2286
02:24:05,229 --> 02:24:06,978
More of my effigies
will burn today!

2287
02:24:06,979 --> 02:24:08,145
- CM!
- Yes?

2288
02:24:08,146 --> 02:24:12,229
Rajeevan and Meera's protest
is national news now.

2289
02:24:14,604 --> 02:24:15,854
What protest?!

2290
02:24:16,187 --> 02:24:19,062
One of them gets on the road,
blocks traffic, and stirs up trouble.

2291
02:24:19,187 --> 02:24:20,854
[crowd shouting slogans]

2292
02:24:21,062 --> 02:24:24,771
The other walks into a bank
with a gun and scares everyone away.

2293
02:24:27,521 --> 02:24:31,146
To top it off, two ministers
from Delhi landed this morning.

2294
02:24:31,354 --> 02:24:34,104
Great. Now we have to deal
with their little circus today as well.

2295
02:24:35,187 --> 02:24:36,478
Sigh!

2296
02:24:36,479 --> 02:24:39,396
Look at all this havoc sparked
by some nobody named Rajeevan!

2297
02:24:40,521 --> 02:24:42,271
[intriguing music]

2298
02:24:53,062 --> 02:24:54,478
- CM?
- Yes?

2299
02:24:54,479 --> 02:24:56,270
Will you try talking to him, CM?

2300
02:24:56,271 --> 02:24:57,354
To who?

2301
02:24:58,729 --> 02:25:00,271
Why should I speak to him?

2302
02:25:00,937 --> 02:25:03,479
If the top brass of the IPS
failed to make him talk,

2303
02:25:03,604 --> 02:25:05,062
do you think I can manage it?

2304
02:25:05,562 --> 02:25:08,021
If we want to wrap
up this issue quickly,

2305
02:25:08,146 --> 02:25:10,146
the guy needs to open
his mouth, CM!

2306
02:25:10,729 --> 02:25:12,812
You've caused so much havoc,

2307
02:25:12,937 --> 02:25:15,062
and you still refuse
to cooperate with the police?

2308
02:25:16,312 --> 02:25:19,396
How long are they supposed
to sit and gaze at your face?

2309
02:25:19,687 --> 02:25:22,896
If you know something, why don't you
just open your mouth and tell them?

2310
02:25:23,312 --> 02:25:25,604
Their job is not just to cater
to your personal problems!

2311
02:25:25,771 --> 02:25:26,771
Do you know that?

2312
02:25:27,646 --> 02:25:28,854
I am aware, CM.

2313
02:25:29,771 --> 02:25:31,271
But then, who will solve
my problems?

2314
02:25:32,604 --> 02:25:34,771
- I have to look out for myself, right?
- No need!

2315
02:25:34,979 --> 02:25:37,229
The State will handle it.
Or I will.

2316
02:25:37,521 --> 02:25:39,271
- Do you doubt that?
- Yes, I do.

2317
02:25:40,979 --> 02:25:42,562
Because to you and the State...

2318
02:25:43,187 --> 02:25:44,604
I'm just a nobody!

2319
02:25:49,312 --> 02:25:50,395
Listen!

2320
02:25:50,396 --> 02:25:52,521
You've been sitting here
talking all this time,

2321
02:25:52,812 --> 02:25:55,271
but did I ask about your child
even once?

2322
02:25:55,729 --> 02:25:57,062
Do you know why?

2323
02:25:57,396 --> 02:25:58,770
You tell me, CM.

2324
02:25:58,771 --> 02:26:01,395
It's because you tucked the child
away safely somewhere

2325
02:26:01,396 --> 02:26:04,604
before walking in here to talk.
I figured that out long ago.

2326
02:26:23,354 --> 02:26:25,312
[tension builds in the score]

2327
02:26:31,021 --> 02:26:32,021
You!

2328
02:26:32,646 --> 02:26:33,646
Hey!

2329
02:26:38,396 --> 02:26:40,187
Did you hear what the CM asked?

2330
02:26:40,729 --> 02:26:42,896
Open your mouth and speak up!

2331
02:26:43,062 --> 02:26:44,687
Did you find your child?!

2332
02:26:44,979 --> 02:26:45,979
Hey!

2333
02:26:46,646 --> 02:26:47,853
Ajas!

2334
02:26:47,854 --> 02:26:49,021
Drop it.

2335
02:26:49,187 --> 02:26:50,436
Rajeevan,

2336
02:26:50,437 --> 02:26:51,854
don't create trouble.

2337
02:26:52,354 --> 02:26:53,854
Your daughter is right here.

2338
02:26:55,396 --> 02:26:56,228
Hey!

2339
02:26:56,229 --> 02:26:58,561
For the last fifteen hours,
the DGP and his entire force

2340
02:26:58,562 --> 02:27:00,520
have been hunting high and low
for your child.

2341
02:27:00,521 --> 02:27:02,103
Where did you hide her?!

2342
02:27:02,104 --> 02:27:03,604
Did you sneak her
out of the state?

2343
02:27:04,729 --> 02:27:06,271
[tense score plays]

2344
02:27:09,354 --> 02:27:10,521
Don't be scared, dear.

2345
02:27:11,187 --> 02:27:12,354
I'm here with your Papa.

2346
02:27:12,771 --> 02:27:14,770
So, no matter how much I insist,

2347
02:27:14,771 --> 02:27:17,104
you won't say a word
about your child?

2348
02:27:17,729 --> 02:27:18,812
I won't, CM.

2349
02:27:19,562 --> 02:27:20,562
Found it, sir!

2350
02:27:27,479 --> 02:27:28,479
The rest is inside.

2351
02:27:34,729 --> 02:27:35,729
Sir!

2352
02:27:38,521 --> 02:27:39,979
Who else wants
a piece of this now?!

2353
02:27:41,479 --> 02:27:42,521
Pick it up.

2354
02:27:45,729 --> 02:27:47,396
I had a moment
of weakness, brother.

2355
02:27:48,604 --> 02:27:50,104
Now this money is all yours.

2356
02:27:56,312 --> 02:27:57,896
If you want to play tough...

2357
02:27:58,937 --> 02:28:00,312
- DGP!
- Sir!

2358
02:28:00,521 --> 02:28:02,104
You have exactly two hours.

2359
02:28:02,271 --> 02:28:04,229
Deploy every cop in Kerala...

2360
02:28:04,437 --> 02:28:05,937
Can you find this child?

2361
02:28:06,312 --> 02:28:07,396
I'll try, sir.

2362
02:28:07,729 --> 02:28:08,895
"Try?" Really?

2363
02:28:08,896 --> 02:28:10,229
So you mean you can't!

2364
02:28:15,896 --> 02:28:18,021
- Where is Papa?
- Papa will be right here, okay?

2365
02:28:18,312 --> 02:28:19,604
He has some work outside.

2366
02:28:21,437 --> 02:28:22,604
You!

2367
02:28:22,771 --> 02:28:24,979
[powerful score swells
as a fight breaks out]

2368
02:28:33,187 --> 02:28:34,395
You!

2369
02:28:34,396 --> 02:28:35,729
[fight continues]

2370
02:29:09,146 --> 02:29:10,604
[screaming in pain]

2371
02:29:11,646 --> 02:29:12,896
- Rajendran.
- Sir?

2372
02:29:13,646 --> 02:29:15,687
He has come here
with a clear agenda.

2373
02:29:15,979 --> 02:29:17,687
No doubt about it, sir.

2374
02:29:18,104 --> 02:29:20,021
Could it be political?

2375
02:29:20,437 --> 02:29:21,645
I don't think so.

2376
02:29:21,646 --> 02:29:22,895
Back in his college days,

2377
02:29:22,896 --> 02:29:24,896
he was part of our own cadre.

2378
02:29:25,937 --> 02:29:28,061
Honestly, it's our own cadre
we have to fear the most today!

2379
02:29:28,062 --> 02:29:30,895
He knows exactly
which cards to play now, CM.

2380
02:29:30,896 --> 02:29:33,853
Look at how he hijacked
the media and public support.

2381
02:29:33,854 --> 02:29:34,895
So...

2382
02:29:34,896 --> 02:29:37,271
we have to deal with him
once and for all.

2383
02:29:38,437 --> 02:29:39,521
Now that...

2384
02:29:39,896 --> 02:29:41,521
I've already gotten
involved in this,

2385
02:29:42,229 --> 02:29:44,687
you'll leave this room only after
this is settled.

2386
02:29:44,896 --> 02:29:46,729
I had already decided
that yesterday, CM.

2387
02:29:47,062 --> 02:29:48,062
So...

2388
02:29:48,937 --> 02:29:51,146
your children need to be
able to go to school safely.

2389
02:29:51,479 --> 02:29:54,062
Beyond that, you don't have
any other ulterior motives.

2390
02:29:54,729 --> 02:29:55,729
None.

2391
02:29:55,979 --> 02:29:58,437
Then hear out my demand first!

2392
02:29:59,229 --> 02:30:00,895
After all,
I'm the Chief Minister here.

2393
02:30:00,896 --> 02:30:02,062
Not you.

2394
02:30:03,604 --> 02:30:04,646
Understood.

2395
02:30:05,896 --> 02:30:08,896
Here is some news
that will bring us all great relief.

2396
02:30:09,979 --> 02:30:13,020
Missing child Jiya Rajeevan
has just been found by police.

2397
02:30:13,021 --> 02:30:16,603
The child was kept hidden
in a police quarters flat.

2398
02:30:16,604 --> 02:30:19,271
Police have now moved her
to the General Hospital.

2399
02:30:21,979 --> 02:30:23,312
What did you understand?

2400
02:30:26,062 --> 02:30:28,146
That you're going to cash in
on me for your own gain.

2401
02:30:30,687 --> 02:30:33,270
It was due to the CM's swift,
decisive intervention

2402
02:30:33,271 --> 02:30:35,270
that Jiya Rajeevan
could be rescued.

2403
02:30:35,271 --> 02:30:39,854
His deep empathy, even for
a common man's plight, is commendable.

2404
02:30:40,021 --> 02:30:41,895
Those who kidnapped the child

2405
02:30:41,896 --> 02:30:44,021
are currently in police custody.

2406
02:30:44,771 --> 02:30:46,936
It brings me great shame
to admit this.

2407
02:30:46,937 --> 02:30:47,978
Because...

2408
02:30:47,979 --> 02:30:50,520
the prime accused in this case
happens to be a policeman.

2409
02:30:50,521 --> 02:30:53,146
And the remaining culprits
are his family members.

2410
02:30:54,854 --> 02:30:57,062
For the past 15 hours,

2411
02:30:57,187 --> 02:31:01,604
working tirelessly around the clock
to rescue this child unscathed,

2412
02:31:01,771 --> 02:31:03,978
our police force
has done a stellar job.

2413
02:31:03,979 --> 02:31:08,146
I congratulate them all
on this occasion, especially the DGP.

2414
02:31:10,104 --> 02:31:11,104
Also...

2415
02:31:11,479 --> 02:31:14,104
when you hear that
Rajeevan is not the culprit,

2416
02:31:14,271 --> 02:31:17,145
you all are bound
to feel a bit disappointed.

2417
02:31:17,146 --> 02:31:18,146
After all...

2418
02:31:18,521 --> 02:31:21,771
you spent all of yesterday
having a field day using him.

2419
02:31:21,896 --> 02:31:25,895
Rajeevan has no connection
to the Vanchiyoor bank robbery

2420
02:31:25,896 --> 02:31:27,854
that took place two weeks ago.

2421
02:31:28,312 --> 02:31:32,770
The Crime Branch and local police
conducted a thorough probe...

2422
02:31:32,771 --> 02:31:34,896
and found absolutely
no evidence against him.

2423
02:31:35,229 --> 02:31:39,271
Yet, Rajeevan and his family were
relentlessly hounded over it.

2424
02:31:40,312 --> 02:31:43,021
It even escalated to the point
where his child was kidnapped.

2425
02:31:43,437 --> 02:31:45,562
The State Police, the media,

2426
02:31:45,812 --> 02:31:48,061
and every one of us are to blame.

2427
02:31:48,062 --> 02:31:51,936
For the trauma and immense pain
caused to Rajeevan and his family,

2428
02:31:51,937 --> 02:31:54,604
I express my profound regret
on behalf of the State.

2429
02:31:55,021 --> 02:31:56,436
At least from now on,

2430
02:31:56,437 --> 02:31:58,979
please leave
Rajeevan and his family alone.

2431
02:31:59,146 --> 02:32:01,521
[dramatic score]

2432
02:32:01,729 --> 02:32:04,021
For messing this up so badly,
slap those two...

2433
02:32:04,229 --> 02:32:05,854
with suspension orders
immediately!

2434
02:32:07,146 --> 02:32:10,729
Until I vacate this chair,
both of them should sit at home.

2435
02:32:11,271 --> 02:32:12,353
- Got it?
- Yes, sir!

2436
02:32:12,354 --> 02:32:15,353
Well, the public and the press
have someone new to celebrate now.

2437
02:32:15,354 --> 02:32:18,062
Now comes a wave of inaugurations,
news channel debates...

2438
02:32:18,396 --> 02:32:20,395
and maybe even a ticket
for the next election.

2439
02:32:20,396 --> 02:32:22,353
With that, Rajeevan
is totally set for life.

2440
02:32:22,354 --> 02:32:25,020
Where the State and system failed,
Rajeevan fought for his daughter--

2441
02:32:25,021 --> 02:32:27,187
I will give you all time
for questions later.

2442
02:32:28,146 --> 02:32:30,729
The reason I summoned you all
so early this morning...

2443
02:32:31,271 --> 02:32:33,270
is to address another
highly important matter.

2444
02:32:33,271 --> 02:32:35,687
So this press meet wasn't
about Rajeevan's case, CM?

2445
02:32:38,021 --> 02:32:41,271
We don't need a brand-new hero
created at the State's expense.

2446
02:32:41,687 --> 02:32:44,020
I'm sick and tired
of the ones we already have.

2447
02:32:44,021 --> 02:32:46,395
Sujaya, in the political history
of our State...

2448
02:32:46,396 --> 02:32:49,436
never before has an incident
like this been reported.

2449
02:32:49,437 --> 02:32:51,354
Will this actually work
in this day and age, CM?

2450
02:32:52,854 --> 02:32:54,270
Just sit back and watch.

2451
02:32:54,271 --> 02:32:55,853
We have some breaking news!

2452
02:32:55,854 --> 02:32:58,978
Alancode MLA Anoop Thottathil,
wanted in a sexual assault case,

2453
02:32:58,979 --> 02:33:01,478
has just been arrested
after being on the run.

2454
02:33:01,479 --> 02:33:05,061
The police tactfully nabbed
Anoop Thottathil

2455
02:33:05,062 --> 02:33:06,603
from a farmhouse in Bengaluru.

2456
02:33:06,604 --> 02:33:10,561
Three young women,
including a television actress,

2457
02:33:10,562 --> 02:33:13,186
had previously filed sexual harassment
complaints against him.

2458
02:33:13,187 --> 02:33:16,604
Following this, Anoop went
into hiding two weeks ago.

2459
02:33:16,812 --> 02:33:18,603
This marks the absolute
first time in Kerala

2460
02:33:18,604 --> 02:33:21,437
that a sitting MLA is arrested
over sexual assault charges.

2461
02:33:22,354 --> 02:33:24,062
[dramatic score swells]

2462
02:33:40,354 --> 02:33:42,562
[emotional, soulful music]

2463
02:34:05,896 --> 02:34:06,896
Sir...

2464
02:34:08,479 --> 02:34:11,687
Because of the blunders I made,
you had to scramble so much, sir.

2465
02:34:12,854 --> 02:34:14,479
It was due to my
lack of experience.

2466
02:34:15,229 --> 02:34:16,271
Please forgive me, sir.

2467
02:34:19,354 --> 02:34:22,562
Ever since this started,
all I've done is make blunders, right?

2468
02:34:24,521 --> 02:34:27,271
You haven't made a bigger blunder
than dragging your own daughter...

2469
02:34:27,896 --> 02:34:28,937
into this mess, have you?

2470
02:34:29,271 --> 02:34:30,271
Forget it, sir.

2471
02:34:30,979 --> 02:34:33,937
At the end of the day,
things panned out exactly as you intended.

2472
02:34:34,354 --> 02:34:35,729
You got your child back safe.

2473
02:34:36,271 --> 02:34:38,187
Did you really get
your child back, sir?

2474
02:34:40,229 --> 02:34:42,354
Isn't she sitting inside
right now with the police?

2475
02:34:45,021 --> 02:34:46,271
As you already know, sir...

2476
02:34:46,729 --> 02:34:49,062
she was with us
the entire night.

2477
02:34:51,771 --> 02:34:53,186
In a situation like this,

2478
02:34:53,187 --> 02:34:55,021
how do kids usually react, sir?

2479
02:34:55,687 --> 02:34:57,437
They weep.
They wail.

2480
02:34:57,979 --> 02:34:59,562
They scream out
for their parents.

2481
02:35:00,604 --> 02:35:02,437
But your daughter
did not do any of that.

2482
02:35:04,312 --> 02:35:05,437
So I thought to myself...

2483
02:35:06,312 --> 02:35:07,771
What a sweet, innocent child!

2484
02:35:10,062 --> 02:35:11,521
She made absolutely no fuss.

2485
02:35:11,729 --> 02:35:12,812
A completely harmless girl.

2486
02:35:14,687 --> 02:35:17,271
But is this how a child her age
is supposed to behave?

2487
02:35:18,104 --> 02:35:19,604
Shouldn't she at least cry?

2488
02:35:20,062 --> 02:35:22,479
Shouldn't she throw a fit,
demanding to see her parents?

2489
02:35:24,437 --> 02:35:26,729
Why didn't your daughter
do any of that, sir?

2490
02:35:28,062 --> 02:35:29,562
Don't you see a problem in this, sir?

2491
02:35:32,104 --> 02:35:33,354
Because I certainly do.

2492
02:35:34,354 --> 02:35:36,021
[poignant score builds]

2493
02:35:40,271 --> 02:35:43,562
I know you fought all this way
for the sake of your children.

2494
02:35:46,354 --> 02:35:47,896
But is that really enough, sir?

2495
02:35:54,271 --> 02:35:55,979
- Aren't you okay?
- Yes.

2496
02:35:57,812 --> 02:35:59,146
[song begins]

2497
02:36:11,729 --> 02:36:14,271
[auto-rickshaw engine running steadily]

2498
02:36:21,854 --> 02:36:27,145
♪ O light that arrives
crossing through the night ♪

2499
02:36:27,146 --> 02:36:32,062
♪ That same desolate,
lonely night ♪

2500
02:36:33,896 --> 02:36:38,687
♪ O star that lets
drops of love descend ♪

2501
02:36:39,021 --> 02:36:42,604
♪ From that same blazing dream
without end ♪

2502
02:36:42,937 --> 02:36:44,771
I don't want the fare, sister.
You carry on.

2503
02:36:45,104 --> 02:36:50,896
♪ As though you cast
one tender-eyed glance ♪

2504
02:36:51,146 --> 02:36:56,437
♪ Into dark forests
where shadows dance ♪

2505
02:36:57,062 --> 02:37:02,936
♪ As though a soul-song
begins to sound ♪

2506
02:37:02,937 --> 02:37:08,604
♪ From a storm's heart
as its rage calms down ♪

2507
02:37:09,062 --> 02:37:14,396
♪ O light that arrives,
crossing the night ♪

2508
02:37:15,021 --> 02:37:20,354
♪ O star that drips
love's gentle light ♪

2509
02:37:31,312 --> 02:37:32,478
[loud, resounding slap]

2510
02:37:32,479 --> 02:37:34,646
How dare you gamble
with my child's life, Rajeevan?!

2511
02:37:36,271 --> 02:37:38,479
If something had happened to her,
what would--

2512
02:37:41,104 --> 02:37:42,312
Sorry.

2513
02:37:56,354 --> 02:37:57,562
[doorbell rings]

2514
02:38:09,104 --> 02:38:10,562
Here's some breakfast for you.

2515
02:38:11,479 --> 02:38:13,687
Isn't it late already?
Don't bother cooking today.

2516
02:38:17,937 --> 02:38:19,562
Where is your daughter, Jiya?

2517
02:38:19,729 --> 02:38:20,854
She's taking a bath.

2518
02:38:21,521 --> 02:38:24,229
If you need anything at all,
don't hesitate to ask.

2519
02:38:24,687 --> 02:38:25,728
Bye.

2520
02:38:25,729 --> 02:38:26,979
Okay.

2521
02:38:33,896 --> 02:38:35,146
What's inside that, Mom?

2522
02:38:35,396 --> 02:38:37,020
Why are you still here?
Go wash up.

2523
02:38:37,021 --> 02:38:38,478
Don't you have to go to school?

2524
02:38:38,479 --> 02:38:40,104
Do I have to go to school
today as well?

2525
02:38:41,271 --> 02:38:42,854
What do you mean,
"today as well"?

2526
02:38:50,104 --> 02:38:53,021
[soft, soulful humming]

2527
02:39:12,437 --> 02:39:13,896
[music fades]

2528
02:39:14,021 --> 02:39:18,937
♪ O light that arrives,
crossing the night ♪

2529
02:39:29,021 --> 02:39:30,896
[intriguing music]

2530
02:39:43,854 --> 02:39:44,896
Sir.

2531
02:39:45,312 --> 02:39:47,479
I've taken the amount
you promised to give me, okay?

2532
02:39:49,021 --> 02:39:52,812
And you already know
where the rest of it is, right?

2533
02:39:54,271 --> 02:39:57,937
You never asked me why I needed
such a large sum of money.

2534
02:39:59,021 --> 02:40:02,021
But I'm sure you figured it out.
[ad seeking medical aid for a girl]

2535
02:40:02,396 --> 02:40:03,520
Otherwise...

2536
02:40:03,521 --> 02:40:07,854
would you trust a total stranger
with your own daughter's life?

2537
02:40:08,854 --> 02:40:11,229
[Prayers futile, Anna departs]

2538
02:40:13,229 --> 02:40:14,271
Michael!

2539
02:40:14,937 --> 02:40:15,937
It's me...

2540
02:40:16,729 --> 02:40:17,729
Jacob.

2541
02:40:20,646 --> 02:40:23,521
Didn't I borrow some money
from you twenty years ago?

2542
02:40:24,521 --> 02:40:26,146
Yeah... Do you remember?

2543
02:40:27,562 --> 02:40:29,062
I'm finally going to
settle that debt.

2544
02:40:30,062 --> 02:40:31,062
With full interest.

2545
02:40:36,812 --> 02:40:38,896
[Michael, Nemom]

2546
02:40:54,146 --> 02:40:55,896
Rajeevan... where's the cash?

2547
02:41:03,021 --> 02:41:05,187
I think they're fighting again.

2548
02:41:09,979 --> 02:41:11,187
I don't think so.

2549
02:41:11,354 --> 02:41:12,770
I can't hear anything.

2550
02:41:12,771 --> 02:41:15,895
♪ To the house in the sky,
where the winds fly high

2551
02:41:15,896 --> 02:41:17,146
♪ Let's go ♪

2552
02:41:17,396 --> 02:41:19,354
♪ Come on, let's go ♪

2553
02:41:21,146 --> 02:41:26,271
♪ Where clouds float above us
and the sweet stars glow, let's go ♪

2554
02:41:27,479 --> 02:41:28,562
♪ Let's go ♪

2555
02:41:31,229 --> 02:41:35,478
Is Mumma scolding Papa
for not throwing the money away?

2556
02:41:35,479 --> 02:41:37,228
No, Papa just didn't get the time.

2557
02:41:37,229 --> 02:41:38,812
He will throw it out tomorrow.

2558
02:41:39,604 --> 02:41:41,895
♪ Grand hopes and desires
turn to butterflies ♪

2559
02:41:41,896 --> 02:41:44,771
♪ Soft as cotton
as they rise ♪

2560
02:41:46,521 --> 02:41:50,229
With that much money...
we can buy a thousand chocolates, right?

2561
02:41:50,354 --> 02:41:53,728
Ugh! Just a thousand?
We can buy millions of chocolates!

2562
02:41:53,729 --> 02:41:54,896
My goodness!

2563
02:41:58,062 --> 02:42:05,187
♪ O lazy silver moonlight,
Don't fade too soon tonight ♪

2564
02:42:06,021 --> 02:42:07,061
♪ Come on, sing ♪

2565
02:42:07,062 --> 02:42:16,228
♪ A wondrous magic
spreads across the sky so wide ♪

2566
02:42:16,229 --> 02:42:23,062
♪ Diving into the heart,
deep down inside ♪

2567
02:42:24,479 --> 02:42:25,520
♪ Come on, sing ♪

2568
02:42:25,521 --> 02:42:34,728
♪ A wondrous magic
spreads across the sky so wide ♪

2569
02:42:34,729 --> 02:42:41,104
♪ Diving into the heart,
deep down inside ♪

